d?"], [435.1, "a", "Yes, it's good because Luke is an admirable man."], [438.1, "s", "He's a very good man."], [439.6, "s", "We admire Luke because he's a good man."], [441.9, "s", "He has a good conscience."], [443.2, "s", "He always thinks about what is right and what is wrong."], [446.3, "s", "What about Dick, Darth Cheney?"], [447.7, "q", "Does he have a good conscience?"], [450.4, "a", "Now, of course not."], [451.2, "s", "He has no conscience at all."], [452.9, "s", "He is unscrupulous."], [454.5, "s", "He's totally unscrupulous."], [456.5, "s", "He has zero conscience, no conscience."], [460.5, "s", "Alright, I'm gonna tell the story one more time."], [463.1, "s", "With not so many questions."], [464.9, "s", "Alright, there was a guy named Luke."], [467.0, "s", "He was a rebel."], [468.6, "s", "He's a rebel because he fights against the government."], [472.1, "s", "The authorities vilified him and said he was an abominable man."], [477.7, "s", "The authorities?"], [478.3, "q", "Who are the authorities?"], [479.7, "a", "Well, the authorities are the government, the president, the army, the police."], [484.1, "s", "These people, the authorities, vilify Luke."], [487.3, "s", "They call him terrible names."], [488.9, "s", "They say he's evil."], [490.2, "s", "They say he's a villain, a bad guy."], [493.3, "s", "All right."], [494.1, "q", "What do they say?"], [494.8, "a", "They say he's an abominable man, a terrible, horrible, evil man, right?"], [499.6, "s", "So the action, what they're doing, is vilifying him, and they're describing him as an abominable man."], [506.7, "s", "That's how they vilify him."], [508.8, "q", "Is Luke really an abominable man?"], [511.3, "a", "Of course not, Luke is a very admirable man."], [514.2, "s", "A very good man."], [515.1, "s", "We admire him, we respect him."], [517.0, "s", "He's admirable because he has a good conscience, a very strong, good conscience."], [522.1, "s", "Always thinking if something is right or if something is wrong."], [526.4, "s", "Always trying to do the good thing, the right thing."], [529.0, "s", "He always wants to be just."], [531.5, "s", "Means he always wants to be fair."], [533.7, "s", "He always wants to help people."], [535.3, "s", "That's why he's a just person."], [537.2, "s", "He wants justice."], [539.6, "s", "But Luke has a problem with the government because he refuses to obey unjust laws."], [545.6, "s", "He says no."], [546.9, "s", "He says I will not do something bad."], [549.3, "s", "I will not obey."], [550.6, "s", "I will not follow."], [552.0, "s", "The bad laws, unjust laws, the bad laws that hurt people."], [556.7, "s", "He says, no, I refuse to follow those laws."], [558.9, "s", "I refuse to obey."], [560.8, "s", "Because he refused to obey, the government was angry."], [564.4, "s", "The authorities were very angry."], [567.0, "s", "They condemned him."], [568.6, "s", "They said, we think he is a bad terrible person."], [572.9, "s", "We decide."], [574.4, "s", "Luke is evil."], [576.0, "s", "Luke is bad."], [577.0, "s", "He must die."], [578.4, "s", "They condemn Luke."], [579.6, "s", "They condemn Luke to die."], [582.0, "s", "They send Darth Cheney to kill him."], [585.5, "q", "Is Darth Cheney the same as Luke?"], [587.7, "a", "No."], [588.5, "s", "He has no conscience."], [590.2, "s", "He doesn't care about right, doesn't care about wrong."], [592.8, "s", "He cares about nothing, only power and himself."], [595.5, "s", "He's an unscrupulous man."], [598.1, "s", "Darth Cheney is totally unscrupulous."], [600.7, "s", "He does not care about anything or anyone other than himself."], [606.0, "s", "He doesn't care about rules."], [607.6, "s", "So he tries to poison Luke."], [609.6, "s", "He tries to shoot him with a gun in the back."], [612.0, "s", "He tries to stab him with a knife, in the back, he's unscrupulous."], [617.7, "s", "But none of this works."], [619.7, "s", "Darth Chaney always fails, and in the end."], [622.5, "s", "Admiral Luke."], [624.3, "s", "Admiral Good Just Luke."], [627.1, "s", "Luke who has a great conscience."], [629.8, "s", "Finally wins."], [631.2, "s", "He fights against Darth Chaney, and he wins."], [634.9, "s", "Darth Chaney is killed."], [637.1, "s", "It's a happy story because Darth Chaney is unscrupulous, but Luke is a rebel and a hero."], [644.0, "s", "He's admirable."], [645.8, "s", "Okay, that's it."], [647.2, "s", "Listen to this story a couple of times."], [649.5, "s", "It will help you remember some of these words, and it might help you, not might, it will help you use these words more correctly."], [658.3, "s", "So if you read the Learning Guide a few times, you start to understand some of the words."], [664.4, "s", "Then you listen to the article, right?"], [667.1, "s", "You listen to the first article, disobedience."], [670.4, "s", "You listen to that many times."], [671.9, "s", "You start to understand more."], [674.4, "s", "After a few times, you listen to the vocabulary explanation, and now you get a little bit better idea."], [680.0, "s", "What is the exact meaning of some of these words?"], [683.0, "s", "Finally, you listen to the mini-story several times, and again, you start to hear these words in a real situation with whole sentences, sentences."], [692.6, "s", "And you get more of a feeling for how the words are actually used."], [696.8, "s", "So all these parts, the learning guide, the article, the vocabulary, and the mini-story, they work together."], [704.8, "s", "So do all of them."], [705.6, "s", "It will help you a lot."], [707.0, "s", "And finally, try to write a little bit about this subject in the forums."], [710.8, "s", "None of you are doing it, so please try."], [713.1, "s", "Okay, I'll see you next time."], [715.0, "s", "Good luck with your English learning."], [716.8, "s", "Bye-bye."]]}]$j$::jsonb,
