  $j$[[0.3, "So let's go: Mind Maps."], [2.0, "Actually, Pin, one of our members, he has been suggesting topics and writing forums."], [8.4, "And he requested this topic."], [9.9, "He sent me some links to mind map articles."], [12.9, "I found one of the links he sent."], [15.0, "It was Wikipedia."], [16.8, "And it's an interesting topic."], [18.6, "In fact, I already knew about mind maps."], [21.1, "I use mind maps myself."], [23.6, "Mind maps are great."], [24.7, "If you still don't quite understand what they look like, I suggest going to the..."], [31.3, "Use the text guide, the learning guide, and go to the bottom."], [35.8, "And you'll see the learn more section, and there's a link, and it says mind map example."], [42.5, "If you go to that, you'll get a picture of what a mind map can look like."], [46.9, "Or the general."], [48.3, "You know, appearance of it."], [49.8, "But anyway, mind maps are very useful."], [52.7, "I use them for writing, I don't know."], [55.4, "Some of you may know, one of my three degrees, my undergraduate degree, was in journalism."], [64.6, "So I'm a writer, and I still write freelance."], [67.7, "I haven't written much, actually, the last year since I came to San Francisco."], [74.2, "But before San Francisco, I was living in Thailand."], [77.0, "And I would write mostly travel articles and send them to different magazines."], [83.0, "Anyway, when I needed to make an article, I needed ideas for an article, I often would use a mind map."], [89.7, "So I would put my central idea in the middle of the paper."], [93.9, "Let's say I'm in Thailand."], [95.1, "I want to write about Thai street food."], [98.0, "That was one of my articles."], [99.5, "So I'd write Thai street food."], [101.2, "I'd put it in the middle of a piece of paper."], [102.7, "I'd write it in the center."], [104.2, "And then I'd just start brainstorming, right?"], [106.3, "I'd just start thinking of random ideas."], [108.1, "Because the first idea, or the first word or phrase that came into my head."], [114.0, "I would write it around, so I'd say Thai street food, I would think, Tom Yum."], [119.1, "Tom Yum is a kind of Thai food."], [120.9, "I would write Tom Yum on the paper and draw a line connecting those two things, street food and Tom Yum."], [126.6, "And then next to Tom Yum, I would write, you know, 50 Bhat."], [132.3, "50 baht is about, I'm sorry, or 10 baht."], [136.8, "10 baht is about 50 cents, so it's very cheap."], [139.8, "And then I would write spicy."], [141.4, "And then I would write, you know, next to my apartment."], [145.5, "Because I'm thinking of a place next to my apartment where I would usually eat."], [149.3, "And I would just keep doing that, going crazy."], [152.6, "Whatever popped into my head, I wrote it down."], [154.8, "And then the next thing that popped into my head, I wrote it down."], [157.2, "And I would connect these with lines."], [159.2, "If I, if I got stuck, if ideas stopped coming."], [163.5, "Then I would just look at the paper, I'd pick one of the words on the paper."], [168.0, "And I'd concentrate on it, and I would see what associations."], [172.4, "What connections, what thoughts I would have connected to that word."], [176.5, "So let's say I'm, I'm doing this, and then I stop, I can't think of anything."], [180.3, "You know, and I'm like, oh, well, I'd look at the phrase “next to my apartment”."], [185.4, "I imagine the place next to my apartment, and suddenly I think “noise”, because it was very noisy, and I write down “noise”."], [192.8, "Then I think “pollution”, oh, I write down “pollution”."], [195.6, "Then I think, you know, “plastic seats”, and I write down “plastic seats”, and then I keep going again."], [201.7, "Well, after doing this for about five or ten minutes, I have a whole page full of words and phrases."], [208.1, "Some are very directly related to my topic, Thai street food."], [211.6, "Some are not."], [212.6, "Some are totally unrelated."], [214.7, "They seem unrelated."], [217.7, "But the great thing about this is I would get a lot of interesting details for my article."], [224.1, "And I would get some interesting ideas that I wouldn't get if I used a normal technique, a normal organization, like an outline: point one, then A, B, C; point two, A, B, C."], [236.5, "That's kind of a very linear, structured."], [240.3, "In my opinion, a little bit boring way to organize a paper."], [243.8, "It's okay for school papers, I guess, but for something a little more creative, it's not so good."], [248.8, "So I would use a mind map instead and my writing."], [253.4, "It would be the first step of my writing."], [255.7, "The second thing I would do, I'd look at my mind map and I would look for interesting ideas and I would start circling them."], [261.7, "For example, pollution was one of the ideas I used because sitting on the street in Bangkok."], [267.8, "Eating, well, there's a lot of pollution."], [270.3, "So I wanted to write about that."], [272.5, "I wanted to give that feeling."], [274.6, "What is it like to be sitting in a street in Bangkok eating or next to a street in Bangkok eating food?"], [282.2, "I wanted to capture some of the feeling and that includes the pollution."], [285.7, "It includes the noise and includes the heat, all those details."], [291.3, "And making the mind map first helped me remember some of those details."], [295.3, "So I would circle the interesting details."], [297.4, "I would circle the interesting ideas."], [300.0, "Then I would organize those ideas."], [302.8, "I would pick the best ones and I would put them in groups."], [306.5, "Maybe I would use a color."], [307.9, "So everything related to the details, like how it looked or felt or sounded."], [315.3, "Maybe I might put that in red, circle those with red."], [318.8, "And then when I'm talking about the actual food."], [321.3, "What food was available, maybe I would circle all the food items in green that I thought about."], [326.8, "And maybe when I'm thinking about cost, how much does it cost."], [330.1, "And saving money and how cheap it is, maybe I'd put that in blue."], [334.4, "So then after I'm finished, I have maybe three or four different colors on the page, and those are my general topics."], [341.3, "That's the general topics that I'm going to write about in my article."], [346.4, "In fact, I would usually write one or two paragraphs for each color, for each group."], [353.7, "So this helped me organize my paper."], [356.2, "It helped my article."], [357.9, "It helped me think of interesting ideas."], [360.0, "It helped me think of interesting details that I wanted to talk about."], [363.6, "It was a really great technique for creative writing, or for any kind of writing, in fact."], [369.6, "I also use mind maps when I just need to think of ideas."], [374.9, "Maybe I'm stuck thinking about ideas for effortless English, for example."], [380.1, "And I don't know what to do next."], [381.7, "So I just will make a mind map."], [383.1, "In the center of the page, I will put effortless English."], [385.7, "I write that phrase."], [386.9, "Then I just start going."], [388.1, "And the first thing I think about, I write down."], [390.5, "Maybe I'll think of, you know, Internet."], [393.0, "And then I'll write Internet."], [394.1, "And then what's the next thing I think about?"], [395.5, "Podcast."], [395.8, "And I write podcasts."], [396.5, "And I just keep going, and the point with a mind map is to do it quickly."], [401.6, "Do not edit your thoughts."], [403.5, "Do not stop and think."], [406.3, "You want to keep the ideas coming quickly."], [408.2, "You want to write fast."], [410.0, "Later you can go back, circle the most interesting ideas, or later you can organize them more."], [417.5, "So anyway, that's how I use mind maps."], [419.5, "So I use mind maps really to generate ideas, I'd say."], [423.0, "That's probably the way I use them most."], [425.8, "Now, some people in the article talks about, you can use mind maps to take notes."], [431.3, "You're in a class."], [433.0, "The professor."], [434.1, "The teacher's lecturing."], [435.8, "Giving a talk."], [437.0, "And you want to write down the main ideas."], [439.0, "So in the center, you might write down the topic, let's say English, learning English."], [447.6, "And then he talks about four main points, speaking, reading, writing, you know, etc."], [453.3, "And then you write each of those around the center of learning English, which is kind of the center idea."], [462.3, "And then you write more details coming off of those."], [464.8, "So you can use it to take notes."], [466.2, "I've never done that myself, but it sounds interesting."], [469.0, "I think it's a good idea."], [471.2, "You could use that for the mini-story, by the way, for any of our lessons."], [476.4, "You can take notes, if you're not in a car."], [479.0, "Driving while you're listening to these lessons."], [482.4, "Take some notes."], [484.0, "And you can do it with a mind map."], [485.3, "I think that would be a good way to do it."], [487.0, "For example, you're listening to the mini-story lesson."], [490.1, "Well, as you listen, you might just write down a key word from each sentence."], [494.9, "And you just write them, and you just connect them to each other."], [498.0, "And that might help you remember the whole story."], [500.9, "You don't have time."], [501.9, "I'm going too fast."], [503.0, "You can't write the whole story."], [505.7, "But you remember the main ideas of the story."], [509.2, "And that would help you at the end when I, at the end of the story I tell you, please stop this, now try to tell the story yourself."], [517.0, "Well, if you've got some notes, if you've got a little mind map to remind you of the vocabulary of the main ideas."], [523.5, "That probably would help."], [525.3, "I don't know."], [525.9, "Try it."], [526.4, "Let me know."], [527.4, "Write it in the forums."], [528.4, "Go to the forums."], [529.1, "Try it and tell us."], [530.2, "Did it help?"], [531.2, "Or did it not?"], [533.1, "Alright, I guess that's it for my commentary."], [535.1, "In general, I think mind maps are a great tool."], [539.1, "I especially think they're a good creativity tool."], [542.1, "And I think they could also be good for note taking, as we just mentioned."], [545.5, "So give it a try."], [546.8, "Try using mind maps when you write."], [549.4, "When you're writing English,"], [551.6, "instead of doing this painful thing and thinking, thinking, thinking forever and making a boring, normal outline."], [559.9, "Try to make a mind map first instead."], [561.6, "It might help you start writing more quickly and more easily."], [567.2, "And when you take notes, if you take notes, when you listen to these lessons, use a mind map."], [571.7, "All right."], [572.1, "And finally, use a mind map and write something in the forums."], [575.8, "Please use the forums."], [578.4, "All right."], [579.0, "See you next time."], [579.9, "Bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["mind map", "/maɪnd mæp/", "bản đồ tư duy"], ["diagram", "/ˈdaɪəɡræm/", "sơ đồ"], ["represent", "/ˌreprɪˈzent/", "thể hiện, đại diện"], ["arrange", "/əˈreɪndʒ/", "sắp xếp"], ["radially", "/ˈreɪdiəli/", "theo hình tỏa tròn"], ["central", "/ˈsentrəl/", "trung tâm"], ["generate", "/ˈdʒenəreɪt/", "tạo ra"], ["visualize", "/ˈvɪʒuəlaɪz/", "hình dung"], ["classify", "/ˈklæsɪfaɪ/", "phân loại"], ["aid", "/eɪd/", "sự hỗ trợ; giúp đỡ"], ["problem-solving", "/ˈprɒbləm ˌsɒlvɪŋ/", "giải quyết vấn đề"], ["decision-making", "/dɪˈsɪʒn ˌmeɪkɪŋ/", "ra quyết định"], ["semantic", "/sɪˈmæntɪk/", "thuộc về ngữ nghĩa"], ["portion", "/ˈpɔːʃn/", "phần"], ["nonlinear", "/ˌnɒnˈlɪniə/", "phi tuyến tính"], ["brainstorming", "/ˈbreɪnstɔːmɪŋ/", "động não"], ["intuitively", "/ɪnˈtjuːɪtɪvli/", "theo trực giác"], ["concept", "/ˈkɒnsept/", "khái niệm"], ["branch", "/brɑːntʃ/", "nhánh"], ["recall", "/rɪˈkɔːl/", "sự gợi nhớ"], ["application", "/ˌæplɪˈkeɪʃn/", "ứng dụng"], ["note-taking", "/ˈnəʊt ˌteɪkɪŋ/", "ghi chép"], ["summarize", "/ˈsʌməraɪz/", "tóm tắt"], ["revise", "/rɪˈvaɪz/", "ôn tập, sửa lại"], ["clarify", "/ˈklærəfaɪ/", "làm rõ"], ["lecture", "/ˈlektʃə/", "bài giảng"], ["take down notes", "/teɪk daʊn nəʊts/", "ghi chép"], ["mnemonic", "/nɪˈmɒnɪk/", "giúp ghi nhớ"], ["sort out", "/sɔːt aʊt/", "sắp xếp, giải quyết"], ["collaborate", "/kəˈlæbəreɪt/", "cộng tác"], ["retain", "/rɪˈteɪn/", "ghi nhớ, giữ lại"], ["sophisticated", "/səˈfɪstɪkeɪtɪd/", "tinh vi, công phu"], ["guideline", "/ˈɡaɪdlaɪn/", "nguyên tắc hướng dẫn"], ["emphasis", "/ˈemfəsɪs/", "sự nhấn mạnh"], ["association", "/əˌsəʊsiˈeɪʃn/", "sự liên kết"], ["hierarchy", "/ˈhaɪərɑːki/", "thứ bậc"]]$j$::jsonb,
