[258.8, "s", "Prevent other people from knowing about the information."], [262.6, "s", "He wanted Bob to censor the information."], [266.4, "q", "Did he want Jim to censor the information?"], [269.9, "a", "No, his friend Jim didn't know about it at all."], [272.7, "s", "You can't censor something if you don't already know about it."], [276.8, "s", "So, he wanted Bob to censor this information."], [280.7, "q", "What information did he want him to censor?"], [285.3, "a", "Well, he wanted him to censor the information that he found gold by the river."], [292.5, "q", "Why did he want to censor this information?"], [296.2, "a", "He wanted to censor the information so other people would not go back to the same spot and take more gold."], [305.4, "s", "That's why he wanted to censor the information."], [308.0, "s", "He wanted the spot, he wanted the gold only for himself."], [313.0, "s", "So he wanted to censor this information."], [315.3, "q", "Did Bob censor the information?"], [318.1, "a", "No, Bob did not censor the information."], [321.0, "s", "Bob told everybody."], [323.0, "s", "Bob smiled and said, But okay, I won't tell anyone."], [328.5, "s", "But his words were at odds with his actions."], [332.8, "q", "Did his words agree with his actions?"], [336.8, "a", "No, they were at odds with his actions."], [340.1, "s", "They were not the same."], [342.1, "s", "His words and his actions were different."], [344.4, "s", "His words were at odds with his actions."], [347.5, "q", "Were his words at odds with his feelings?"], [351.3, "a", "Well we don't know."], [352.6, "s", "No, we don't know what his feelings were, but we do know his words were at odds with his actions."], [360.3, "s", "They did not agree with his actions."], [363.1, "s", "Whose words were at odds with his actions?"], [368.0, "q", "Were John's words at odds with his actions?"], [372.2, "a", "No, not John's words."], [374.5, "s", "Bob's words were at odds with his actions."], [377.9, "s", "Because he soon told everyone about John's gold, even though he promised he would not."], [385.7, "s", "So, when John returned to his river spot, he found 10,000 people there."], [392.4, "s", "They were all filtering the river looking for gold."], [396.3, "q", "Were they all swimming in the river?"], [399.0, "a", "No, they were all filtering the river."], [402.9, "q", "Were they filtering the ground?"], [405.6, "a", "No, they weren't filtering the ground."], [408.6, "s", "They weren't separating pieces of the ground."], [411.4, "s", "They were filtering the river."], [412.6, "s", "They were filtering the river water and the river rocks, separating them, looking for gold."], [419.2, "s", "John went crazy and attacked them."], [421.0, "s", "He was so angry, he massacred everyone."], [425.0, "q", "Did he kill everyone?"], [427.8, "a", "Yes he did."], [428.8, "s", "He killed them all."], [430.7, "q", "Did these people have guns?"], [435.2, "a", "Well, we don't know, but probably not, because he massacred them."], [439.8, "s", "He killed them all."], [441.7, "s", "If you massacre somebody, usually it means if you massacre many people, usually they are weak or peaceful."], [449.0, "s", "So he massacred all of them."], [450.7, "s", "He killed all of them."], [452.9, "q", "Did Bob massacre everybody?"], [455.8, "a", "No."], [457.1, "s", "No, not Bob."], [458.8, "s", "John massacred everyone."], [461.6, "q", "Who did John massacre?"], [465.4, "a", "Well, John massacred all the people looking for gold."], [469.8, "q", "How many people did John massacre?"], [473.8, "a", "Well, actually, he massacred 9,999 people because one person survived, one person lived."], [483.5, "s", "It was Bob."], [485.2, "q", "Who survived the massacre?"], [488.7, "a", "Using it as a noun now, the massacre... well, Bob survived the massacre."], [494.9, "s", "And after he survived, Bob cried, oh, please don't kill me, John, I'm sorry, please."], [502.5, "s", "John, he relaxed."], [505.3, "s", "John calmed himself."], [507.9, "s", "He calmed down."], [508.8, "s", "He calmed himself."], [510.6, "s", "And he said, okay, I will give you amnesty."], [515.2, "s", "But only if you leave America and never come back."], [518.5, "q", "Did John give Bob amnesty?"], [523.0, "a", "Yes he did."], [524.1, "s", "John gave Bob amnesty."], [526.9, "q", "Did John forgive Bob?"], [529.0, "a", "Yes he did."], [529.9, "s", "He did."], [530.2, "s", "He gave John amnesty."], [533.4, "q", "Did John give the other people amnesty?"], [538.0, "a", "No, he did not."], [539.2, "s", "He massacred them."], [540.2, "s", "He killed all of them."], [541.4, "s", "He did not give amnesty to the other people."], [544.3, "s", "He only gave amnesty to Bob."], [548.2, "q", "Did Bob ask for amnesty?"], [552.5, "a", "Well, yes, he did."], [553.1, "s", "He said, please don't kill me."], [554.5, "s", "Please don't kill me."], [555.2, "s", "Please forgive me."], [556.3, "s", "He asked for amnesty."], [559.6, "q", "Why did John give Bob amnesty?"], [564.0, "a", "Well, he probably forgave him."], [565.4, "s", "He probably gave him amnesty because he was his best friend."], [569.8, "s", "But there was one condition, one thing he had to do to get amnesty."], [574.2, "s", "Bob had to leave America and never come back."], [579.0, "s", "Bob said, okay, I'll go now, thank you."], [582.7, "s", "This time his words were not at odds with his actions."], [586.4, "s", "He left America and never came back."], [590.0, "s", "This time, did Bob's words, his promise, and his actions, did they agree?"], [595.0, "q", "Were they the same?"], [596.5, "a", "Well, yes, this time they were the same."], [598.6, "s", "This time his words were not at odds with his actions."], [603.1, "q", "Were his words at odds with his actions?"], [607.4, "a", "No, they were not at odds with his actions this time."], [611.0, "s", "This time they agreed."], [613.2, "s", "This time his actions and his words were the same."], [617.6, "s", "Okay then, very nice."], [619.8, "s", "Now one more time I'm going to just say key phrases and please repeat the key phrases after me."], [627.9, "s", "Don't just copy the words."], [630.5, "s", "Copy my pronunciation."], [632.6, "s", "Copy my tone."], [634.2, "s", "Copy my emotion."], [636.3, "s", "Exaggerate."], [637.8, "s", "Copy me exactly."], [639.6, "s", "Here we go."], [641.2, "s", "John was next to a river."], [642.8, "s", "He was using a pan to filter the rocks."], [648.1, "s", "He was using a pan to filter the rocks."], [655.7, "s", "Good."], [656.2, "s", "He hoped to find gold."], [657.6, "s", "And he did find gold."], [659.8, "s", "After he found gold."], [661.4, "s", "He ran to town and told Bob his best friend about the incident."], [666.7, "s", "He told Bob his best friend about the incident."], [675.5, "s", "He told Bob his best friend about the incident."], [684.1, "s", "Good."], [684.6, "s", "He said, Bob, don't tell anyone."], [686.3, "s", "I need to censor this information."], [689.4, "s", "He said, I need to censor this information."], [696.8, "s", "He said, I need to censor this information."], [704.5, "s", "Good."], [704.8, "s", "He said, I need to censor this information so no one steals my gold by the river."], [710.5, "s", "Bob smiled and said, okay, I won't tell anyone."], [713.6, "s", "But his words were at odds with his actions."], [717.4, "s", "But his words were at odds with his actions."], [724.4, "s", "But his words were at odds with his actions."], [727.6, "s", "Good, but his words were at odds with his actions, because he soon told everybody about John's gold."], [738.6, "s", "So when John returned to his river spot, he found 10,000 people there."], [743.3, "s", "They were all filtering the river looking for gold."], [747.8, "s", "They were all filtering the river looking for gold."], [755.5, "s", "They were all filtering the river looking for gold."], [759.4, "s", "Good, John went crazy and attacked them."], [767.0, "s", "He was so angry, he massacred everyone."], [771.3, "s", "He was so angry, he massacred everyone."], [778.2, "s", "He was so angry, he massacred everyone."], [784.7, "s", "Only one person lived."], [786.8, "s", "It was Bob."], [787.9, "s", "Bob cried and said, please don't kill me, I'm sorry."], [790.4, "s", "Hey, John calmed himself and said, Okay, I will give you amnesty."], [798.0, "s", "John said, Okay, I will give you amnesty."], [804.8, "s", "John said, Okay, I will give you amnesty."], [811.9, "s", "But you can never come back to America."], [814.6, "s", "Bob said, Okay, I'll go now."], [816.8, "s", "This time his words were not at odds with his actions."], [820.0, "s", "This time, his words were not at odds with his actions."], [828.6, "s", "This time, his words were not at odds with his actions."], [837.0, "s", "Okay, very good."], [839.4, "s", "Now please, this time, pause your MP3 player, pause your iPod, and try to tell the story yourself."], [849.9, "s", "All of the story."], [851.3, "s", "Try to tell all of the story."], [853.3, "s", "You don't need to remember every word."], [856.9, "s", "Tell the general story."], [859.1, "s", "But try to remember some of the new vocabulary."], [864.0, "s", "To filter, the incident, to censor, at odds with, filtering, massacred, amnesty, at odds with."], [875.2, "s", "Try to use these vocabulary phrases, these vocabulary words when you retell the story."], [881.7, "s", "So please pause now and tell the story yourself."], [884.6, "s", "Say it out loud so you can hear it."], [887.2, "s", "Tell the story again."], [889.0, "s", "If you forget, if you can't remember, it's okay."], [892.6, "s", "Just listen to it again."], [895.2, "s", "And please review this every day."], [897.6, "s", "Listen to this story one time every day for a few months."], [902.4, "s", "Maybe two, three, maybe even four months."], [905.3, "s", "If you review every day, the words, the phrases, the grammar will become automatic."], [906.8, "s", "But you must do it many times, many days, over a long period of time."], [908.4, "s", "Okay, I will see you next time, bye."]]}]$j$::jsonb,
