  $j$[[0.0, "About three years ago, I did a Vipassana meditation course."], [4.0, "It was a 10-day meditation course."], [7.0, "I actually did it in Florida, in the United States."], [10.4, "Vipassana means insight meditation."], [15.1, "It's a kind of meditation."], [18.8, "I guess technically it's a Buddhist meditation, although there's not really a lot of religious teaching around it."], [26.8, "You can be any religion and do Vipassana meditation."], [31.4, "And it's basically a system, a way of examining, looking at your brain, your mind and your body."], [41.4, "So it's just paying attention basically to your mind and your body."], [45.0, "In the article I started off very dramatically describing this intense pain that I felt at one point in the meditation course I did."], [56.8, "It's a very intensive course I did."], [58.5, "It's ten days, meditating all day, very positive."], [62.5, "But because of the way I am, my personality, I tend to do things very strongly sometimes."], [71.6, "Sometimes too strongly."], [73.4, "In fact, Pin."], [74.7, "One of our members, sent me an email saying, oh my God, what were you doing?"], [78.7, "That's not real vipassana."], [80.9, "You shouldn't be, you know, torturing yourself with pain."], [84.7, "And of course he's right."], [86.5, "In fact."], [87.3, "The Vipassana teacher at my course, I told him, oh, I'm in so much pain, but I'm trying not to move."], [94.8, "Because I'm not supposed to move."], [96.0, "I'm supposed to observe the pain, and at one point my body's shaking because my back and my knees hurt so much."], [103.8, "And he told me, oh, you need to relax."], [107.2, "He's like, you know."], [108.4, "It's not a, This is not a torture exercise, so please relax."], [112.2, "And if you're in a lot of pain."], [114.5, "Move your body if you need to."], [117.0, "Anyway, so that kind of intense pain is not the normal thing you need to experience in a Vipassana retreat."], [126.0, "I hope I didn't scare all of you away from Vipassana."], [129.5, "It's actually very positive."], [131.3, "In fact, overall, my experience with the Vipassana course was very, very positive, especially after I talked to the instructor and realized I could relax and not be so intense with it."], [147.3, "And at the end of the course, I felt that I had a lot greater awareness of myself, my own mind and my own body."], [155.8, "And I continued to meditate for quite a while after that, every day."], [160.6, "But, unfortunately, life intruded."], [164.5, "And I got busier and busier, and I just started meditating less and less each day."], [169.7, "Until finally I just stopped doing it all together."], [172.4, "And it's now been, I suppose it's been a couple years since I regularly meditated every day."], [179.0, "And it's really something you should do every day."], [181.1, "It's kind of like running."], [182.6, "I consider it a kind of mental exercise."], [186.0, "You could think of it that way."], [187.4, "You need to exercise your mind every day just like you need to exercise your body."], [192.2, "And with meditation it's the same thing."], [194.1, "You really need to do it daily so that you can experience, you know, a deeper and deeper awareness."], [202.6, "And it has various benefits, but anyway, and there are lots of different schools of meditation."], [208.0, "Vipassana is only one."], [209.7, "There are Tibetan styles of meditation."], [212.5, "There are, you know, there's endless number of kinds of meditation."], [216.3, "And each one tends to appeal to different kinds of personalities, different kinds of people."], [222.5, "But they all have similar benefits, I think."], [226.4, "If done well."], [228.4, "So anyway, I've started thinking about Vipassana lately because my life has been quite unbalanced."], [234.8, "I've been so busy with my students here in San Francisco and the website."], [242.4, "And I'm still doing a little bit with the linguists, just started up."], [246.5, "Of course, just my general social life, you know, I've got to take care of my friends at Tomoe, and lots of things to juggle, lots of things to balance, and not so easy sometimes."], [257.3, "So I started thinking, you know, Vipassana, I should really be doing Vipassana."], [262.3, "It's very healthy for me."], [264.4, "It's a very good practice, both at a very surface level, at a surface level, it helps you kind of stay calm and kind of keep your emotions from getting too crazy."], [276.7, "And at a much deeper level, it is kind of a, I don't know if I want to say religious, but spiritual practice."], [284.3, "So anyway, for all those reasons, I've been thinking about it again lately."], [287.9, "I've also been thinking about running again."], [290.5, "I used to run quite a bit."], [292.5, "I used to train for marathons."], [294.7, "I did a couple marathons, and I felt great when I did that."], [297.9, "My body was very healthy."], [299.1, "Again, I got really busy."], [301.6, "I also moved to Bangkok, Thailand, which has a lot of air pollution."], [306.2, "And I didn't enjoy running there."], [309.1, "So for that reason, also for a couple years, I have not run."], [313.1, "So I've been neglecting my mind and my body lately."], [316.3, "That's why I decided to write this article about Vipassana, because I've been thinking about it."], [322.4, "So anyway, in the article at the end, I give you a website."], [326.2, "Website, you can check out, if you're interested in meditation and particularly Vipassana meditation."], [332.8, "You go to www.dhamadhama.org and you can find more information about courses."], [342.2, "They have Vipassana courses and Vipassana centers all over the world."], [346.8, "Every inhabited continent has, I think, at least one, probably many."], [352.6, "So anyway, check it out."], [353.6, "It is quite positive, and it's not quite as torturous and painful as my article might imply."], [361.9, "In general, one last issue here before I go."], [366.6, "I've been thinking a lot about the issue of life balance, balancing the different things in our life."], [372.8, "Everyone listening to this is trying to learn a language."], [375.6, "You're trying to improve your English."], [377.4, "For me, I'm trying to learn Spanish."], [380.8, "Most of us also work."], [381.9, "A lot of us have girlfriends, boyfriends, husbands or wives."], [387.8, "Some of you may have children."], [390.7, "Of course we have our bodies to take care of, physical exercise, eating well."], [395.9, "We have a community of friends and extended family, such as our grandparents, uncles, aunts."], [402.6, "So, you know, how do we balance all those things?"], [404.8, "How do we find the time to take care of all of those things?"], [408.5, "And, you know, some of you also like me may be starting your own programs or little businesses."], [415.3, "You might be entrepreneurs."], [417.0, "That adds yet another thing to balance and work on."], [420.4, "So we have all these things we want to improve in our lives and keep going."], [425.3, "And it's quite tough, you know, you start focusing on your body and exercising, and you spend a lot of time doing that, and it's easy to maybe forget your relationships."], [435.7, "Or maybe your job suffers a little bit, or maybe your English learning suffers a little bit."], [441.6, "So, it's quite tricky, I think, to find the balance and find the time to do all of these things and to keep them all going and to be successful in all the different areas in our lives, all the aspects of our lives."], [456.6, "I think we need to think about that a lot and we need to constantly look at our lives and make sure we've got that balance, that we're not doing too much in one area and forgetting another area."], [468.8, "We don't want to lose our girlfriend or boyfriend or husband or wife just to learn English."], [474.7, "On the other hand, we do want to continue to keep learning and developing our mind."], [480.5, "So we don't want that to suffer either."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["stab", "/stæb/", "đâm"], ["kidney", "/ˈkɪdni/", "thận"], ["burning", "/ˈbɜːnɪŋ/", "bỏng rát"], ["unavoidable", "/ˌʌnəˈvɔɪdəbl/", "không thể tránh"], ["scan", "/skæn/", "rà soát"], ["sear", "/sɪə/", "thiêu đốt"], ["flesh", "/fleʃ/", "da thịt"], ["numb", "/nʌm/", "tê dại"], ["dull ache", "/dʌl eɪk/", "cơn đau âm ỉ"], ["panic", "/ˈpænɪk/", "sự hoảng loạn"], ["butterflies in my stomach", "/ˈbʌtəflaɪz ɪn maɪ ˈstʌmək/", "bồn chồn, cồn cào"], ["tremendous", "/trəˈmendəs/", "mãnh liệt, to lớn"], ["urge", "/ɜːdʒ/", "sự thôi thúc"], ["gulp", "/ɡʌlp/", "nuốt khan"], ["sensation", "/senˈseɪʃn/", "cảm giác"], ["flee", "/fliː/", "chạy trốn"], ["dispassionately", "/dɪsˈpæʃənətli/", "khách quan, không cảm xúc"], ["delve into", "/delv ˈɪntuː/", "đi sâu vào"], ["drain away", "/dreɪn əˈweɪ/", "tan biến"], ["heave", "/hiːv/", "phập phồng"], ["exhale", "/eksˈheɪl/", "thở ra"], ["creep", "/kriːp/", "len lỏi"], ["intense", "/ɪnˈtens/", "dữ dội"], ["vibration", "/vaɪˈbreɪʃn/", "sự rung động"], ["break through", "/breɪk θruː/", "vượt qua, đột phá"], ["meditation", "/ˌmedɪˈteɪʃn/", "thiền định"], ["insight", "/ˈɪnsaɪt/", "sự thấu hiểu"], ["systematic", "/ˌsɪstəˈmætɪk/", "có hệ thống"], ["variant", "/ˈveəriənt/", "biến thể"], ["transformation", "/ˌtrænsfəˈmeɪʃn/", "sự thay đổi"], ["participant", "/pɑːˈtɪsɪpənt/", "người tham gia"], ["donation", "/dəʊˈneɪʃn/", "sự quyên góp"], ["voluntary", "/ˈvɒləntri/", "tự nguyện"], ["coercion", "/kəʊˈɜːʃn/", "sự ép buộc"], ["centered", "/ˈsentəd/", "cân bằng, vững vàng"], ["volatile", "/ˈvɒlətaɪl/", "thất thường"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["It felt like two hot knives were stabbing me", "Cảm giác như hai con dao nóng đang đâm tôi"], ["a burning pain, unavoidable", "cơn đau bỏng rát, không thể tránh"], ["numb with a dull ache", "tê dại với cơn đau âm ỉ"], ["a wave of panic", "một làn sóng hoảng loạn"], ["butterflies in my stomach", "bụng cồn cào, bồn chồn"], ["a tremendous urge to get up and run away", "thôi thúc mãnh liệt muốn đứng dậy bỏ chạy"], ["remained still", "ngồi yên"], ["Don't flee from the pain.", "Đừng chạy trốn cơn đau."], ["Go deeply into it.", "Hãy đi sâu vào nó."], ["observe the pain dispassionately", "quan sát cơn đau một cách khách quan"], ["As I delved into the pain", "Khi tôi đi sâu vào cơn đau"], ["The panic and fear drained away.", "Sự hoảng loạn và nỗi sợ tan biến."], ["a deep sense of calm", "một sự bình an sâu sắc"], ["That was the moment I broke through.", "Đó là khoảnh khắc tôi vượt qua."], ["rather than theory or philosophy", "chứ không phải lý thuyết hay triết lý"], ["there is no coercion", "không hề ép buộc"], ["clearer than it had ever been", "minh mẫn hơn bao giờ hết"], ["I got out of the practice", "tôi bỏ thói quen đó"], ["It's been quite a while now.", "Đến giờ cũng khá lâu rồi."], ["has gotten me thinking about", "khiến tôi nghĩ về"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["It felt like + clause", "It felt like the room was spinning.", "Cảm giác như căn phòng đang quay.", "felt like"], ["As + clause, + clause", "As I opened the door, the phone rang.", "Khi tôi mở cửa thì điện thoại reo.", "as"], ["S + felt + a + noun + of + noun", "I felt a wave of relief.", "Tôi cảm thấy nhẹ nhõm.", "felt a"], ["a tremendous urge to + V", "I had a tremendous urge to laugh.", "Tôi rất muốn bật cười.", "urge to"], ["S + tried to + V + adv", "She tried to speak calmly.", "Cô ấy cố nói một cách bình tĩnh.", "tried to"], ["Don't + V + from + noun. + V + into + it.", "Don't run from your fear. Walk into it.", "Đừng chạy trốn nỗi sợ. Hãy bước vào nó.", "don't"], ["S + no longer + V-ing / V", "I no longer live in Hanoi.", "Tôi không còn sống ở Hà Nội nữa.", "no longer"], ["That was the moment + clause", "That was the moment I fell in love.", "Đó là khoảnh khắc tôi yêu.", "the moment"], ["S + be + so + adj + by + noun, + S + V", "He was so moved by the film, he cried.", "Anh ấy xúc động vì bộ phim đến mức bật khóc.", "so"], ["... rather than + noun", "We focus on practice rather than theory.", "Chúng tôi tập trung vào thực hành chứ không phải lý thuyết.", "rather than"], ["S + be + adj-er + than it had ever been", "The city was quieter than it had ever been.", "Thành phố yên tĩnh hơn bao giờ hết.", "than it had ever been"], ["one of the most + adj + noun + I've ever + V3", "It's one of the best books I've ever read.", "Đó là một trong những cuốn sách hay nhất tôi từng đọc.", "one of the most|one of the"], ["It's been quite a while (since + clause)", "It's been quite a while since we met.", "Đã khá lâu rồi chúng ta mới gặp.", "quite a while"], ["S + has gotten + me + V-ing", "This book has gotten me thinking about my life.", "Cuốn sách này khiến tôi suy nghĩ về cuộc đời.", "gotten me"]]$j$::jsonb
