s."], [431.3, "q", "After 10 minutes, what happened?"], [433.0, "a", "Well, they finished their competition, they finished writing, and then another group of writers read their papers."], [439.5, "s", "They read what they wrote."], [442.0, "s", "But they could not pick a winner."], [443.8, "s", "Both of the writing, both of the pieces of paper, both of the stories were so great they could not pick a winner."], [451.9, "s", "Everybody was shocked."], [454.7, "s", "However, there was no clear winner, but this competition made history."], [460.1, "s", "It was very famous."], [461.4, "s", "It started a new movement called fast writing."], [465.2, "q", "Did it start a small movement?"], [468.9, "a", "No, it started a big movement."], [470.5, "s", "It means a lot of people copied what they did."], [474.8, "q", "Was this a famous movement?"], [476.7, "a", "Yes, it was a famous movement."], [479.0, "s", "It means a lot of people followed this technique of fast writing; it became a movement."], [485.1, "s", "Large numbers of writers began to do this; it became a big movement, an international movement."], [491.2, "s", "It went from America to Mexico to Canada to Europe."], [495.0, "s", "Soon every writer in all these countries was trying to write fast, trying to write quickly."], [501.1, "s", "It became a big movement, a new movement in writing."], [504.9, "s", "Many writers tried to copy Mike and Stephen King's fast writing style."], [510.1, "s", "However, no one could beat them."], [512.3, "s", "All the fast writing in all these countries in this big movement, most of it was terrible."], [518.6, "s", "Only Mike and Stephen King were good."], [522.2, "s", "Alright, let's go back to the beginning one more time and listen again."], [527.1, "s", "Mike is a writer, but he's not a normal writer."], [530.0, "s", "He's a very controversial writer."], [532.1, "s", "He creates a lot of conflict, a lot of argument with his writing."], [535.7, "s", "He's a controversial writer."], [537.5, "s", "Liberal people love him."], [538.9, "s", "People like Michael Moore or John Kerry or other liberals, environmentalists, labor union people."], [546.9, "s", "They all love his writing."], [549.5, "s", "Conservative people hate his writing."], [551.1, "s", "George Bush hates his writing."], [554.3, "s", "Republicans hate his writing."], [556.6, "s", "Fox News hates his writing."], [559.1, "s", "Okay, Mike is famous in the American literary scene."], [562.3, "s", "He's not famous in the French literary scene or the Mexican literary scene."], [566.2, "s", "He's only famous to American writers and American readers."], [570.1, "s", "He's famous in the American literary scene."], [574.0, "s", "He helped make history by challenging Stephen King to a competition."], [578.2, "s", "He made history."], [579.3, "s", "He did something famous by challenging Stephen King to a competition."], [584.1, "s", "He said to King, I'm the best writer in America."], [586.4, "s", "I challenge you to a competition to prove who the best writer is."], [590.4, "s", "He asked him for a competition; he asked him for a fight."], [594.1, "s", "He challenged him."], [596.0, "s", "King said yes; King accepted."], [599.2, "s", "They decided to hold the competition in New York City."], [602.5, "s", "They did not hold the competition in Maine, where Stephen King lives."], [606.5, "s", "They held the competition in New York City."], [609.5, "s", "Both writers sat at a table with a pen, some paper, and a clock."], [614.8, "s", "They wrote for 10 minutes, and only 10 minutes, very quickly."], [619.0, "s", "Stephen King was not animated when he wrote."], [621.7, "s", "He was very calm."], [623.3, "s", "He wrote slowly."], [625.6, "s", "However, Mike was very animated when he wrote."], [628.7, "s", "He moved his body."], [630.0, "s", "He shook his head."], [631.2, "s", "He moved his feet."], [632.3, "s", "He smiled."], [632.9, "s", "He frowned."], [633.8, "s", "He laughed."], [634.5, "s", "He cried."], [635.8, "s", "He wrote very quickly."], [638.1, "s", "He was very animated when he wrote."], [640.4, "s", "After 10 minutes they both finished and the judges, the group of writers, the referees, read both papers."], [649.5, "s", "Both stories were fantastic."], [651.6, "s", "In fact, they were so good they could not pick a winner."], [655.1, "s", "They decided both of them won."], [658.2, "s", "Everybody was surprised and shocked."], [660.4, "s", "This made history."], [661.6, "s", "It was a famous competition and it created a new movement."], [665.9, "s", "It started a new literary movement, a new writing movement."], [670.3, "s", "Lots of people copied their style and tried to write quickly."], [675.1, "s", "Writers all over America started writing very fast."], [678.9, "s", "Writers in other countries started writing very fast."], [681.2, "s", "It became a big movement."], [684.1, "s", "However, most people in the movement, most writers in this movement, were very bad writers."], [690.0, "s", "None of them could match them."], [691.9, "s", "None of them could beat Mike and Stephen King."], [696.2, "s", "Alright, please stop your iPod now and try to repeat this story."], [702.2, "s", "Tell this story out loud, so you can hear it, to yourself."], [707.3, "s", "You don't need to say every word correctly."], [710.4, "s", "However, try to use the new vocabulary correctly."], [714.8, "s", "So don't memorize the story."], [716.3, "s", "Just tell the general story, but use the new vocabulary."], [719.7, "s", "See if you can remember how to use it correctly."], [722.6, "s", "If you have trouble, if you can't do it, listen again, and then try again to tell the story yourself."], [729.6, "s", "Okay."], [730.3, "s", "I will see you next time."]]}]$j$::jsonb,
