 "The goats will be working."], [2489.9, "s", "The goat herder said he will probably visit San Diego while his goats are working."], [2500.7, "q", "Who are working?"], [2503.2, "a", "The goats."], [2505.2, "q", "Who's visiting San Diego?"], [2508.2, "a", "The goat herder."], [2510.8, "q", "What did the goat herder say?"], [2514.3, "a", "He said he will probably visit San Diego while his goats are working."], [2522.3, "s", "The goat herder said he will probably visit San Diego while his goats are working."], [2529.4, "s", "I want to take one of those hang glider rides."], [2534.6, "q", "Who wants to take a hang glider ride?"], [2539.3, "a", "The goat herder."], [2541.6, "q", "What does he want to do?"], [2545.2, "a", "He wants to take a hang glider ride."], [2550.5, "q", "Who wants to take a hang glider ride?"], [2554.6, "a", "The goat herder."], [2556.4, "q", "Do the goats want to take a ride, or does the goat herder want to take a ride?"], [2564.2, "a", "The goat herder."], [2565.4, "s", "The goat herder said, I want to take one of those hang glider rides."], [2573.0, "q", "What's a hang glider?"], [2575.0, "a", "Hmm."], [2577.5, "s", "A hang glider is like a plane without an engine."], [2584.0, "s", "An unpowered plane."], [2586.1, "s", "A hang glider is an unpowered plane."], [2590.8, "s", "The goat herder said, I want to take one of those hang glider rides."], [2597.2, "s", "He wants to ride on a hang glider."], [2600.3, "s", "He wants to ride in a hang glider."], [2604.9, "s", "He said, I want to take one of those hang glider rides."], [2610.0, "s", "I just hope we don't crash."], [2614.5, "s", "Who?"], [2615.6, "q", "Who hopes he doesn't crash?"], [2620.3, "a", "The goat herder."], [2621.8, "s", "The goat herder hopes."], [2624.2, "s", "The goat herder hopes that he doesn't crash."], [2629.3, "s", "He says, I just hope we don't crash."], [2637.1, "s", "Does he hope he doesn't crash?"], [2640.3, "q", "Or does he hope he doesn't fly?"], [2646.6, "a", "Crash."], [2648.1, "s", "He hopes he doesn't crash."], [2651.4, "s", "He wants to fly."], [2653.6, "s", "He says, I just hope we don't crash."], [2659.4, "s", "I want to take one of those hang glider rides, I just hope we don't crash."], [2665.8, "s", "My goats would end up missing me a lot, he said."], [2673.0, "q", "What did the goat herder say?"], [2676.8, "a", "My goats would end up missing me a lot."], [2680.1, "s", "He said my goats would end up missing me a lot."], [2685.5, "q", "Would the goats miss him a little, or a lot?"], [2692.6, "a", "A lot."], [2694.2, "s", "They wouldn't miss him a little, they would miss him a lot."], [2699.9, "q", "Who would the goats miss?"], [2705.7, "a", "The goat herder."], [2707.5, "s", "He said my goats would end up missing me a lot."], [2713.7, "s", "They would miss me a lot."], [2718.0, "q", "What does end up mean?"], [2719.9, "a", "It means something unexpected."], [2726.8, "s", "My goats would unexpectedly miss me."], [2732.6, "s", "They would unexpectedly miss him because he died in the crash."], [2740.0, "s", "He said, I just hope we don't crash."], [2744.5, "s", "My goats would end up missing me a lot."], [2748.5, "s", "End up means to do something unplanned or unexpected."], [2755.8, "s", "So, he said, I want to take one of those hang glider rides, I just hope we don't crash."], [2762.6, "s", "My goats would end up missing me a lot, he said."], [2769.2, "s", "This is the end of the mini-story for goats being hired."], [2773.2, "s", "Let's do a final read-through and let's do a vocabulary review."], [2781.3, "s", "First, the read-through."], [2783.9, "s", "Goats being hired."], [2786.3, "s", "Goats were hired to do the work of men in a neighborhood outside of San Diego."], [2792.2, "s", "The fires that occurred in the neighborhood four years ago burned thirty homes."], [2798.7, "s", "Most of the homes were rebuilt."], [2800.2, "s", "While contractors were rebuilding the homes, nature was regrowing the grasses, bushes, and shrubs."], [2809.8, "s", "The area is once again overgrown with brush that poses a major fire hazard."], [2818.5, "s", "The city council asked for bids to remove the brush."], [2823.1, "s", "The lowest bid they received was $50,000."], [2827.6, "s", "And that was if the city provided breakfast and lunch for the work crews for six weeks."], [2835.0, "s", "The city countered and offered unlimited coffee and a donut a day for each crew member."], [2842.9, "s", "When that offer was rejected, the city asked for help on its website."], [2849.2, "s", "A sheep herder in Montana and a goat herder in San Bernardino read about the city's plight."], [2857.5, "s", "They read about it while surfing on the web on their laptops."], [2862.8, "s", "They read about it while surfing the web on their laptops."], [2867.2, "s", "They both offered to do the job for $25,000."], [2872.4, "s", "The council chose the goat herder because he lived closer."], [2879.0, "s", "If all goes well, they will invite the goat herder and his goats back every three years."], [2886.0, "s", "The goat herder said he will probably visit San Diego while his goats are working."], [2892.7, "s", "I want to take one of those hang glider rides."], [2896.2, "s", "I just hope we don't crash."], [2898.0, "s", "My goats would end up missing me a lot."], [2904.1, "s", "Now let's review the vocabulary quickly."], [2908.4, "s", "Vocabulary for Goats Being Hired."], [2913.2, "s", "Occurred means happened; occurred means happened."], [2918.9, "s", "Contractors means builders, or companies that build; contractors are builders, or companies that build."], [2932.2, "s", "Regrowing means to grow again."], [2935.2, "s", "It means to regrow."], [2938.8, "s", "Once again means again."], [2945.2, "s", "To happen again."], [2949.1, "s", "Brush means small plants or weeds."], [2952.3, "s", "In this story the brush is flammable."], [2957.4, "s", "The brush is a major fire hazard."], [2961.5, "s", "The brush can burn."], [2966.0, "s", "Countered means counter offer."], [2969.2, "s", "Countered means negotiation."], [2972.5, "s", "They are trying to make a deal, so they give a counter offer."], [2978.4, "s", "They countered."], [2982.1, "s", "Sheep herder is a sheep owner or a sheep farmer."], [2986.0, "s", "Goat herder, a goat owner or goat farmer."], [2990.9, "s", "Plight means a problem."], [2993.2, "s", "Plight is a problem."], [2996.3, "s", "Surfing the web."], [2997.6, "s", "Surfing the web means using the internet or using the web."], [3003.8, "s", "Hang glider is an unpowered plane."], [3007.1, "s", "A hang glider is a plane without an engine."], [3010.1, "s", "And finally, end up means to do something unplanned or something unexpected."], [3018.7, "s", "Something unexpected happens."], [3021.8, "s", "End up means to do something unplanned or unexpected."], [3026.9, "s", "This concludes the vocabulary review and the mini-story for Goats Being Hired."], [3034.6, "s", "Flow on with Flow English."]]}]$j$::jsonb,
