  $j$[[0.4, "Hi, this is AJ."], [2.4, "This is a commentary about the mama's boys story."], [8.2, "So this is an interesting story because of culture."], [14.4, "Because I know that this idea of mama's boys is actually different in different countries, in different cultures."], [25.3, "I know this because when I was teaching my classes in San Francisco, when I was teaching at my school in San Francisco."], [36.4, "We would talk about this, this idea of independence for children."], [43.8, "And you know, where should children live when they are adults?"], [48.8, "So in some countries, in many countries, children will continue to live with their parents until they're married."], [60.1, "So even if they're 25 years old."], [62.6, "Even if they're maybe even 30 years old."], [66.0, "If they're not married."], [67.4, "They might continue to live with their parents."], [71.9, "In fact, in some countries, even if they are married, they will live with their parents."], [78.7, "So, they're, say, 28 years old."], [82.6, "They get married."], [83.9, "And the couple will live with the parents."], [88.0, "The girl's parents or the man's parents."], [91.4, "So that's true in some countries."], [94.1, "In other countries, probably in more countries now."], [98.3, "A man will stay with his parents until he gets married."], [104.8, "So, for example, some of my students told me that it was normal for a man maybe 30 years old to still live with his family, with his mom and dad."], [122.0, "That this was normal and that mom would still cook for him and still clean his clothes even though he's 30 years old."], [131.7, "So, we talked about this in my class, because in America, it's very different."], [140.1, "And it's actually very bad."], [144.5, "In our culture, we really expect, we really value independence for adults."], [153.4, "This is true for men and women, it's true for both, but especially men."], [160.0, "But really there's not we don't have a name like mama's girls we never say that."], [166.8, "So boys, it's stronger for boys, but it's true for both."], [174.9, "So in the United States, adults, so maybe 23, 25 and older, should live in their own place, not with their parents."], [191.1, "If a man lives with his parents, if he's 25 or older, then we think it's very bad."], [204.1, "We think something is wrong."], [206.6, "We think this man, this guy, is a mama's boy that he's not independent."], [215.4, "He still wants his mom to take care of him, he's not strong."], [221.8, "So it's it's not good and especially after 30 years old then it's very strange."], [234.0, "So in the United States if a man is 30 years old and he lives with his mom or with his parents."], [243.7, "Then we think, oh, something is very wrong."], [248.1, "People will laugh."], [249.4, "They will joke about this man."], [251.8, "They'll laugh at him."], [252.8, "They'll say he's a mama's boy."], [255.5, "And it's a big problem for dating."], [258.6, "So American women do not like mama's boys."], [262.9, "They do not want to date mama's boys."], [268.0, "So, it's a big, big problem in the United States."], [271.7, "If you live with your parents."], [274.0, "And you see a girl, you like her."], [277.4, "And you go to dinner together or you go to a coffee shop together."], [283.6, "And you're talking."], [285.4, "And she says, so where do you live?"], [288.4, "And the man, he's 27, he says, oh, I live with my mom."], [293.3, "The girl will laugh, or the girl will be surprised, and she will not want to see him again."], [305.7, "Usually she will think, oh my god, this guy, he's a mama's boy, what's wrong with him?"], [316.7, "So mama's boys have a problem getting girlfriends, if you're an American girlfriend."], [325.2, "American women do not like it."], [328.0, "American women want men who are independent."], [333.0, "So this is a big, big, strong cultural thing in the United States."], [338.3, "It's very strong."], [340.9, "Independence is very important."], [343.1, "So it's very important, I think, after university."], [347.6, "So if someone's 21 or 22 and they're going to school, they're still in school, university or college, that's okay, that's normal."], [359.8, "But after university, after they finish school, when they get a job, then they should go out and be independent."], [370.9, "And this was true for me in my life: I left my house when I was 18."], [380.4, "So I went to a university, you know, in another city, which is normal, probably, in many places in the world."], [392.1, "So I went to university, and then I graduated."], [397.1, "I finished school."], [398.6, "That was 22 I guess."], [401.0, "And I got my own apartment."], [404.1, "Actually I had my own apartment when I was in school also."], [408.1, "So I got an apartment during university."], [412.0, "But then after university I continued to have my own apartment."], [416.6, "I did not go back to my parents house, I would never have gone back."], [422.1, "I had a very strong feeling I was not a mama's boy."], [427.3, "And even though I had very little money, I was poor after school, I had a really bad job and I had no money, it was very difficult, very tough for me,"], [441.2, "but I would never have gone back to live with my parents, because it's such a bad thing."], [449.1, "I wanted to be independent; I did not want to live with my parents again."], [455.6, "So this was very, very strong for me."], [458.2, "And it's very, very strong for most Americans, in fact."], [463.8, "There's another thing that's quite different, I think, between the United States and some other countries."], [473.3, "And that's with older people And with parents."], [478.2, "So for example."], [480.4, "In some countries, parents want the children to come and live with them."], [488.1, "So the parents want them to stay."], [492.8, "But in the United States, again, most parents do not."], [497.7, "Most parents want the children to leave."], [502.0, "Why?"], [503.2, "Because they hate their children?"], [506.0, "No."], [507.4, "Because they don't love their children?"], [509.9, "No."], [511.6, "Because they think they must help their children become independent."], [518.4, "This is very important in American society."], [522.5, "So parents know this."], [524.7, "So the parents don't want their children to be too weak."], [529.2, "They don't want their children to have problems."], [533.4, "They want their children to be strong and independent."], [537.5, "So it's not only the children."], [539.7, "The children want to be independent."], [541.6, "Most children want to leave the house."], [544.8, "Most children like me, I wanted to leave."], [548.7, "I was 18, I wanted to be free."], [552.6, "But also parents want their children to be independent."], [556.2, "It."], [556.5, "My father wanted me to leave."], [560.4, "He did not want me to live at home and he would not have been happy."], [567.7, "He would have been very unhappy if I stayed at home."], [572.9, "So it's both with the parents and the children."], [575.9, "Now it's not always there are mama's boys in America but it's you know in our culture it's seen as something bad."], [584.1, "And it's seen as something negative."], [588.4, "Now this is also true somewhat for older people when people become old."], [598.3, "So it's a little different, but still many old people in America when they're quite old."], [608.4, "They also want to be independent."], [611.2, "So maybe they're 70 years old."], [613.1, "Maybe they're 80 years old, but they want to be independent; they don't want to live with their children."], [624.6, "This is a big difference between America and other countries also, because I know in many countries the older parents will live with their children."], [639.7, "The children feel they must take care of their older parents."], [646.3, "So in my school, many students, they felt, oh my god, America is terrible."], [655.2, "They're terrible."], [656.1, "The children don't take care of their old parents."], [661.0, "They don't want them to stay in the house with them."], [666.4, "And, you know, maybe it's true sometimes, but it's also true that the parents often do not want to live with their children."], [675.3, "They want to stay independent even when they're very old."], [682.0, "For example, my grandmother, my grandmother, my father's mother, she likes to be independent."], [693.8, "She lives in her own apartment."], [696.8, "She's over 80 years old, but she has her own apartment in a community, and she likes it."], [705.2, "She has a lot of friends."], [706.8, "She still does many things, many activities, so she likes to be independent."], [715.2, "So this is a strong cultural point for the United States."], [721.4, "It's this idea of independence."], [725.8, "It's strong at every age that we value independence, and on the other side, we don't value dependence."], [737.4, "Finally, this can cause problems with dating, with relationships, with husbands and wives, with girlfriends and boyfriends."], [748.8, "So, another example is from my life."], [753.1, "Tomoe and I."], [755.3, "We often have discussions, disagreements."], [760.4, "Sometimes arguments about this idea of independence."], [765.9, "Because for me, in a relationship with her, I feel I want, I still want time alone."], [775.3, "I want to be alone sometimes."], [777.0, "I often want to do things with my friends alone so not together with her."], [786.4, "So I like a lot of time doing stuff alone, and I need that."], [793.0, "I need that time to work alone, to do some things with just my friends, just to sit and read, and, I don't know, exercise, whatever."], [805.2, "Just alone by myself."], [807.7, "But Tomoe, she's Japanese, you know, this is true in Japan also, but less true."], [815.4, "So Tomoe likes to spend much more time together."], [821.1, "So she feels that I'm too independent sometimes."], [826.1, "She often says that I'm too independent, and that it's strange that, you know, we're together but I am still so independent."], [837.1, "So it's a cultural difference; you know, she's not wrong, I'm not wrong, but it is different."], [845.7, "We do have to discuss this all the time, and it does cause problems many times, because we view this very differently."], [856.7, "Sometimes other countries, other cultures."], [860.4, "They think Americans were selfish."], [863.7, "We're selfish."], [864.5, "We only care about ourselves."], [867.0, "And it's very negative and bad."], [869.4, "And some of my students, they get upset because they think, oh Americans, they're selfish."], [876.3, "They're selfish."], [877.2, "So they think it's quite negative."], [879.5, "But you know we think it's very positive so we think it's good we're independent we take care of ourselves we don't make other people help us so much."], [893.4, "And so we feel it's a very good that these are good things so are they good are they bad no they're not good or bad it's just different cultures."], [906.1, "Anyway, so that explains the idea of mama's boys."], [906.7, "I hope you enjoyed the story; it's a little bit funny, I think."], [907.6, "It's a little funny, but also it gives you a little idea about independence in American culture and how important it is."], [909.2, "Okay, I hope you enjoyed this little commentary."], [909.7, "See you next time, bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
