 "a", "No, I couldn't."], [2852.5, "s", "I couldn't eat Indian curries anymore."], [2863.8, "s", "Who couldn't eat Indian curries anymore."], [2868.5, "q", "Why couldn't I eat Indian curries anymore?"], [2876.2, "a", "Because my stomach was sick."], [2878.9, "s", "Because my stomach was sick, I couldn't eat Indian curries anymore."], [2885.4, "q", "What could I eat?"], [2891.1, "a", "Bananas and white rice."], [2893.4, "s", "I could eat bananas and white rice could."], [2898.8, "s", "I eat spaghetti."], [2901.4, "s", "No only bananas and white rice the doctor said I could eat only bananas and white rice he."], [2916.5, "s", "gave me a big banana."], [2920.1, "s", "I ate it and I was very happy; my stomach felt much better."], [2929.4, "q", "Did I feel better?"], [2932.3, "a", "Yes, my stomach felt much better."], [2936.6, "q", "Why did my stomach feel much better?"], [2941.6, "a", "Because I ate a big banana did."], [2947.8, "s", "I feel better because I ate a banana yes."], [2952.9, "s", "I felt better much better because I ate a banana."], [2960.1, "s", "I was very happy."], [2963.8, "s", "Okay, that is all."], [2965.2, "s", "That is the end of the mini-story for Sick in India."]]}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.8, "Hi, this is AJ, and this is a commentary for Sick in India."], [10.3, "I'm going to talk a little about that story and where that story comes from."], [19.0, "Actually, the Sick in India story is a little bit true."], [24.0, "Because I did go to Jodhpur India, and I did get sick, very sick, and in Jodhpur."], [32.6, "Now, not all of the story is true, but a lot of it's true."], [36.4, "It was my first time."], [38.8, "Traveling outside the United States."], [42.0, "And I decided to go to India because."], [45.9, "I don't know, I had a strong interest in India for many different reasons."], [52.6, "One reason is that I'm Buddhist."], [55.5, "So Buddhism comes from India."], [57.7, "It was born in India."], [59.7, "So that's that was a big reason I wanted to go."], [62.4, "But in general, I just I like the diversity of India."], [66.8, "So many different kinds of people, languages, religions."], [72.5, "And of course, it has such a long, deep, ancient history."], [78.5, "So for all of these reasons, I wanted to visit India."], [83.5, "But unfortunately, on my first trip to India I became very sick, in Jodhpur, India, in fact, which is in the desert."], [93.5, "It's in the western part of India called Rajasthan; the state is called Rajasthan and the town is called Jodhpur."], [102.6, "So I was in Jodhpur and I was getting more and more sick."], [108.5, "And just like in the story, I had diarrhea, I had nausea, I was vomiting, I was very weak, I was pale; all these things were happening to me."], [121.6, "So I got to Jodhpur feeling terrible, and I got a cheap little guest house."], [128.4, "Actually, I shared a guest house with a British tourist; I met her on the train going to Jodhpur."], [137.0, "And we shared a place to save money, as I was broke, I had no money."], [144.3, "And she was also broke, she didn't have much money either."], [147.6, "And then she convinced me to go see the fort."], [151.0, "So Jodhpur has an incredible fort."], [155.7, "In fact in Rajasthan there are many towns with incredible forts and they're usually on top of these huge hills or mountains."], [165.4, "These big castles, big forts."], [168.2, "Very impressive."], [170.3, "Very fantastic looking from the bottom down in the city."], [175.7, "You look up and you see this huge hill with this giant fort."], [180.2, "It's really great."], [182.0, "So we went up there, went to the fort."], [184.9, "And I started feeling really bad at the beginning at the entrance to the fort."], [191.7, "So I told this British girl, I said, oh, just go ahead."], [195.9, "Go ahead and see the fort yourself."], [200.3, "I'm going to stay here and rest."], [203.1, "So I sat down, I rested near the entrance to the fort and I was feeling worse and worse."], [211.0, "And then I vomited."], [212.7, "I'm sorry."], [214.5, "This is not a nice story."], [216.4, "But anyway, I threw up, I vomited outside the fort, and then I lay down."], [222.5, "I was so weak I could hardly stand up; you know, it was very difficult to stand up."], [229.8, "So I waited and waited, and the British girl finally came back, and she could see I was really sick."], [238.0, "And I asked her, you know, please take me to a doctor."], [242.9, "So we walked down to some taxis, rickshaws actually, but they're like little taxis."], [248.6, "And then, I remember, it's one of my strong memories from traveling in India, the taxi driver wanted a lot of money."], [257.5, "He could see that I was sick, he knew I really needed a taxi, so he tried to charge extra; he tried to charge us a very high price."], [269.3, "And so the girl was upset, and another American guy there was upset, and they're arguing about the price."], [277.1, "And I'm trying to stand up, very weak, and finally I just sit down on the street."], [284.0, "I'm so weak and The taxi driver won because I just said oh, I don't care."], [290.0, "I'll pay anything Take me to the doctor."], [293.1, "I'm too sick to argue about the money."], [296.4, "So."], [297.6, "So we got in the taxi and."], [301.5, "Went to a."], [303.3, "hospital in the middle of Jodhpur."], [306.2, "I don't know where it was, or is; I couldn't find it again, actually, because it's not a famous hospital."], [315.8, "And at this hospital, they were surprised to see me, because this was an Indian hospital and they treated Indian people."], [325.9, "They never got, you know, American or European patients."], [330.2, "So I was kind of strange for them, kind of something new."], [334.8, "Because normally there may be more expensive hospitals somewhere that the foreigners might go to like private hospitals."], [345.1, "But I went to this one in the middle of the city so they finally had to wait a long time for the doctor but he finally came and he was a really, really nice guy."], [359.5, "He had gone to medical school in England."], [364.8, "So he spoke excellent English, which was nice for me, made it easy for me."], [370.9, "And in the story, you know, I just eat a banana and I feel better."], [375.9, "But in the real story, I had to stay in the hospital for three days."], [382.3, "I was so sick, they made me stay."], [384.5, "Three days in the hospital giving me medicine every day and resting all day."], [392.5, "Now it's true, I only ate bananas and white rice."], [395.6, "My stomach was very bad, so the doctor told me, you know, just eat white rice and bananas, very simple food."], [404.9, "So, you know, one nice thing about this: the doctor and the nurses at this hospital were excellent, fantastic, better than the United States."], [417.4, "Many of you probably know that America, the United States, has terrible health care; so expensive."], [425.7, "And also the health care people are not so nice, usually; doctors are always in a hurry, they never take time to help you."], [438.2, "I hate doctors in America, I hate hospitals in America; unless I'm super sick, I will not go to a doctor here."], [449.7, "So I was surprised and actually happy in India, because the doctor was excellent, the nurses were very nice, the hospital was super clean."], [462.2, "And it was not expensive; it was very cheap compared to the United States."], [469.5, "So I got all this great care, lots of medicine, and I was feeling fantastic after three days."], [478.9, "And the bill was so small, I can't remember, maybe like a hundred dollars or something."], [487.2, "And, you know, in America that would cost probably"], [491.9, "$10,000 at least, maybe more; if you spend three nights in a hospital in America, probably at least $10,000."], [501.8, "I don't know exactly, maybe 15,000, maybe 12,000, I'm not sure, but very expensive."], [509.1, "So in India it was like 100 or $200; I was so happy, thank you so much."], [518.0, "After that I felt much better, and I enjoyed the rest of my trip."], [525.3, "But actually, for the rest of my trip I could not eat Indian curries; so that's also true from the story."], [536.2, "The doctor told me to eat simple food only, so it was terrible, because I love Indian food."], [545.6, "In San Francisco I go to Indian restaurants all the time."], [551.4, "In Malaysia, I visit my friend, and his wife is Indian, so we also go to many Indian restaurants."], [561.3, "We eat a lot of Indian food, and Indian food is fantastic; I love it."], [569.1, "So I was in India, but I couldn't eat anything only bananas and rice and like."], [576.7, "Plain bread, you know, just brown bread, chapati, they call it."], [582.7, "So it was a little bit difficult for me in India."], [587.5, "But it was a great trip, really fantastic."], [590.7, "And I've actually been to India three times total."], [595.1, "So that was my first trip, when I got very sick; then I went back a second time with a friend, and I went again a third time a few years ago."], [610.5, "And I hope to go yet again soon; I would like to go to South India sometime."], [618.8, "I have always traveled in North India: Bombay, Rajasthan, which is in the west, and then the north, like Delhi, Varanasi."], [628.9, "Bodh Gaya is the Buddhist holy city where Gautama Buddha sat under the tree and became enlightened; I visited there because I'm Buddhist."], [640.1, "And I also like to visit the Tibetan areas in India, where the Dalai Lama is; Dharamsala is a really nice place in India."], [651.7, "It's in the mountains and all these Tibetan people are there."], [656.1, "The Dalai Lama lives there."], [658.2, "That's his home."], [660.1, "The Tibetan government in exile is in Dharamsala and the Tibetan people are so wonderful, so fantastic."], [670.0, "So that's another great thing."], [673.2, "about visiting India is to visit these Tibetan areas, because the Tibetan people, I think, are very special people."], [683.2, "And it's terrible what the Chinese government has done to them; murdered them, you know, killed them, tortured them."], [693.1, "Horrible stuff that the Chinese government has done to the Tibetans, and also to the Falun Gong, another spiritual group."], [703.6, "The Chinese government kills them, tortures them, puts them in prison only because of their religion; really horrible."], [713.1, "So this is a special issue for me, the Tibetan issue, probably because I am a Buddhist."], [722.0, "And because I do feel some connection to the Tibetan people, because I visited them in India."], [730.9, "So I heard their stories about what the Chinese did to them or have done."], [737.7, "What the Chinese are still doing, the Chinese government."], [741.6, "So it's horrible."], [744.1, "So unfortunately this is happening everywhere."], [746.5, "You know the American government does terrible things also."], [751.2, "We have a prison on the Cuban island."], [755.7, "We also torture people and kill them."], [759.2, "So it's not only the Chinese government, but the Chinese government is quite bad, obviously."], [766.6, "So anyway, but more good news, happy news, that India is a fantastic place."], [771.9, "And I recommend."], [774.0, "If you have a chance, visit India."], [777.3, "It's a really amazing place."], [779.5, "It's a special place, I think."], [783.0, "Because."], [785.3, "Well, for many reasons."], [787.9, "The history is so ancient and old and, you know, so many religions started in India."], [800.1, "Hinduism and Buddhism, of course, and these are probably two of the oldest."], [808.5, "But also, these religions, these ideas, influenced the Middle East."], [816.1, "They've had an influence even on Christianity and even on Islam."], [823.4, "So it's kind of the spiritual center of the world, I think, India."], [832.0, "And you find every religion there so many religions you know they have a huge Muslim population Islamic population giant Hindu population of course Buddhists are there Christians are there even a small Jewish population."], [852.2, "Zoroastrianism Zoroastrians are there which is a very another old religion so it's amazing."], [860.6, "And then you have many different cultural groups."], [864.7, "A lot of different languages, people speak many different languages."], [869.6, "So much history going back so far."], [873.6, "It's just a fantastic place."], [876.4, "And it's a democracy."], [877.8, "So you have all these different people, but they still manage to have a democracy."], [887.3, "And I think that's hopeful."], [889.5, "It's not a perfect democracy, of course."], [892.7, "They have a lot of problems, but still, still, it's a democracy."], [898.5, "And it shows that even if it's very difficult, it's possible for very different people to live together."], [907.6, "To share a government."], [909.4, "To have a democracy."], [911.9, "And, you know, that's great."], [913.5, "It's something I really love about India also."], [917.6, "So, if you get a chance, go to India."], [922.5, "Alright, that is all of my commentary for the Sick in India story."], [928.8, "Hope you enjoyed it."], [929.9, "I'll see you next time."], [930.9, "This is AJ."], [932.0, "Bye-bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["by myself", "/baɪ maɪˈself/", "một mình"], ["though", "/ðəʊ/", "mặc dù"], ["stomach", "/ˈstʌmək/", "bụng, dạ dày"], ["get worse", "/ɡet wɜːs/", "trở nên tệ hơn"], ["nausea", "/ˈnɔːziə/", "cảm giác buồn nôn"], ["appetite", "/ˈæpɪtaɪt/", "sự thèm ăn"], ["diarrhea", "/ˌdaɪəˈrɪə/", "tiêu chảy"], ["vomiting", "/ˈvɒmɪtɪŋ/", "nôn mửa"], ["be filled with", "/bi fɪld wɪð/", "đầy, tràn ngập"], ["make my way to", "/meɪk maɪ weɪ tə/", "tìm đường đến"], ["fort", "/fɔːt/", "pháo đài"], ["hail a cab", "/heɪl ə kæb/", "vẫy taxi"], ["view", "/vjuː/", "cảnh, tầm nhìn"], ["sharp pain", "/ʃɑːp peɪn/", "cơn đau nhói"], ["pale", "/peɪl/", "tái nhợt"], ["weak", "/wiːk/", "yếu"], ["tourist", "/ˈtʊərɪst/", "khách du lịch"], ["nearest", "/ˈnɪərɪst/", "gần nhất"], ["ghost", "/ɡəʊst/", "con ma"], ["definitely", "/ˈdefɪnətli/", "chắc chắn"], ["nurse", "/nɜːs/", "y tá"], ["fill out", "/fɪl aʊt/", "điền (mẫu đơn)"], ["form", "/fɔːm/", "mẫu đơn"], ["blank", "/blæŋk/", "ô trống"], ["instead", "/ɪnˈsted/", "thay vào đó"], ["act as if", "/ækt əz ɪf/", "giả vờ như thể"], ["seizure", "/ˈsiːʒə(r)/", "cơn co giật"], ["examine", "/ɪɡˈzæmɪn/", "khám (bệnh)"], ["curry", "/ˈkʌri/", "món cà ri"]]$j$::jsonb,
