h the public."], [2005.5, "s", "The USDA completely lost touch with the public."], [2014.3, "s", "They'd probably say that eggshells are healthy if a company asked them to, said one consumer."], [2024.1, "q", "Who said they'd probably say?"], [2029.5, "a", "Said one consumer."], [2031.9, "s", "One consumer said they'd probably say that eggshells are healthy if a company asked them to."], [2041.9, "s", "What would they say about eggshells?"], [2046.4, "q", "Were they healthy or unhealthy?"], [2052.4, "a", "They'd probably say that eggshells are healthy."], [2059.2, "q", "Who would say that eggshells were healthy?"], [2066.3, "a", "The USDA."], [2067.2, "s", "USDA."], [2069.1, "q", "And who would ask the USDA to say that eggshells are healthy?"], [2076.5, "a", "A company."], [2078.8, "s", "If a company asked them to."], [2084.4, "s", "Asked them to."], [2087.7, "s", "Asked who to."], [2092.6, "s", "Asked the USDA to."], [2096.6, "s", "Ask the USDA to say that eggshells are healthy."], [2106.6, "s", "Consumers said that the USDA totally lost touch with the public."], [2114.5, "s", "Who did the USDA lose touch with?"], [2118.9, "q", "The public or consumers?"], [2123.2, "a", "The public."], [2125.4, "s", "The USDA totally lost touch with the public."], [2131.3, "s", "They'd probably say that eggshells are healthy if a company asked them to, said one consumer."], [2140.9, "q", "Who said it?"], [2143.8, "a", "One consumer."], [2146.4, "q", "What did the consumer say?"], [2149.6, "a", "The consumer said they'd probably say that eggshells are healthy if a company asked them to."], [2160.2, "q", "What would they say about eggshells?"], [2165.1, "a", "They'd say eggshells are healthy."], [2170.2, "q", "Who would say it?"], [2174.5, "a", "The USDA would say it."], [2178.6, "s", "The USDA would say eggshells are healthy if a company asked them to."], [2186.1, "s", "So, consumers said the USDA totally lost touch with the public."], [2194.8, "s", "They'd probably say that eggshells are healthy if a company asked them to, said one consumer."], [2204.6, "s", "Okay, that's it for Eat Your Vegetables."], [2208.2, "s", "Let's do the final read-through for the past tense."], [2214.6, "s", "Eat your vegetables."], [2216.2, "s", "The U.S."], [2218.9, "s", "Federal government displayed even less sense than usual and yielded to the French fry industry."], [2230.4, "s", "Frozen french fries."], [2232.4, "s", "Cut."], [2233.8, "s", "Fried in oil."], [2234.7, "s", "And then packaged have been approved as fresh vegetables by the U.S."], [2241.8, "s", "Department of Agriculture, USDA."], [2245.0, "s", "The French fry industry has been asking the USDA for years to get this approval."], [2256.6, "s", "They said that their product is similar to cucumbers that have wax on them."], [2264.5, "s", "They argued that they use 100% vegetable oil, which is much healthier for consumers than plain wax."], [2277.9, "s", "Most consumers, of course, beg to differ."], [2283.7, "s", "You must be joking, said Ann, 50."], [2289.5, "s", "How can you think a product that's deep fried in oil is a fresh vegetable?"], [2297.3, "s", "Even if I cooked broccoli, I could no longer call it fresh broccoli."], [2306.0, "s", "It's cooked!"], [2308.4, "s", "I wish I were a big company, so my congressman would help me."], [2315.8, "s", "Unfortunately, I'm only a citizen."], [2320.2, "s", "The USDA defended its decision and said that potatoes undeniably are vegetables."], [2334.4, "s", "Although French fries are fried in oil, they are still potatoes."], [2340.4, "s", "If you let them sit on your counter for a couple weeks."], [2344.5, "s", "A USDA spokesman said."], [2346.9, "s", "The fries will rot just like all other fresh vegetables."], [2356.0, "s", "Consumers said the USDA totally lost touch with the public."], [2365.6, "s", "They'd probably say that eggshells are healthy if a company asked them to, said one consumer."]]}]$j$::jsonb,
