  $j$[[0.3, "Welcome, Flow English listeners."], [4.0, "This is the commentary for Lemon Dog's Lucky Day."], [8.8, "A little background on Lemon Dog's Lucky Day and Lemon Dog."], [13.9, "I lived in Korea in 1997, 1998, and I lived in Seoul, actually the north side of Seoul."], [23.5, "I was living up on the northern part of Seoul in a place called Eum Pyeong-gu."], [30.7, "And I was teaching at a place called Kids College, teaching English."], [36.7, "Taught kindergartners through eighth graders for the most part, and we did whatever we needed to, to keep things interesting."], [46.2, "One of the things we like to do are to tell stories and draw cartoons."], [53.9, "I used to draw different cartoons and stories to make things interesting."], [61.1, "And one of the characters I came up with while I was there was a character."], [65.7, "A cartoon called Lemon Dog."], [68.8, "Lemon Dog was a character who loved lemons."], [73.0, "He loved everything with lemons."], [75.0, "He loved to cook with lemons."], [77.4, "He loved to sleep on lemons."], [80.6, "He loved to make pillows and food and clothing."], [85.6, "Whatever he could out of lemons and lemon skins."], [89.8, "Lemon products."], [91.2, "He loved lemons."], [93.4, "And my students loved Lemon Dog too."], [95.9, "They thought he was fun to get to know."], [99.1, "A fun way to learn English."], [100.9, "So I used to draw different cartoons, different days about the adventures of Lemon Dog."], [108.8, "Lemon Dog going around town again to the movies or the grocery store going on trips, that kind of thing."], [119.1, "So this story is inspired by Lemon Dog."], [121.9, "It's a new story that I wrote for Flow English."], [125.7, "I think we'll talk a little bit about the story as well."], [130.7, "We begin talking about a little background in the story about a Lemon Dog."], [136.4, "He's loving food that's made from lemons."], [139.7, "His mother's a bulldog."], [142.5, "His father's a sheepdog."], [144.8, "So they got together and they had him as a son."], [149.0, "We also talk about different fruit and vegetables in the story."], [156.5, "We also talk about the idea of being vegetarian."], [160.9, "We talk about the idea of being vegan."], [164.6, "So I've been vegetarian for 17 years and my good friend AJ that you all know also has been vegetarian for a number of years and he's currently vegan."], [175.9, "So we wanted to include some talk about food."], [180.3, "Food idioms."], [182.0, "Also about eating practices, dietary practices."], [187.2, "Including being vegetarian and being vegan."], [191.5, "Being vegetarian means you don't eat any meat or flesh, no fish as well."], [201.1, "Being vegan means avoiding all animal products, including milk and dairy products."], [209.6, "So being vegetarian, being vegan."], [213.1, "That's a health practice that both AJ and I stick to and it's also we believe good for the environment, good for the animals."], [222.7, "It's an animal welfare issue and we both have concerns about the environment and the way animals are treated in factory farming."], [232.3, "So that's a little bit of background about us and a little bit of background about the story."], [237.2, "So, in the story."], [240.2, "Um."], [241.3, "Lemon Dog's father is a sheep dog."], [244.4, "And a sheep dog is a dog that should protect sheep."], [250.0, "But he doesn't protect sheep, he eats sheep."], [254.3, "So he's supposed to protect them, but he eats them."], [257.9, "So we say he's crazy, we say he's as nutty as a fruitcake."], [264.1, "He's crazy."], [264.8, "So nutty means crazy, and then another expression, nutty as a fruitcake, also means crazy."], [272.4, "There are a lot of nuts in a fruitcake, so that's where that comes from."], [280.0, "Later in the story, it talks about Lemon Dog before he liked lemons: he liked pumpkin."], [288.1, "In fact, he only ate things made from pumpkin when he was a puppy."], [295.2, "So we talk about vegan cream of pumpkin popsicles."], [299.8, "So that's sort of a silly idea but we thought we thought that might be funny and so the vegan cream of pumpkin popsicles."], [312.1, "Vegans don't eat cream."], [314.3, "They don't eat milk or cheese or cream."], [317.4, "So in the story, it's vegan cream of pumpkin popsicles."], [322.4, "The cream is actually made from soy milk."], [325.8, "It's not actually milk, it's we say instead of using cream, he uses soy milk for the popsicles."], [333.6, "The popsicles are a frozen treat."], [337.9, "You may or may not know what a popsicle is, but it's usually a frozen juice treat made out of orange juice or grape juice, something like that."], [346.3, "Also called an icicle, but usually called a popsicle, a flavored popsicle."], [352.4, "Later in the story, Lemon Dog decides he wants to throw a party, and again he decides that everything will be made from lemon."], [364.5, "So he's gonna make lemon soup and lemon sandwiches, lemon salad; he wants to make lemon cake and lemon pie."], [374.7, "But it's going to take a lot of lemons to make all this, so he needs to buy 36,000 lemons."], [384.8, "So in the first part of the story, he decides that everybody's going to love his party."], [391.4, "As long as he makes everything from lemons."], [395.2, "So everything for the party will be made from lemons."], [400.0, "And the first part ends with him finding his keys and driving away, and then it's a to-be-continued story."], [409.2, "So you have to wait to see what happens in the next part of the story."], [416.9, "So as the suspense builds and you can't resist, you go and start studying part two of Lemon Dog's Lucky Day."], [427.0, "And it begins again with him getting into his car and driving off."], [433.3, "He has to make his way through traffic, so we get to talk about a number of different idioms on his way."], [441.6, "Getting through a long line of traffic, we also talk about his car being souped up."], [448.5, "Which means he has a high powered car."], [451.6, "He made changes to his car to soup it up."], [456.8, "When he gets to the grocery store, he goes straight to the fruit and vegetable aisle."], [463.2, "Isle is a word we use for line or lane."], [467.7, "So he goes straight to the part of the store where the fruit and vegetables are."], [473.4, "And then he has a great experience there because he looks at the shelf and he sees beautiful sexy delicious lemons."], [484.0, "So this helps us Let's understand how much Lemon Dog loves lemons because he thinks they're beautiful."], [493.5, "He thinks they're sexy."], [495.4, "He thinks they're delicious."], [498.1, "So he couldn't feel any better, stronger feeling towards lemons."], [504.2, "He loves them."], [505.4, "He thinks they're beautiful, sexy, and delicious."], [509.6, "He can see that they're loaded with lots of juice."], [514.3, "Means they're full of lots of juice, and he loads his shopping cart up with 36,001 plump juicy lemons."], [527.4, "So he takes his cart, he takes his lemons up to the checkout line."], [533.6, "And the cashier knows him."], [537.6, "She knows that he likes to buy lemons, but she's not used to him buying so many lemons."], [546.4, "She rings up his bill, that means she totals his bill, and the bill is $53 million."], [554.4, "So it's a huge bill."], [557.2, "And Lemon Dog is very upset because he only has $40 million with him."], [562.7, "So, he doesn't know what to do."], [565.7, "He doesn't know how to deal with it."], [569.7, "But, it's Lemon Dog's lucky day."], [572.8, "So, it's a lucky day for Lemon Dog."], [575.0, "It's a good day."], [576.8, "Because, the cashier likes Lemon Dog."], [580.2, "In fact, she has strong feelings for Lemon Dog."], [584.3, "She thinks he is beautiful, sexy, and delicious."], [591.6, "So this is a parallel in the story."], [594.0, "Lemon Dog loves lemons."], [596.8, "The cashier loves Lemon Dog."], [600.4, "So just like Lemon Dog thinks that the lemons are beautiful and sexy and delicious."], [608.4, "The cashier thinks that Lemon Dog is beautiful, sexy and delicious, so she makes a deal with Lemon Dog."], [617.9, "She says that she'll pay for the rest of the lemons if Lemon Dog invites her to the party."], [627.4, "And he thinks that's a great deal too; he agrees and he says great."], [634.4, "So he pays the 40 million and the cashier pays the 13 million, and everything gets paid for."], [643.4, "Lemon Dog leaves the store and he gives the cashier his telephone number so the cashier can call him later about the party."], [653.8, "And as he's leaving Lemon Dog says call me and he sort of leaves the store with a smile and that's where the end of the story is."], [663.8, "That's the last part of the story."], [668.5, "But it sort of has a to-be-continued feel with the dot after the store."], [675.3, "So you can imagine that there will be later lessons at some point involving Lemon Dog for Flow English."], [684.0, "Okay, so that's the brief commentary on Lemon Dog."], [688.9, "A little bit of background about myself."], [690.8, "The time I spent in Korea."], [693.4, "Where Lemon Dog came from, the idea for Lemon Dog,?"], [698.4, "And a little bit about Lemon Dog and his love of lemons."], [704.7, "Okay, thanks for listening."], [707.0, "I'll talk to you again soon on Flow English."]]$j$::jsonb,
