  $j$[[0.4, "Hi, this is AJ again with another commentary."], [4.9, "This is a commentary for Roach Vacation."], [7.8, "Now, I'm not going to talk about roaches right now, but I'm going to talk about vacations and travel."], [15.5, "So actually, that story, that Roach Vacation story."], [19.9, "It came from my."], [22.8, "The idea came from my travels to Chapel Hill, North Carolina."], [30.2, "Chapel Hill, North Carolina is where Chris Moses lives."], [34.6, "The other person on these lessons, Chris Moses."], [38.8, "So Chris lives in Chapel Hill, North Carolina."], [42.0, "Chapel Hill, North Carolina is in the east, the eastern part of the United States."], [49.8, "It's actually in the southeast."], [52.9, "So North Carolina is in the southeast."], [55.7, "I, AJ, I live in San Francisco, which is in the west on the west coast, of course."], [63.5, "So I had a very difficult trip coming here."], [68.3, "It was terrible."], [69.8, "In fact."], [70.6, "So I had a ticket, of course, I had a ticket on American Airlines to fly to Chapel Hill."], [78.3, "I was supposed to get up in the morning and leave in the morning, I think it was 9 o'clock in the morning, and I was supposed to arrive in Chapel Hill about 7 o'clock at night, 7 or 8 at night."], [95.7, "So it would be okay."], [97.1, "It's a little bit long because I had to fly across the United States, across the country, but not bad."], [107.0, "Unfortunately, the night before, the American Airlines called me on my cell phone at 2 a.m."], [117.1, "2 in the morning, they called me and left a message."], [122.1, "So I'm sleepy, I wake up, I check my message, it says, your flight is cancelled."], [129.6, "Dammit, man!"], [131.0, "So I was unhappy."], [132.7, "My flight was cancelled, and they gave me a new flight."], [136.4, "The new flight was leaving, I think, at 10 o'clock at night."], [141.9, "Which is terrible."], [145.0, "I hate to fly at night."], [148.4, "I hate buses at night."], [150.8, "I hate planes at night."], [152.6, "It's terrible, because I can't sleep."], [154.8, "You know, some people are lucky, they can sleep on a plane."], [159.7, "Tomoe can sleep on a plane, she's usually okay, but she's little."], [164.0, "But I know people, they get on a plane."], [166.7, "They can fly all night, and they sleep."], [170.0, "And the next day they don't feel terrible, they feel okay."], [173.4, "But not me, I feel terrible."], [176.8, "When I take a bus or a train at night, I never sleep,?"], [181.8, "Also I have long legs, my legs are very long."], [185.6, "And the seats are always small."], [187.9, "And so it's very uncomfortable for me."], [192.2, "So I was unhappy, they changed my flight."], [196.2, "So anyway, I slept all night, and the next day I got up, and so I went to the airport."], [203.8, "But then I got to the airport, and my flight was canceled again!"], [209.2, "They canceled it again, and now they gave me a new flight."], [213.3, "This time at 11 o'clock at night so or 1130 I think it was so this is my third flight now it's at 11 30 p.m."], [224.8, "So, very late, I'm tired, I'm at the airport."], [228.9, "So anyway, I sit at the San Francisco Airport; luckily I had my computer, and they had a wireless connection, so I could get on the internet."], [241.1, "So I did some email, just waiting for my plane, and then they delayed my flight."], [248.4, "So they didn't cancel it, not canceled, not finished, but they delayed it; delayed means late, it's gonna be late."], [257.5, "So now my flight was at 12:40, so after midnight."], [262.0, "12:40, oh no, so this was not good."], [265.7, "But anyway, I got on the flight at 12:40 and flew to Chicago, because it was not a direct flight."], [274.9, "A direct flight means no stopping, right, no stopping in between; but this was not a direct flight, I had to stop in Chicago and change."], [286.9, "Unfortunately, I missed my next flight, because my first flight was late, because it was delayed."], [294.3, "I got to Chicago, and my next airplane was already gone; it had left."], [300.8, "Oh, so I'm very tired, because I had no sleep that night, and now I missed my plane; I have to find another plane."], [311.9, "So I go to American Airlines and I show them my boarding pass, and they say, oh, okay."], [320.2, "They check their computer, and the next flight was like four hours later, so they give me a new boarding pass for the new flight in four hours."], [333.1, "So then I had to wait in the Chicago Airport for four hours, and I have no sleep, I'm very tired."], [342.8, "I tried to sleep, I lay down on the floor in the Chicago Airport; I didn't really sleep, maybe a little bit."], [352.9, "And then finally I couldn't sleep, so I decided to drink some coffee; I went to Starbucks and got a big coffee and drank it."], [364.5, "And then finally I got on my last plane, and I arrived here in North Carolina, I think at about four o'clock in the afternoon."], [376.0, "And I rented a car and I drove to Chris's house, but I was really tired; of course I was exhausted, because of this whole long night and day without sleep, in airports, in airplanes; truly terrible."], [393.1, "So anyway, I came here, and then I took a nap; and really, the next day I went to sleep and slept really late, until I finally felt better."], [406.5, "So that's where I thought about the Roach Vacation story."], [411.1, "I thought that we should write a story about traveling, so people can learn a little vocabulary like boarding pass; that's a very common"], [422.2, "word, a very common phrase that you hear in the airports all the time."], [428.8, "But I was also just thinking about airplanes and travel a lot, so that's why that one's on there."], [437.7, "So, in general, then I arrived here in North Carolina, and this is where we have recorded all the lessons for Flow English."], [448.6, "So we've been recording at Chris's house; each of us has a laptop computer, and we each have an expensive professional microphone and some recording software for our computers."], [462.2, "And so for, I guess, over two weeks now, every day we're recording lessons; we write the stories and we record the lessons."], [473.0, "And it's been a lot of work; my head is crazy, because I'm just thinking about lessons and stories all the time."], [483.4, "But you know it's also been fun."], [485.4, "Chris is an old friend so we know each other."], [488.4, "We have known each other for a long time."], [492.3, "Chris and I met in 1994."], [498.7, "We went to school together at the University of Georgia."], [503.0, "We went to graduate school together, master's degree program."], [508.3, "So since then, we have known each other."], [511.2, "After we finished school."], [513.9, "After we finished our master's degrees."], [516.9, "Actually we both worked at the 1996 Atlanta Olympics."], [524.4, "We both worked there for the summer."], [526.6, "We had summer jobs at the Olympics."], [529.0, "And then both Chris and I taught English in Korea together; it was our first teaching jobs, actually, both of us."], [540.3, "We both taught in Seoul, Korea; for anyone from Korea, I can tell you my neighborhood: I lived in Yeonhui-dong in Seoul."], [552.2, "Korea."], [553.2, "This was in 1996 and 1997."], [557.7, "It was my very first English teaching job, and I was teaching little children, little Korean children."], [566.1, "In fact, they were great."], [567.4, "They learned English so fast because little children learn very, very fast."], [574.6, "That experience, I think, it affected me."], [580.1, "Seeing the children learn fast, you know, I started thinking, why do adults have so much trouble?"], [591.1, "Right?"], [591.6, "Because, you know, I was trying to learn a little Korean, but it was so difficult for me."], [598.7, "But my little children in my class, they're learning English very, very, very fast."], [604.6, "After one month, my students were speaking only English in my class."], [611.6, "I had a rule, no Korean."], [613.9, "So after one month, no Korean, these little children could speak only English to me."], [620.6, "It's amazing."], [622.8, "So, you know, later I got another master's degree."], [626.6, "My second master's degree is in English, teaching English."], [632.1, "And I learned about this idea of learning languages, and the differences between adults and children."], [641.2, "And there are different ideas about this; some people think that, you know, children have a special ability and adults lose it, that adults can't learn in a natural way."], [658.2, "Some people think this."], [660.5, "However."], [662.5, "Other people, including me."], [664.9, "Think that adults can learn like children."], [669.1, "That we definitely can learn like children."], [671.8, "There's good research about this, that in fact, adults can do it."], [678.7, "The problem is, adults don't do it."], [683.1, "Children learn very naturally."], [686.4, "Basically, how do children."], [689.0, "Little children, small children."], [691.2, "Kindergarten."], [691.9, "First grade, four years old, five years old, how do they learn a new language."], [699.1, "A foreign language?"], [701.6, "Well, basically they listen."], [703.9, "Basically they listen."], [705.0, "My little Korean students listen to me every day."], [709.8, "They listen to me tell stories."], [712.4, "They listened to me sing songs and they sang songs also."], [718.7, "We played games."], [721.5, "We did little picture games, but they mostly they listened, they listened, they listened."], [728.3, "I didn't force them to speak."], [731.3, "I didn't say, you must speak."], [733.0, "Okay."], [734.2, "They, I was relaxed."], [735.5, "They could just listen, listen, listen."], [739.4, "Did they study grammar?"], [740.5, "My little four-year-old children?"], [742.9, "No, of course not."], [744.2, "We never studied grammar rules."], [746.8, "They couldn't understand grammar rules, but they did learn grammar."], [751.8, "They learn grammar from the stories."], [754.5, "They learn grammar from listening to me."], [757.9, "So they learned natural grammar, not textbook grammar."], [763.0, "But what do adults do?"], [764.4, "Do adults learn this way usually?"], [767.8, "No."], [769.1, "What do adults, and by adults I mean middle school, high school, university, and older."], [777.9, "Older children and adults learn very unnaturally."], [785.0, "What do they do?"], [786.1, "They get textbooks and they study these difficult, complicated rules."], [792.9, "The past tense, the past perfect, the present perfect, the past perfect, progressive, modals, etc., etc., right?"], [804.5, "All these difficult grammar ideas."], [808.6, "What do adults do also?"], [810.0, "Adults try to speak too soon."], [814.5, "They force themselves to speak."], [816.9, "In an adult class, on the first day, or let's say middle school in Japan, day one, they make those children say, hello, how are you?"], [830.7, "Repeat after me: hello, how are you?"], [834.4, "And the middle school children say, hello, how are you, and they say, no, try it again."], [843.4, "So it's all speaking, speaking."], [846.1, "Speaking, not listening."], [847.9, "Not listening to correct English."], [851.9, "Not listening to native speakers."], [854.4, "Not listening to funny stories."], [857.5, "No."], [858.5, "They are trying to speak immediately."], [862.6, "So that's what, that's the problem."], [865.1, "That's why adults cannot learn or do not learn the same as children."], [873.7, "What do adults need to do?"], [876.7, "Well, if you want to speak well, if you want to have natural English, you've got to listen."], [883.5, "You've got to focus on listening first."], [886.7, "You've got to forget the grammar rules."], [889.3, "Focus on listening, listening, listening."], [892.3, "Relax."], [893.5, "Be like a child."], [896.2, "Learn like a little small child."], [900.4, "Don't think about rules."], [904.0, "Just listen to stories."], [907.6, "Listen."], [909.5, "When you can speak, just speak."], [913.2, "Communicate."], [915.3, "If you make a mistake, it's okay."], [917.7, "Don't think about mistakes."], [919.1, "Little children don't worry about mistakes."], [922.5, "Only adults are so serious."], [924.4, "Oh no, I must not make a mistake."], [928.8, "So, try to be like a little child."], [932.2, "That's the best way to learn English."], [936.2, "Okay."], [936.9, "See you next time."], [938.0, "Bye-bye."], [938.4, "This is AJ."]]$j$::jsonb,
