t Jimbo will be very happy."], [564.2, "He'll buy 65,000 TVs, 80,000 cell phones, and 28,000 electric toothbrushes."], [573.8, "The End."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.1, "Okay, welcome to the commentary for Financial Liberation."], [6.3, "I'm just going to talk about some main ideas in this article and a little bit about my life and how I have used these ideas."], [16.4, "To create a successful business and to become free financially."], [24.9, "So let's talk about that little bit."], [27.0, "First of all, the quote is from a book called Small is Beautiful."], [31.6, "It's an excellent book, a very interesting book, by an economist."], [35.7, "Now this is not a book about Buddhism."], [39.7, "This one quote, this one section."], [44.0, "Very short, it's two paragraphs."], [46.0, "He just talks about Buddhist economics simply because he likes the idea."], [53.0, "So this man, E.F."], [54.9, "Schumacher, he's not a Buddhist and the book is not about Buddhism in any way."], [60.8, "It's about economics and the rest of the book talks about other economic ideas."], [67.3, "So this little section about Buddhism and Buddhist economics is just a small part of the book and you don't need to be a Buddhist to understand these ideas or to agree with these ideas."], [81.2, "The writer, E.F."], [82.4, "Schumacher, is not a Buddhist."], [85.2, "So anyway, so don't worry about that part."], [87.4, "It's not about religion."], [88.5, "It's about economics."], [90.2, "It's about becoming more free with your money and free with your life."], [96.5, "That's the idea."], [98.4, "Okay, so anyway, it's a great book."], [99.8, "E.F."], [100.2, "Schumacher, Small is Beautiful."], [103.5, "And of course, the title, Small Is Beautiful, gives the idea of this central philosophy, this central method, this central way of thinking."], [117.3, "Right? We are usually taught, especially in the United States, that big is better."], [125.7, "That is probably the motto, probably the number one belief in America: big is better, more is better."], [136.4, "That is our economy; that is our culture."], [141.2, "Sometimes big is better, sometimes more is better, but not always; often it's the opposite."], [150.2, "Often small is better; often small is beautiful."], [155.0, "And that's what I want you to think about, because for many years I did not have much money; I was not successful."], [168.8, "Not successful, I mean, I had jobs that I did not like."], [175.3, "For many years, 23 years, I had jobs I didn't like, I had bosses that I didn't like."], [185.0, "I had very little money, and I didn't feel free."], [190.4, "That's the most important part for me."], [193.4, "I didn't feel free."], [194.8, "I couldn't do what I wanted to do."], [197.7, "I couldn't live the life I wanted to live."], [201.9, "So I really thought about this a lot and I read a lot of books."], [207.2, "Now there are a lot of business books."], [209.7, "a lot of books about improving your career and your job, and a lot of books about starting your own company or your own business."], [222.7, "And, you know, they all have some good ideas, usually, but they have a central problem."], [231.1, "The central problem is that they convince you, they tell you, that getting more money is your first job, your first goal, the most important thing."], [244.6, "And it's not the most important thing."], [248.3, "I know a lot of people who have a lot of money."], [253.4, "They make a lot of money."], [255.4, "They have big houses, big cars, but they're not free."], [259.4, "They're not happy."], [262.2, "They're stressed; they work all the time, work, work, work, always working."], [268.2, "And, you know, they don't even enjoy their jobs much; they don't really like their jobs, and often their boss is not nice."], [279.8, "So they're stressed, they're not so happy, and they feel they always need more."], [286.9, "Right? Most people look at them and think, oh, they're rich, but they don't feel rich."], [294.9, "They feel they need more and then more and then more and then more."], [300.2, "So this is not a way to be successful, I don't think, in my opinion."], [306.0, "It's not very successful."], [310.7, "There's another problem, and this is a bigger problem."], [315.6, "Maybe you're not rich, probably you're not, like me, okay?"], [321.4, "For most of my life I was not rich and there's a problem when you're not rich."], [329.4, "And then you think, oh, I need to be rich, I need to be rich."], [335.0, "You create a lot of stress in your life, and you always focus on what you do not have; it's just natural, right?"], [343.5, "You're always worrying: I don't have this, I don't have enough, I don't have enough."], [349.1, "Constantly thinking this, that creates stress."], [354.5, "It also stops you from being more successful."], [360.4, "When you think that way, when you focus on what you don't have,?"], [365.1, "When you focus on not having enough,?"], [369.2, "Well, then you usually continue to not have enough; you continue to be stressed; you make bad decisions."], [376.8, "So let me tell you about my life, and how this happened with me."], [382.7, "In the beginning, I thought, okay, I'm not free, and I'm not happy in my jobs, and I want to be free."], [392.0, "So I thought, okay, I need more money; I have to make a lot more money."], [398.7, "If I make a lot more money, I'll be free."], [401.6, "I'll be successful."], [402.7, "I'll be happy."], [404.3, "So I tried to get a job that made a lot more money."], [410.7, "Of course I failed, okay, because I didn't have the skills I needed."], [417.6, "And so I went back to school and then I did start getting jobs that paid more."], [425.0, "But then I discovered, wow, I'm still not making very much."], [429.0, "I'm making more, I'm better than the past, but I still feel like I don't have enough."], [435.1, "I always wanted more; I thought, well, now I need a bigger apartment."], [439.8, "Now I need a... you know, I have a very old, ugly car; maybe I need a nicer car."], [446.6, "And also, I was unhappy at my jobs."], [449.5, "My bosses were not so nice."], [452.5, "I hated the schedule."], [453.8, "I don't like working from nine to five or sometimes you know eight to five or sometimes seven to six."], [462.2, "You know I don't like working a lot."], [464.6, "I enjoy my life."], [465.8, "I enjoy my friends."], [467.4, "I don't want to work all the time."], [470.7, "So then I tried to join this business."], [474.6, "Some friends were doing a business; they were selling vitamins, and, you know, like pills to make you more healthy."], [484.3, "And I thought, oh, I can get rich, I can sell these pills and these vitamins, and I'll have enough money."], [494.5, "And then I'll be rich and free, and I'll feel happy."], [499.8, "Well, again, I was focusing on not having enough."], [504.2, "I was focusing on getting more and more and more only."], [508.3, "So what happened?"], [510.0, "Well, I failed, of course I failed."], [515.8, "Well, a few reasons."], [517.2, "Number one, I didn't really care about vitamins and pills."], [524.5, "Not really."], [525.3, "I was not excited about it."], [528.0, "I just cared about the money; I just wanted to become more rich, more free and happy, etc."], [536.2, "I didn't care about pills and vitamins, so how could I sell those things to other people, right?"], [544.4, "People know; they understand if you care or you don't care."], [549.4, "And I really didn't care, right? I was being selfish, only thinking about myself."], [555.8, "Only thinking about trying to make more money."], [560.8, "Another problem, I didn't trust the company really."], [566.5, "I knew inside I knew it was wrong, there was something wrong."], [571.3, "So I quit after a few months and I failed and I felt terrible and I went back to work at normal jobs and a lot of stress."], [582.1, "And then I read a great book, a classic book called Walden, Walden by Henry David Thoreau."], [593.3, "This is a classic American book."], [596.2, "Every American knows this book."], [598.2, "We have to read it in school."], [600.0, "But in school, when I was in high school, I didn't understand this book."], [604.5, "But reading it later, as an adult, oh, it was genius, amazing."], [609.0, "Now, it's a very difficult book; the English is very difficult."], [613.2, "You can try to read it if you want to, but let me warn you, it's quite difficult."], [620.0, "But the idea of this book is that this man,"], [623.8, "Henry David Thoreau, simplified his life."], [626.8, "He decided, I don't need a lot of things, I don't need a lot of money."], [634.6, "I'm going to go into the woods, into the forest, and I'm gonna make a small, tiny little house, like one little tiny room."], [646.5, "And I'm going to grow my food, and I'm going to live without money; I'm going to live a super simple life."], [657.3, "And then I will write about it, and I will see if I feel successful or not, if I feel free or not."], [668.6, "And he did it, and he wrote about it, and he discovered a secret: simplicity gives you freedom."], [677.5, "The less you need, the more free you are."], [681.9, "Now, this is actually a very religious, spiritual idea; Buddhism talks about this idea, but so do most major religions."], [691.8, "Most major religions, if you look."], [694.3, "Do have this idea that we don't need a lot of stuff, we don't need a lot of things, we don't need a lot of money."], [701.3, "And if we let go of that."], [704.2, "If we can live more simply."], [707.8, "We find."], [709.3, "It's a surprise sometimes."], [711.2, "We find, wow."], [712.6, "I feel more free."], [714.1, "I feel more relaxed."], [715.8, "This is Great."], [717.4, "And that's what happened to Thoreau."], [720.4, "And then he wrote about it, and he thought about it very deeply, and he created a philosophy."], [726.5, "So I read this book, and then I started reading a lot more books, reading a lot about, a lot of Buddhist books, in fact."], [732.8, "Taoist books."], [734.7, "Some Hindu-inspired books."], [737.6, "Even some books inspired by mystical Christianity and Islam."], [746.9, "And they all had this central idea, the same central idea of simplicity."], [752.7, "So I thought, well, I tried trying to get money, money, money, and I failed."], [758.9, "And it felt wrong."], [760.3, "It felt bad."], [761.9, "So let's try to live a simple life."], [767.0, "So I got rid of almost all of my stuff."], [773.4, "Almost everything."], [774.7, "I gave it away."], [775.6, "I gave, I didn't even sell it."], [777.4, "I just gave it to people."], [780.1, "And I decided to live in my car, a Toyota Corolla, a 1984 Toyota Corolla, very old car."], [790.0, "So I lived in this tiny little car and I built, I made a little bed inside this small car and I lived in the car for one summer with my dog."], [803.2, "Why did I do this?"], [805.6, "Was I crazy?"], [806.9, "Yes, a little crazy."], [810.0, "To live simply."], [812.5, "So I lived in my car with my dog for one summer."], [817.2, "And I found that Thoreau was correct."], [821.6, "Because living in my car was so cheap."], [825.3, "No rent, no power bills, right?"], [829.8, "Super cheap."], [831.2, "So I was free, I didn't need a job."], [833.9, "I already had some money saved a little bit but it was enough so I had a great time I had so much freedom every day I could wake up when I wanted to wake up I."], [848.0, "could do anything I wanted to do during the day."], [852.9, "I felt no stress, no worry; it was wonderful."], [857.2, "Now, of course, I ran out of money, right? Eventually I was spending all my money,"], [865.0, "Slowly but eventually."], [868.3, "And so I went to Japan actually and I got a job teaching there and then I saved more money and then I came back to America and this time I bought a van."], [878.7, "Kind of like a little truck, right?"], [880.0, "A van."], [881.0, "And I lived in the van for one year with my dog."], [886.5, "So again living very simply."], [889.2, "I learned to need less."], [892.8, "I learned to be comfortable with less."], [896.7, "I learned that I didn't need a big house."], [900.9, "I learned that I didn't need a big apartment."], [904.5, "I learned that I didn't need expensive clothes."], [909.5, "I learned that I didn't need anything expensive."], [914.6, "I learned that I needed only a few clothes and a small space to sleep and good food."], [925.3, "That's all."], [927.1, "And so during that year my needs got less and less and less."], [934.9, "As my needs got But less and less, I felt more and more free."], [942.3, "I felt more and more powerful."], [945.9, "I felt more and more flexible, free, wonderful."], [956.9, "That was the key."], [959.4, "That was the key."], [961.1, "I realized I didn't need much."], [965.8, "I could survive with almost zero money and I could be very happy."], [972.6, "I was happy."], [973.2, "I had a very good time."], [975.2, "I worked only a little bit."], [977.0, "I got a small part-time job only working 15 hours a week but it was enough."], [984.0, "I had plenty of money because I was living so simply so I spent lots of time with my friends."], [992.0, "I went running."], [993.9, "I joined a gym and worked out so I my body was very healthy and strong."], [999.4, "I ate good food."], [1001.3, "I started to write."], [1004.1, "This is when I started to think about creating my podcast and my blog."], [1013.7, "And that started Effortless English, really; the very beginnings of Effortless English started then."], [1023.2, "I had so many good ideas; every day I would write and write and write, more and more ideas."], [1033.7, "I had more energy, I enjoyed my life more, less stress; everything became better."], [1041.4, "That's why simplicity is so important it frees your mind it frees your emotions it gives you the time and the freedom necessary to grow."], [1063.4, "To be yourself again."], [1068.0, "Now eventually, you know, I had the idea for effortless English."], [1075.3, "Eventually I realized I don't need more but more would be nice as long as I'm not attached to it, right?"], [1085.4, "I didn't crave more this time, but I thought, well, it would be nice to have more."], [1091.7, "And also, I thought, I really want to help people learn English."], [1097.2, "So I started Effortless English."], [1100.8, "This time, I was very successful."], [1104.5, "What was the difference?"], [1105.8, "Why was I successful with effortless English, not successful with the vitamin health company."], [1116.0, "Well, number one, with the vitamin health company, I focused on more, more, more, money, money, money, money."], [1124.0, "I focused on money."], [1126.0, "I focused on not having enough."], [1128.0, "With effortless English, I had enough already."], [1131.5, "I had a very small apartment in San Francisco."], [1135.8, "I had a part-time job."], [1138.1, "I enjoyed my life."], [1139.5, "I didn't need more."], [1142.0, "I didn't crave more."], [1146.8, "So I didn't focus on money with effortless English."], [1151.5, "And that's the number two difference."], [1154.5, "Passion."], [1156.4, "Excitement."], [1158.8, "I am passionate about teaching English."], [1162.4, "I love teaching English."], [1164.5, "I don't care about the money."], [1167.6, "I will teach English for zero money."], [1172.1, "I will teach English even for very, very little money with a cheap, cheap job."], [1178.9, "In fact, I did do it."], [1181.1, "And I still loved it."], [1183.7, "So with effortless English, I did not focus on only money."], [1189.7, "No, I focused on having fun."], [1192.2, "I focused on being excited."], [1195.0, "I focused on helping students learn English better."], [1201.6, "That's a big difference."], [1204.0, "I didn't need to worry about more, more, more money."], [1209.3, "Of course, I wanted the business to grow, yes."], [1212.3, "Of course, I'm happy that the business became very successful, but I didn't need it and that's key I didn't need it because I learned simplicity so."], [1230.0, "This is the end of the commentary the important point is that simplicity will free your mind the funny thing the strange thing is if you live simply."], [1247.0, "Eventually you will get much more."], [1251.6, "If you worry about money, money, money, if you focus on money, money, money all the time, more, more, more, more."], [1258.4, "You actually will get less."], [1261.8, "Eventually you get less."], [1263.8, "You get more if you focus on simplicity."], [1268.3, "You get more if you focus on freedom."], [1271.8, "You get more if you focus on helping people."], [1278.2, "You get more if you focus on what you love to do."], [1286.1, "Simplicity gives you the freedom to do that."], [1292.5, "Simplicity gives you the freedom, the financial freedom, the emotional freedom, the mental freedom."], [1301.4, "It gives you the time to do what you love."], [1308.1, "To relax about money."], [1311.4, "To focus on helping people."], [1314.1, "That's why simplicity is so, so important."], [1318.2, "That's why simplicity is your first step for success."], [1325.9, "For success in your career or for success with your own business."], [1334.6, "So good luck and please focus on simplifying your life."], [1339.8, "Make it more simple."], [1340.9, "You don't need so much."], [1343.2, "You really don't."], [1344.9, "What we need is love and understanding and connection."], [1350.1, "We need to feel excited."], [1351.6, "We need to feel passionate."], [1353.2, "We need to enjoy our lives."], [1357.2, "We need all of those things."], [1360.0, "But we don't need goods so much."], [1364.0, "You know, we need a safe place to sleep."], [1366.4, "We need healthy food and water."], [1369.3, "We need clothes that are clean to keep us warm and healthy."], [1374.2, "That's all we really need."], [1377.2, "Right?"], [1377.9, "More than that, all the gadgets: they're not necessary; they're fun, they're nice, but they're not necessary."], [1378.8, "Okay, so good luck; I hope you can simplify your life as a first step."], [1379.6, "And don't worry, we will talk more about how to grow a business, and how to grow your career, in the future."], [1380.8, "But first, please focus on simplicity."], [1381.1, "All right, great; I'm wishing you a very happy and successful life."], [1381.7, "Take care, bye-bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["materialist", "/məˈtɪəriəlɪst/", "người duy vật, người trọng vật chất"], ["goods", "/ɡʊdz/", "hàng hóa, của cải"], ["liberation", "/ˌlɪbəˈreɪʃn/", "sự giải thoát, sự giải phóng"], ["the middle way", "/ðə ˈmɪdl weɪ/", "con đường trung đạo"], ["antagonistic to", "/ænˌtæɡəˈnɪstɪk tə/", "đối nghịch với"], ["well-being", "/ˌwel ˈbiːɪŋ/", "sự an lạc, sức khỏe và hạnh phúc"], ["stand in the way of", "/stænd ɪn ðə weɪ əv/", "cản trở"], ["attachment to", "/əˈtætʃmənt tə/", "sự bám víu, gắn bó với"], ["craving", "/ˈkreɪvɪŋ/", "sự thèm khát"], ["simplicity", "/sɪmˈplɪsəti/", "sự giản dị"], ["non-violence", "/ˌnɒn ˈvaɪələns/", "bất bạo động"], ["standard of living", "/ˈstændəd əv ˈlɪvɪŋ/", "mức sống"], ["annual consumption", "/ˈænjuəl kənˈsʌmpʃn/", "lượng tiêu dùng hằng năm"], ["better off", "/ˈbetər ɒf/", "khá giả hơn, ở tình thế tốt hơn"], ["excessively", "/ɪkˈsesɪvli/", "quá mức"], ["irrational", "/ɪˈræʃənl/", "phi lý"], ["merely", "/ˈmɪəli/", "chỉ đơn thuần"], ["a means to", "/ə miːnz tə/", "phương tiện để"], ["toil", "/tɔɪl/", "sự lao lực, công việc vất vả"], ["recipe for success", "/ˈresəpi fə səkˈses/", "công thức thành công"], ["assumption", "/əˈsʌmpʃn/", "giả định"], ["underlying", "/ˌʌndəˈlaɪɪŋ/", "ẩn bên dưới, cơ bản"], ["mainstream", "/ˈmeɪnstriːm/", "chính thống, đại trà"], ["essentially", "/ɪˈsenʃəli/", "về cơ bản"], ["ultimately", "/ˈʌltɪmətli/", "sau cùng, rốt cuộc"], ["qualified to", "/ˈkwɒlɪfaɪd tə/", "đủ tư cách, đủ năng lực để"], ["profound", "/prəˈfaʊnd/", "sâu sắc"], ["gadget", "/ˈɡædʒɪt/", "đồ công nghệ, thiết bị nhỏ"], ["debt elimination", "/det ɪˌlɪmɪˈneɪʃn/", "việc xóa nợ, trả hết nợ"], ["persistently", "/pəˈsɪstəntli/", "một cách bền bỉ"], ["relentlessly", "/rɪˈlentləsli/", "không ngừng nghỉ"], ["pare away", "/peər əˈweɪ/", "gọt bỏ, cắt giảm"], ["drastically", "/ˈdræstɪkli/", "một cách triệt để"], ["put off", "/pʊt ɒf/", "trì hoãn"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["is mainly interested in", "chủ yếu quan tâm đến"], ["is in no way antagonistic to", "hoàn toàn không đối nghịch với"], ["It is not wealth that stands in the way of liberation", "Không phải của cải cản trở sự giải thoát"], ["They are used to measuring ...", "Họ quen đo ..."], ["is better off than", "sung túc hơn"], ["the maximum of well-being with the minimum of consumption", "an lạc tối đa với tiêu dùng tối thiểu"], ["my recipe for economic success", "công thức thành công kinh tế của tôi"], ["are filled with books about making money", "đầy sách về kiếm tiền"], ["the key to success is to be rich", "chìa khóa thành công là giàu có"], ["I'm only qualified to give advice about", "tôi chỉ đủ tư cách khuyên về"], ["the profound difference between", "sự khác biệt sâu sắc giữa"], ["Learn to need less", "Hãy học cách cần ít hơn"], ["or better yet", "hay tốt hơn nữa là"], ["no matter how much money you have", "dù bạn có bao nhiêu tiền"], ["remain a slave to work", "mãi là nô lệ của công việc"], ["the things you always put off doing", "những việc bạn cứ trì hoãn mãi"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["While + S + V, S + V", "While my brother loves cities, I prefer the countryside.", "Trong khi anh tôi thích thành phố, tôi lại thích nông thôn.", "While"], ["It is not A that + V, but B", "It is not money that makes you happy, but the people around you.", "Không phải tiền làm bạn hạnh phúc, mà là những người quanh bạn.", "It is not"], ["S + is/are used to + V-ing", "I'm used to getting up at 5 a.m.", "Tôi quen dậy lúc 5 giờ sáng.", "used to"], ["The + comparative ..., the + comparative ...", "The less you spend, the more you can save.", "Càng tiêu ít, bạn càng tiết kiệm được nhiều.", "The less"], ["Even + noun + that + S + V, ...", "Even shops that I like are too expensive now.", "Ngay cả những cửa hàng tôi thích giờ cũng quá đắt.", "Even"], ["Learn to need + less/fewer + noun", "Learn to need fewer things, and you'll feel freer.", "Hãy học cách cần ít thứ hơn, bạn sẽ thấy tự do hơn.", "Learn to need"], ["Before you + V, + imperative", "Before you buy a new phone, ask yourself if you really need it.", "Trước khi mua điện thoại mới, hãy tự hỏi bạn có thật sự cần không.", "Before you"], ["..., no matter how + adj/much + S + V", "You'll feel tired, no matter how much coffee you drink.", "Bạn vẫn sẽ mệt, dù uống bao nhiêu cà phê.", "no matter how"], ["You'll find that + clause", "You'll find that English gets easier every day.", "Bạn sẽ thấy tiếng Anh dễ hơn mỗi ngày.", "You'll find"]]$j$::jsonb
