s a good investment."], [1158.5, "q", "Who made a good investment?"], [1165.4, "a", "Wilson."], [1165.8, "s", "Wilson made a good investment."], [1170.0, "q", "Did he make a bad investment with the flower farm or a good investment?"], [1177.8, "a", "Well, with the flower farm, he made a good investment."], [1186.6, "q", "Did he make a good investment with the stock market?"], [1192.4, "a", "No, no."], [1193.5, "s", "The stock market was a bad investment."], [1198.4, "q", "Why was the stock market a bad investment?"], [1206.0, "a", "Because he lost money."], [1209.2, "s", "Wilson lost money in the stock market."], [1212.1, "s", "So, it was a bad investment."], [1216.6, "q", "What was a good investment?"], [1220.1, "a", "Flower farm."], [1221.1, "s", "The flower farm was a good investment."], [1224.4, "q", "What was a bad investment?"], [1227.7, "a", "Well, stocks and gold."], [1231.1, "s", "He lost money with stocks."], [1233.8, "s", "He lost money with gold."], [1236.3, "s", "They were bad investments."], [1239.2, "s", "The flower farm was a good investment."], [1245.1, "s", "In fact, soon, King Wilson is rich."], [1251.5, "s", "The kingdom has great cash flow."], [1255.7, "q", "Ah, what has great cash flow?"], [1260.1, "a", "The kingdom."], [1261.7, "s", "The kingdom of monkeys has great cash flow."], [1265.4, "q", "Does Wilson the King have great cash flow?"], [1271.0, "a", "Oh yes, yes he does."], [1274.0, "s", "Wilson has great cash flow."], [1277.2, "s", "Is he spending more?"], [1280.8, "q", "Or is he making more every month?"], [1288.2, "a", "Making."], [1289.0, "s", "He's making more money every month."], [1292.7, "s", "He has great cash flow."], [1296.8, "q", "Who has great cash flow Wilson has great cash flow?"], [1307.8, "a", "Every monkey is very happy in fact all the monkeys are ecstatic are the monkeys sad."], [1321.6, "s", "No the monkeys aren't sad they are ecstatic are they a little happy."], [1333.2, "s", "No not a little happy they are ecstatic are the monkeys super happy yes."], [1348.0, "s", "The monkeys are ecstatic, woohoo!"], [1352.9, "q", "Why are the monkeys ecstatic?"], [1359.2, "a", "Because the kingdom is rich."], [1363.6, "s", "Because the kingdom has great cash flow."], [1370.5, "q", "Is Wilson ecstatic?"], [1373.9, "a", "Yes, of course."], [1375.9, "s", "Wilson is ecstatic."], [1379.1, "q", "Does Wilson have positive cash flow?"], [1383.4, "a", "Yes now he has positive cash flow does Bill Gates have positive cash flow."], [1395.7, "s", "Yes Bill Gates has positive cash flow he's the richest man in the world he has very positive cash flow who."], [1410.4, "q", "Has more positive cash flow Bill Gates or Wilson?"], [1418.6, "a", "Well Bill Gates of course Bill Gates is the richest man in the world Bill Gates has more positive cash flow than Wilson."], [1432.9, "s", "Okay, that is the end of the mini-story."], [1438.2, "s", "Every day, listen to this story one time, two times, maybe three times."], [1446.9, "s", "Listen to this story every day for one week, maybe two weeks."], [1454.9, "s", "If it's easy, that's okay; in fact, that's good."], [1460.8, "s", "You want to learn very deeply, so you need to repeat a lot."], [1469.5, "s", "Even when it's easy, especially when it's easy."], [1473.7, "s", "Okay?"], [1474.2, "s", "You have to let the words, let the phrases, let the grammar go deep, deep in your brain."], [1483.6, "s", "Then you will speak automatically."], [1486.5, "s", "Then you will speak quickly and easily, okay?"], [1490.8, "s", "So listen to all of these lessons."], [1493.8, "s", "What is success?"], [1494.7, "s", "Yes, listen to all of them every day for one week, maybe two weeks."], [1500.2, "s", "Alright, after this, listen to the point of view mini stories."]]}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.4, "Welcome to the Point of View mini-stories for What is Success?"], [8.3, "Let's start first with the past."], [13.7, "Two hundred years ago, there was a king."], [20.2, "His name was King Wilson."], [23.6, "Wilson, king of the monkeys."], [27.0, "Wilson had a problem."], [31.4, "He had negative cash flow."], [35.0, "His kingdom was losing money every month."], [39.8, "He couldn't afford to buy extra food for the monkeys in his kingdom."], [45.4, "He paid bills with most of his money."], [48.9, "He had to pay for the monkey army, for example."], [54.4, "Some monkeys were very angry."], [58.3, "They wanted to kill Wilson."], [62.6, "But the angry monkeys were a small group."], [67.2, "Most mainstream monkeys supported Wilson."], [72.8, "But still, King Wilson was worried."], [77.0, "He had to make more money."], [79.2, "He tried to invest in the stock market, but he lost money."], [86.3, "He tried to invest in gold, but he lost money."], [92.2, "Finally, he invested in a flower farm."], [97.1, "He grew big yellow flowers and exported them to Europe."], [102.9, "He made money, so he invested more money in the big, yellow flower farm."], [112.9, "It grew and made more and more money."], [117.1, "Soon, King Wilson was rich."], [121.6, "The kingdom had great cash flow."], [126.0, "Every monkey was very happy."], [128.1, "In fact, all of the monkeys were ecstatic."], [136.6, "Okay, next, starting with since 2005, since the year 2005."], [147.0, "Wilson has been king of the monkeys since 2005 and since 2005 he has had a problem he has had negative cash flow."], [170.0, "His kingdom has been losing money every month since 2005."], [175.8, "He hasn't been able to afford to buy extra food for the monkeys in his kingdom."], [184.9, "He has had to pay bills with most of his money; for example, he has had to pay for the monkey army."], [197.6, "Some monkeys have been very angry they have wanted to kill Wilson."], [207.0, "But the angry monkeys have been a small group."], [212.3, "Most mainstream monkeys have supported Wilson all this time since 2005."], [221.5, "Still, King Wilson has been worried."], [225.8, "He has known that he must make more money."], [230.3, "Finally, one day, he tried to invest in the stock market, but he lost money."], [239.1, "He tried to invest in gold, but he lost money."], [244.2, "Finally, he invested in a flower farm."], [247.8, "He grew big yellow flowers and exported them to Europe."], [253.2, "He made money."], [255.1, "So he invested more money in the yellow flower farm."], [258.7, "It grew and made more and more money."], [263.5, "Soon, King Wilson was rich."], [270.1, "The kingdom had great cash flow."], [274.9, "Every monkey was very happy."], [278.2, "In fact, all the monkeys were ecstatic."], [285.4, "Okay, finally, the future."], [288.5, "The future."], [289.0, "Imagine this story in the future; maybe next year."], [295.9, "Next year, there will be a new king of the monkeys; Wilson will be king of the monkeys."], [309.6, "But he's gonna have a problem: he's gonna have negative cash flow."], [318.8, "His kingdom is going to lose money every month."], [324.6, "He won't be able to afford to buy extra food for the monkeys in his kingdom."], [332.9, "He won't be able to pay bills, only the army."], [342.0, "Some monkeys are going to be very angry."], [347.1, "They'll want to kill Wilson."], [351.4, "But the angry monkeys will be a small group."], [355.9, "Most mainstream monkeys will support Wilson."], [362.1, "But King Wilson will be worried."], [367.9, "He'll have to make more money."], [370.7, "So he'll try to invest in the stock market."], [373.7, "It, but he'll lose money."], [377.6, "He'll try to invest in gold, but he'll lose money."], [383.8, "Finally, he'll invest in a flower farm."], [388.1, "He'll grow big yellow flowers and he'll export them to Europe."], [394.0, "He's gonna make money, so he'll invest more money in the yellow flower farm."], [401.6, "It'll grow and make more money, and more money, and more money."], [406.3, "Soon, King Wilson is gonna be rich."], [410.8, "The kingdom will have great cash flow."], [416.3, "Every monkey will be very happy."], [419.7, "In fact, all the monkeys will be ecstatic."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.8, "Hi, this is A.J. hogue and this is the commentary for what is success."], [10.7, "I want to talk a little bit about this question."], [14.1, "What is success?"], [17.9, "Now that's a big question and there are many, many different answers."], [23.0, "So let's talk only about financial success."], [28.3, "Okay, because success can have many different parts, right? Emotion means, you know, our feelings."], [34.8, "To be successful, I think you need to be happy most of the time; if you're very unhappy, in my opinion, you're not successful."], [45.3, "But anyway, those are more difficult questions to answer, about the total idea of success."], [51.8, "So let's talk only about money."], [54.4, "Financial success."], [55.6, "Let's keep this simple."], [58.9, "What is financial success?"], [63.5, "In this article we talk about the idea of cash flow and the idea of financial freedom."], [81.1, "Financial Many people do understand these ideas, but many people don't."], [86.8, "Or they understand them, but they don't take action."], [91.9, "And you know, action is the important part."], [94.1, "You have to, number one, you have to know what to do, right?"], [99.4, "You need knowledge."], [100.9, "You need information."], [102.6, "But number two, you have to do what you know."], [106.7, "It means you have the information, you know, but that's not enough."], [113.3, "You need action, and you need action every day, not just one time."], [120.2, "So this idea of financial freedom, of financial success."], [125.7, "Most people, I think, imagine that more money, more money, more money means financial success."], [135.4, "If you have a big expensive house."], [138.6, "If you have a big expensive car."], [141.3, "If you make a lot of money from your job or your business."], [146.8, "Most people think, well, that is financial success."], [152.2, "I don't."], [153.8, "I don't."], [154.5, "I think that can be financial success."], [158.0, "It depends on other things."], [161.7, "But I don't really think that's the key."], [166.1, "I think that cash flow, freedom, and control equal financial success."], [176.3, "Cash flow means you have more money coming in every month than you spend, right?"], [184.0, "You make more than you spend."], [186.8, "The bigger that gap."], [189.5, "The bigger the amount coming in, and the smaller the amount leaving."], [195.6, "Means more and more financial success."], [201.7, "And why is that?"], [202.6, "It's because you have more freedom, more flexibility."], [207.0, "And that's the next part."], [208.8, "It means you have choices."], [210.6, "You have financial choices."], [212.2, "Cases."], [213.2, "It means you don't need to worry about emergencies."], [216.6, "If you get sick, no problem."], [219.1, "You have big cash flow, you have big positive cash flow, you have a lot of money saved."], [226.1, "If you have an emergency, no stress, no worry."], [232.3, "If your cash flow is negative, or just even, right, the same coming in, the same going out, then an emergency is a big problem."], [242.5, "It's very stressful, even if you're rich, even if a lot of money is coming in."], [249.1, "If the same amount is leaving every month, and suddenly you have a big bill,"], [255.2, "unexpected, a surprise bill, that's gonna be a big stress."], [260.8, "Another situation: if you have negative cash flow, it means you're borrowing money, right?"], [268.7, "Maybe you're using credit cards, or maybe you're using a loan from the bank."], [276.6, "But anyway, if you're spending more than you're making, and suddenly your income goes down,"], [285.1, "maybe you lose your job, maybe your business goes down a little bit, if your cash flow is even or negative,"], [296.9, "You're going to be super stressed."], [299.0, "You're going to be worried."], [301.1, "You're going to have a big, big problem."], [304.4, "If you have very positive cash flow and you're saving a lot of money."], [312.1, "Then that situation is not so bad."], [315.6, "If you lose your job, it's not good, but you have time to find another job, right?"], [322.5, "You have a lot of savings, so you can relax a little bit: I'm okay, I have time to find a new job."], [331.7, "Or if your business goes down, again, it's not good, but you have time to find a new way to make money."], [340.6, "You can think, okay, I need to bring my business up again; you have time to find a solution,"], [348.3, "if you have positive cash flow every month, if you are saving money every month."], [354.3, "So that's very important."], [355.6, "And the last part for me of financial success is control."], [360.5, "It means you control your money."], [364.0, "Other people don't control it."], [367.1, "So if you have a lot of money saved, you have control."], [372.5, "You can quit your job if you're unhappy."], [376.8, "You can change your business if you're unhappy or you don't like it."], [381.2, "Right?"], [381.4, "Your decision."], [382.3, "You control that."], [384.6, "If you don't have positive cash flow."], [388.0, "If you don't have a lot of money saved every month."], [392.9, "Then someone else controls you."], [397.9, "You're afraid to lose your job."], [400.2, "You're afraid to quit."], [402.9, "And when you're afraid to quit, the boss can treat you very badly, right?"], [410.0, "You're afraid to lose your job."], [412.0, "So even if it's a very bad job, you'll keep doing it."], [417.4, "Not because you like it, because you have negative cash flow, because you must keep the job."], [424.5, "You need the money every month, every month, every month; you don't have enough saved so you could quit and find a better job, right?"], [435.3, "So you live in fear when your cash flow is low; when your cash flow is even or negative, you live in fear constantly."], [445.7, "You're always worried; you're always afraid something might happen."], [449.6, "You're afraid to lose your job, you're afraid your business will go down, you're afraid of some emergency, some surprise."], [458.2, "That's not control."], [459.6, "That means other things control you, other people control you."], [464.6, "Even if you're very rich, even if your house is expensive and your car is expensive and your clothes are expensive."], [472.4, "If your cash flow is low, negative."], [476.2, "If you owe money, you have big loans, you're borrowing money from the bank."], [481.5, "You're using credit cards."], [483.9, "You don't have control."], [486.2, "Other people may think you're rich, they may think you're successful, but really you're not."], [494.4, "So that's why this cash flow idea is so important."], [498.7, "So important."], [499.9, "It's simple, right?"], [501.7, "It's so simple."], [503.0, "I'm not telling you something new."], [506.4, "I'm not giving you some difficult information."], [509.6, "It's so simple."], [511.8, "And yet, so many people forget or ignore this very simple, very important idea."], [521.8, "Why?"], [523.0, "Well, you know, for one thing, we are taught to ignore it from TV."], [529.8, "From movies."], [531.2, "From advertising."], [533.2, "From our parents."], [535.8, "From our friends."], [537.8, "From our coworkers."], [541.0, "From our bosses."], [543.1, "Our jobs, from everywhere."], [545.2, "Where we are taught that more money equals success."], [553.4, "We're taught that a big house, an expensive car, expensive clothes equals success."], [563.3, "So what do we do?"], [564.8, "We borrow money to buy a more expensive car."], [569.2, "We borrow money to buy a big, big house."], [572.3, "We borrow money, with a credit card maybe, to buy very nice clothes, expensive looking clothes."], [581.7, "We're always borrowing money so that we look successful."], [587.8, "That's what TV tells us to do."], [589.7, "That's what everybody tells us to do."], [593.3, "But that is not success, and it really means stress in the future."], [602.7, "If you do that, you might feel successful in the beginning for a while."], [608.6, "But eventually, you're going to feel very, very stressed."], [613.5, "You will not feel free."], [615.3, "You will not feel in control."], [618.8, "You will not have flexibility."], [621.1, "You will not have a lot of choices."], [624.7, "So, we have to forget what our cultures tell us, and it's everywhere in the world now."], [633.1, "This is not just America, it's not just your country."], [635.7, "It's all over the world."], [637.0, "It's the same message, right?"], [639.1, "It means, look like you're rich."], [641.7, "That means success."], [644.2, "And we make bad choices because of that."], [647.7, "It's not just spending."], [649.9, "We also make bad choices about making money."], [653.5, "What do I mean by that?"], [655.1, "Well, it means we take jobs that we hate just because they pay more money."], [662.7, "Well, I think that's a terrible idea."], [665.2, "Why would you want to do something you hate every day just for more money?"], [671.4, "It's a bad choice, in my opinion; so, you know, we don't want to do that."], [679.1, "That's not financial success: 40, 50, 60 hours a week, you're doing something you hate, or something you think is boring,"], [689.3, "maybe working with people you don't like, just so you can have more money."], [696.0, "That's not success."], [697.5, "Going to be more stressed."], [699.2, "You're going to be unhappy."], [701.9, "You're not going to enjoy your life when you do that."], [705.3, "So just making more money is not the answer, okay?"], [712.2, "So we need to think instead about cash flow."], [715.6, "Cash flow is the important concept, the important idea for financial success, okay?"], [723.7, "Get this out of it."], [724.4, "Forget this idea that just make more money more and more and more and more and more Make more, spend more."], [730.0, "That's what we're taught."], [731.3, "Make more money, even at a bad job."], [734.0, "Spend more money, even if we have to borrow."], [737.9, "That's what most people are doing, trying to be successful."], [742.5, "Most people do not feel successful."], [745.2, "Most people feel stressed and worried all the time about money."], [749.9, "Most people don't feel free."], [751.5, "Most people don't feel like they control their finances."], [755.8, "So, this is a new way to think, and it's very important to look at the order, at the numbers there."], [762.8, "Right?"], [764.0, "It's very important that number one is reduce spending, right?"], [769.9, "I did not put make more money as number one."], [772.1, "That's number two."], [773.3, "Number one, the first step is reduce your spending."], [778.5, "That's tough."], [780.8, "Why is it tough?"], [781.7, "It's not actually tough to spend less money."], [787.3, "The tough part is changing your brain, changing your belief, changing your mind and your attitude."], [795.2, "The tough part is to resist, to forget all the messages from people, from other people."], [804.3, "That's the hard part."], [806.7, "You know, it's very easy to live simply, in fact, it's easier, it's less stressful."], [813.2, "The hard part is everybody's telling you, oh, get more, more, more."], [817.9, "But you're trying to do, to spend and get less, less, less."], [822.7, "You're going against the mainstream culture."], [826.0, "But you know, the mainstream culture is stressed and unhappy and not in control."], [832.1, "So, if you want to be happy and have a lot of money and be free."], [837.7, "You have to go against mainstream culture."], [841.5, "You begin by spending less."], [845.4, "Get a smaller apartment that costs less money."], [849.9, "Sell your house."], [851.1, "Buy a cheaper house, a smaller house."], [856.0, "Sell your car."], [857.3, "Get a cheaper car."], [859.0, "Or don't use a car at all."], [860.8, "Get a motorcycle."], [861.5, "Or take the bus or the subway it might feel inconvenient in the beginning but when your cash flow gets better and better every month you will feel stronger and happier."], [880.9, "So it's a very small thing to do to feel happier."], [887.4, "Okay so reduce that amount reduce the amount you spend on food stay at home more."], [894.7, "Cook more at home."], [897.4, "It's pretty easy actually."], [898.9, "There's a lot of different ways to spend less money."], [904.1, "I recommend you start with rent."], [906.7, "Rent is usually the biggest expense for most people."], [912.8, "It's usually the largest amount of money people spend on their home or apartment."], [918.2, "So that's the first place to reduce your spending."], [922.3, "And then cars, transportation, is usually maybe number two; that's also a very big one."], [929.0, "For some people, clothes, expensive clothes, is a major expense; it's a lot of money they spend."], [936.7, "You need to reduce that if you want to be financially successful and free, if you want to feel relaxed about your money, and happy."], [948.0, "If you want that, you must do this."], [951.4, "If you don't care about that, if you don't mind being stressed or if you're super rich."], [955.3, "You can ignore my advice."], [957.6, "But if you feel some stress about money, if you hate your job and you feel like it controls you."], [963.9, "If you're tired of working all the time."], [967.6, "Then this is the first step."], [970.2, "Reduce your spending every month; your goal is to spend less."], [976.2, "Spend less this month; next month, spend even less; the next month, even less; every month less than the previous month. That's your goal."], [989.2, "Do that for a year, maybe, and then part two: increase your income, make more money."], [997.9, "Now, that might mean getting another job that pays more."], [1003.3, "But only if you like that job."], [1005.6, "I never recommend getting a job you hate."], [1010.2, "It's never worth it, okay?"], [1012.4, "The extra money, it's never enough to replace your happiness."], [1019.1, "If you're feeling stressed, if you're feeling very unhappy, if your boss is an asshole, a jerk."], [1026.0, "Look, there's not enough money to compensate for that."], [1032.3, "There's not enough money to make you feel better about that."], [1036.4, "So don't get a terrible job."], [1038.7, "But if you can find a nice job that makes more money, that's great."], [1043.4, "Of course, go for it."], [1044.6, "Do it."], [1046.3, "If you can't, then find other ways to make more money."], [1052.2, "I think the best way is to start your own business."], [1057.9, "It really is the best way to make more money."], [1062.0, "It's scary for a lot of people because they do it wrong, because they borrow money."], [1067.7, "If you borrow money to start a business, you're going to probably fail."], [1073.5, "I think something like 90% of businesses fail."], [1079.1, "Why do they fail?"], [1080.2, "What's the number one reason new businesses fail?"], [1085.8, "You know, cash flow."], [1089.1, "Cash flow."], [1090.8, "There's a lot of research about this."], [1093.6, "You can read any business book about small business."], [1097.0, "You will find this same information."], [1099.7, "Cash flow is the reason most businesses fail."], [1104.9, "And most businesses, 90, I don't know, 95%."], [1108.5, "It's above 90, above 90 percent of new businesses fail within five years."], [1116.9, "That's terrible, right?"], [1118.9, "It's pretty scary."], [1120.5, "But why do they fail?"], [1122.2, "They fail because of negative cash flow."], [1127.2, "Why do they have negative cash flow?"], [1131.3, "Why are they spending more money than they make?"], [1136.4, "Well, number one, they borrow money in the beginning."], [1141.7, "I mean, it's crazy."], [1142.6, "I can't believe what some people do to start a business."], [1146.8, "They borrow $100,000, for example, to start their business."], [1152.8, "Oh my God."], [1153.4, "Well, of course, that's a lot of stress."], [1156.5, "You're already negative $100,000 on the first day."], [1162.2, "It's going to be very difficult to get positive cash flow if you borrow money."], [1170.5, "So, number one, my advice, start a small business."], [1174.9, "Do not borrow money."], [1178.7, "So, that means start something very, very, very, very small."], [1183.1, "I started Effortless English with $200."], [1188.2, "I did not borrow $200."], [1190.2, "I saved $200 from my job, then I started Effortless English."], [1198.6, "The first website was ugly and cheap because I did not borrow money."], [1207.7, "I did not create a big, expensive, nice website because I did not want to borrow money."], [1218.3, "I did not want negative cash flow."], [1220.3, "Instead, I started a tiny, super cheap website and did not borrow money."], [1230.3, "So on the first day of Effortless English."], [1234.0, "I had positive cash flow because the first month actually, on the first month of Effortless English, I made more money than I spent."], [1243.6, "I spent $200; I think I made $225, so in total, my first month, I made $25."], [1253.2, "Okay, that's not much, but it's positive cash flow; it's not negative."], [1260.0, "Most businesses have negative cash flow the first month, actually the first year, and as we see, actually, most of them fail."], [1272.4, "So if you want to start a business."], [1274.3, "Do not start a business that requires you to borrow money."], [1282.0, "Maybe you have a fantastic idea for a super website or a great restaurant or something."], [1290.5, "That's fine, but if you need to borrow money, forget it."], [1294.6, "Do it later."], [1295.3, "Do it later after you have a lot of money from another business, a cheaper business to start."], [1302.5, "So, start a super cheap business first without borrowing money."], [1307.9, "Build it very slowly, a little bit, you know, I made $25 my first month, that's all."], [1313.8, "That's okay."], [1315.4, "You can do the same thing."], [1316.7, "I was still working, I had my job."], [1319.0, "I was doing my business part time."], [1321.1, "You can do that also."], [1322.4, "Start a cheap business, and then build it slowly, slowly, every month, a little better, a little better."], [1331.0, "Always focusing on cash flow, positive cash flow, positive cash flow."], [1336.0, "Never spend more than you make."], [1340.1, "Your business will eventually grow, I promise you."], [1345.2, "As long as you have positive cash flow."], [1348.3, "And you keep trying new things, you keep trying, you keep learning, you will succeed."], [1355.7, "I guarantee you can't fail; you cannot fail if you have positive cash flow and you continue to learn."], [1365.0, "Maybe you might need five months, maybe you need five years, maybe you need 12 years,"], [1372.9, "but you won't fail if you have positive cash flow and you are always learning."], [1380.3, "That's the two key things for a successful business, small business."], [1387.1, "Now maybe your business will grow and grow and grow and then you have a lot of cash flow and you have a lot of money saved."], [1395.0, "Then you can try your big idea, your big expensive website, your big expensive restaurant."], [1402.0, "No problem, you don't need to borrow money, it's okay."], [1405.4, "Right?"], [1405.6, "But don't do it first."], [1407.4, "Don't start with the big expensive business."], [1410.1, "Start with something tiny, small, part-time, without borrowing money."], [1417.5, "That's the key to a successful business."], [1420.9, "Okay, well that's all."], [1423.0, "That's the discussion, the commentary for what is financial success."], [1431.0, "I hope you enjoyed this."], [1432.4, "I hope you follow this advice."], [1434.5, "I want you to feel relaxed."], [1438.1, "I want you to feel happy about money."], [1441.0, "I want you to feel ecstatic about money."], [1444.3, "I want you to feel free."], [1446.7, "I want you to feel in control of your money."], [1451.6, "I want you to start your own little business and then grow it."], [1457.4, "I want it to be successful."], [1459.2, "I want you to be financially successful."], [1462.4, "Follow this advice and I promise you will be."], [1468.0, "Okay, take care, good luck, see you next time."], [1472.2, "Bye-bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["define", "/dɪˈfaɪn/", "định nghĩa"], ["equal", "/ˈiːkwəl/", "bằng, đồng nghĩa với"], ["shallow", "/ˈʃæləʊ/", "nông cạn"], ["miserable", "/ˈmɪzrəbl/", "khổ sở"], ["broaden", "/ˈbrɔːdn/", "mở rộng"], ["in terms of", "/ɪn tɜːmz əv/", "xét về, theo"], ["connection", "/kəˈnekʃn/", "sự kết nối"], ["ecstasy", "/ˈekstəsi/", "sự ngây ngất, hạnh phúc tột độ"], ["obviously", "/ˈɒbviəsli/", "rõ ràng"], ["commit suicide", "/kəˈmɪt ˈsuːɪsaɪd/", "tự tử"], ["vital", "/ˈvaɪtl/", "thiết yếu"], ["compassion", "/kəmˈpæʃn/", "lòng trắc ẩn"], ["ingredient", "/ɪnˈɡriːdiənt/", "thành phần"], ["financially free", "/faɪˈnænʃəli friː/", "tự do tài chính"], ["cash flow", "/ˈkæʃ fləʊ/", "dòng tiền"], ["finances", "/ˈfaɪnænsɪz/", "tài chính (cá nhân)"], ["appear", "/əˈpɪə(r)/", "có vẻ, trông như"], ["owe", "/əʊ/", "nợ"], ["loan", "/ləʊn/", "khoản vay"], ["credit card debt", "/ˈkredɪt kɑːd det/", "nợ thẻ tín dụng"], ["bill", "/bɪl/", "hóa đơn"], ["income", "/ˈɪnkʌm/", "thu nhập"], ["option", "/ˈɒpʃn/", "lựa chọn"], ["invest in", "/ɪnˈvest ɪn/", "đầu tư vào"], ["opportunity", "/ˌɒpəˈtjuːnəti/", "cơ hội"], ["positive gap", "/ˈpɒzətɪv ɡæp/", "khoảng chênh dương (thu > chi)"], ["drastically reduce", "/ˈdræstɪkli rɪˈdjuːs/", "cắt giảm mạnh"], ["advantage", "/ədˈvɑːntɪdʒ/", "lợi thế"], ["flexibility", "/ˌfleksəˈbɪləti/", "sự linh hoạt"], ["rent", "/rent/", "tiền thuê nhà"], ["afford", "/əˈfɔːd/", "có đủ tiền chi trả"], ["maximize", "/ˈmæksɪmaɪz/", "tối đa hóa"], ["reinvest", "/ˌriːɪnˈvest/", "tái đầu tư"], ["accomplish", "/əˈkʌmplɪʃ/", "hoàn thành, đạt được"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["we must first be able to define success", "trước hết ta phải định nghĩa được thành công"], ["success equals money", "thành công đồng nghĩa với tiền"], ["a very shallow idea of success", "một quan niệm rất nông cạn về thành công"], ["broaden our idea of success", "mở rộng quan niệm về thành công"], ["I define success in terms of ...", "Tôi định nghĩa thành công qua ..."], ["nothing else matters", "mọi thứ khác đều vô nghĩa"], ["Obviously not", "Rõ ràng là không"], ["feel connected to other people", "cảm thấy gắn kết với người khác"], ["have total control over your finances", "hoàn toàn làm chủ tài chính"], ["owe more money than they actually have", "nợ nhiều hơn số họ thực sự có"], ["On the outside, they appear rich", "Bề ngoài họ có vẻ giàu"], ["more money coming in than is going out", "tiền vào nhiều hơn tiền ra"], ["you make more than you spend every month", "mỗi tháng bạn kiếm nhiều hơn số bạn tiêu"], ["I could afford something much more expensive", "tôi có thể chi trả cho thứ đắt hơn nhiều"], ["until you accomplish this first", "cho đến khi bạn làm được điều này trước đã"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["If we want to + V, we must first + V", "If we want to save money, we must first track our spending.", "Muốn tiết kiệm, trước hết ta phải theo dõi chi tiêu.", "must first"], ["S + define(s) + noun + in terms of + A, B and C", "I define a good job in terms of time, money and people.", "Tôi định nghĩa một công việc tốt qua thời gian, tiền bạc và con người.", "in terms of"], ["Without + noun, nothing else matters", "Without health, nothing else matters.", "Không có sức khỏe thì mọi thứ khác đều vô nghĩa.", "Without"], ["S + owe(s) more + than + S + have", "They owe more than they earn in a year.", "Họ nợ nhiều hơn số họ kiếm được trong một năm.", "owe"], ["On the outside, S + appear(s) + adj, but ...", "On the outside, he appears calm, but he is very nervous.", "Bề ngoài anh ấy có vẻ bình tĩnh, nhưng thực ra rất lo lắng.", "On the outside"], ["The bigger ..., the greater ...", "The bigger your savings, the greater your freedom.", "Tiền tiết kiệm càng lớn, bạn càng tự do.", "The bigger"], ["Even though + S + V, S + V + even + comparative", "Even though I earned little, I spent even less.", "Dù kiếm được ít, tôi còn tiêu ít hơn.", "Even though"], ["Do not + V + until + S + V", "Do not buy a car until you have saved enough.", "Đừng mua xe cho đến khi bạn tiết kiệm đủ.", "until"]]$j$::jsonb
)
