-- ── Business English · Bài 4: Stand Out (chữ từ audio bằng Whisper, đã soát) ──
insert into public.effortless_lessons (course, lesson_no, slug, title, level, description, cover, main_audio, vocab_audio, ms_audio, pov_audio, com_audio, main_story, mini_story, ms_parts, pov_story, com_story, vocab, phrases, patterns)
values (
  'Business English',
  4,
  'stand-out',
  'Stand Out',
  'advanced',
  'Muốn thành công lớn, bạn phải nổi bật — dù điều đó đồng nghĩa với bị chỉ trích. A.J. kể chuyện dám khác biệt với Effortless English. Học cách nói về rủi ro, điểm mạnh, sự khác biệt và nỗi sợ thất bại — kèm POV và lời bình.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1713001075225-8c490e800e29',
  'Bussiness English/304a Stand Out (main).mp3',
  'Bussiness English/304b Stand Out (vocabulary).mp3',
  'Bussiness English/304c Stand Out (ms).mp3',
  'Bussiness English/304d Stand Out (pov).mp3',
  'Bussiness English/304e Stand Out (com).mp3',
  $j$[[1.4, "Stand Out!", "Hãy nổi bật!"], [4.8, "\"If you're remarkable, it's likely that some people won't like you.", "\"Nếu bạn xuất chúng, nhiều khả năng sẽ có người không thích bạn."], [9.7, "That's part of the definition of being remarkable.", "Đó là một phần định nghĩa của sự xuất chúng."], [14.1, "Nobody gets unanimous praise, ever.", "Không ai được khen ngợi tuyệt đối, chưa bao giờ."], [18.1, "The best the timid can hope for is to be unnoticed.", "Điều tốt nhất người nhút nhát có thể mong là không bị ai để ý."], [22.7, "Criticism comes to those who stand out.", "Sự chỉ trích đến với những ai nổi bật."], [26.5, "Where did you learn how to fail?", "Bạn học cách thất bại ở đâu?"], [30.1, "If you're like most people, you learned in first grade.", "Nếu bạn giống hầu hết mọi người, bạn đã học từ lớp một."], [33.6, "That's when you started figuring out that the safe thing to do was to fit in.", "Đó là lúc bạn bắt đầu nhận ra điều an toàn là hòa vào đám đông."], [39.7, "The safe thing to do was to color inside the lines; don't ask too many questions in class, etc.", "Điều an toàn là tô màu trong đường kẻ; đừng hỏi quá nhiều trong lớp, vân vân."], [49.2, "Playing it safe. Following the rules.", "Chơi an toàn. Tuân theo luật lệ."], [53.4, "Those seem like the best ways to avoid failure, and in school they may very well be.", "Đó có vẻ là cách tốt nhất để tránh thất bại, và ở trường có khi đúng là như vậy."], [61.7, "However, these rules set a pattern for most people, like your boss, and that pattern is awfully dangerous.", "Tuy nhiên, những luật lệ này tạo thành khuôn mẫu cho hầu hết mọi người, như sếp của bạn, và khuôn mẫu đó cực kỳ nguy hiểm."], [71.5, "These are the rules that ultimately lead to failure.", "Đây chính là những luật lệ rốt cuộc dẫn đến thất bại."], [83.6, "In a crowded marketplace, not standing out is the same as being invisible.", "Trong một thị trường đông đúc, không nổi bật cũng giống như vô hình."], [90.4, "The good news is that the prevailing wisdom makes your job even easier, since just about everyone else is petrified of being different.", "Tin tốt là quan niệm phổ biến còn khiến việc của bạn dễ hơn, vì hầu như ai cũng sợ chết khiếp chuyện khác người."], [103.1, "You can be remarkable with even less effort.", "Bạn có thể xuất chúng mà còn tốn ít công sức hơn."], [106.6, "If successful new products are the ones that stand out, and most people desire not to stand out, you're set!", "Nếu sản phẩm mới thành công là những sản phẩm nổi bật, và hầu hết mọi người lại muốn không nổi bật, thì bạn nắm chắc phần thắng!"], [119.2, "So it seems we face two choices: to be invisible, anonymous, uncriticized, and safe, or to take a chance at greatness, uniqueness, and big success.\" Seth Godin, marketing expert", "Vậy có vẻ ta đứng trước hai lựa chọn: vô hình, vô danh, không bị chỉ trích và an toàn, hoặc nắm lấy cơ hội để vĩ đại, độc đáo và thành công lớn.\" Seth Godin, chuyên gia marketing"], [148.3, "If you want to be a big success in your career, or if you want to create your own successful business, you must be remarkable.", "Nếu bạn muốn thành công lớn trong sự nghiệp, hay muốn xây dựng doanh nghiệp riêng thành công, bạn phải xuất chúng."], [158.1, "The problem is, being remarkable is scary.", "Vấn đề là, xuất chúng thì đáng sợ."], [162.4, "We are taught all our lives to be the same.", "Cả đời ta được dạy phải giống nhau."], [167.2, "We are taught to avoid criticism. We are taught to fit in.", "Ta được dạy phải tránh bị chỉ trích. Ta được dạy phải hòa nhập."], [171.6, "We learn to do what everyone else is doing.", "Ta học cách làm những gì người khác đang làm."], [175.4, "That does give us a little security.", "Điều đó đúng là cho ta chút an toàn."], [179.2, "We manage to keep a safe but boring job.", "Ta giữ được một công việc an toàn nhưng nhàm chán."], [183.4, "We make a little money. Maybe we get a small promotion.", "Ta kiếm được chút tiền. Có thể được thăng chức nho nhỏ."], [188.0, "But we never achieve our dreams.", "Nhưng ta không bao giờ đạt được ước mơ."], [191.4, "We never attain big success, total financial freedom, plenty of time to enjoy our lives, and feelings of happiness and ecstasy.", "Ta không bao giờ có được thành công lớn, tự do tài chính trọn vẹn, nhiều thời gian để tận hưởng cuộc sống, và cảm giác hạnh phúc ngây ngất."], [202.2, "Most people feel stuck in their jobs.", "Hầu hết mọi người thấy mắc kẹt trong công việc."], [205.2, "They want something more, but they are afraid to be different.", "Họ muốn điều gì đó hơn thế, nhưng lại sợ khác biệt."], [210.5, "Starting your own business is scary. I know.", "Tự khởi nghiệp thật đáng sợ. Tôi biết mà."], [214.4, "I was terrified when I started Effortless English.", "Tôi đã sợ khiếp vía khi bắt đầu Effortless English."], [218.6, "To be honest, I wasn't worried about money.", "Thành thật mà nói, tôi không lo về tiền."], [220.8, "What terrified me was humiliation.", "Điều làm tôi khiếp sợ là sự bẽ mặt."], [226.0, "I told everyone about the business.", "Tôi đã kể với mọi người về việc kinh doanh."], [228.8, "If it had failed, I would have felt embarrassed. I would have felt like a total idiot.", "Nếu nó thất bại, tôi hẳn đã thấy xấu hổ. Tôi hẳn đã thấy mình như một tên ngốc."], [238.5, "This fear is normal. Don't worry about it.", "Nỗi sợ này là bình thường. Đừng lo lắng về nó."], [241.9, "Unfortunately, many new business owners play it safe because they are afraid.", "Đáng tiếc, nhiều chủ doanh nghiệp mới chọn an toàn vì sợ."], [248.6, "They start a new business, but then they copy what everyone else is doing.", "Họ mở doanh nghiệp mới, nhưng rồi lại sao chép những gì người khác đang làm."], [254.7, "There's nothing remarkable about the business.", "Doanh nghiệp chẳng có gì nổi bật."], [258.3, "What happens? Usually the business fails.", "Chuyện gì xảy ra? Thường là doanh nghiệp thất bại."], [263.0, "Since the business isn't remarkably different, no one is interested in it.", "Vì doanh nghiệp không khác biệt nổi bật, chẳng ai quan tâm đến nó."], [269.0, "Over 90% of new businesses fail within 5 years.", "Hơn 90% doanh nghiệp mới thất bại trong vòng 5 năm."], [275.8, "That's a scary statistic.", "Đó là một con số thống kê đáng sợ."], [278.6, "How do you avoid being in that 90%?", "Làm sao để bạn không nằm trong 90% đó?"], [283.5, "Or maybe you just want to go higher in your career. How do you move up?", "Hoặc có thể bạn chỉ muốn tiến xa hơn trong sự nghiệp. Làm sao để thăng tiến?"], [289.5, "You do it by being remarkable.", "Bạn làm được điều đó bằng cách xuất chúng."], [292.0, "You must be different. You must be unique.", "Bạn phải khác biệt. Bạn phải độc đáo."], [295.3, "You must take risks and do things that no one else is doing.", "Bạn phải chấp nhận rủi ro và làm những điều chưa ai làm."], [301.8, "When you do this, people will criticize you.", "Khi bạn làm vậy, người ta sẽ chỉ trích bạn."], [305.2, "I was criticized by many English teachers when I started Effortless English.", "Tôi bị nhiều giáo viên tiếng Anh chỉ trích khi bắt đầu Effortless English."], [311.5, "They said I was crazy not to teach grammar rules.", "Họ nói tôi điên khi không dạy quy tắc ngữ pháp."], [315.3, "They said students wanted grammar rules and would never buy my lessons.", "Họ nói học viên muốn học quy tắc ngữ pháp và sẽ không bao giờ mua bài học của tôi."], [321.1, "Now, I have a successful, growing business, and they are still working bad jobs for little money.", "Giờ đây tôi có một doanh nghiệp thành công đang phát triển, còn họ vẫn làm những công việc tệ với đồng lương ít ỏi."], [330.8, "Why? Because I chose to be different and remarkable.", "Vì sao? Vì tôi chọn khác biệt và xuất chúng."], [336.2, "They chose to stay the same and play it safe.", "Họ chọn giữ nguyên và an toàn."], [341.5, "It's easy to be remarkable. Here's how you do it.", "Xuất chúng thì dễ thôi. Đây là cách làm."], [344.5, "Number one, identify your strong points.", "Thứ nhất, xác định điểm mạnh của bạn."], [348.6, "What are the strongest points of your personality and skills?", "Đâu là những điểm mạnh nhất trong tính cách và kỹ năng của bạn?"], [355.5, "Two, exaggerate those strong points. Make them super strong.", "Thứ hai, phóng đại những điểm mạnh đó. Làm chúng thật mạnh."], [362.2, "At the same time, ignore your weak points. Don't try to correct them.", "Đồng thời, hãy bỏ qua điểm yếu. Đừng cố sửa chúng."], [367.3, "Focus on making your strong points even stronger.", "Hãy tập trung làm cho điểm mạnh càng mạnh hơn."], [372.6, "Three, take risks where you are strong.", "Thứ ba, chấp nhận rủi ro ở những chỗ bạn mạnh."], [378.5, "Try new things. To succeed, you must be extreme.", "Thử điều mới. Muốn thành công, bạn phải đi đến tận cùng."], [385.7, "For example, the strongest point of Effortless English is listening and speaking fluency.", "Ví dụ, điểm mạnh nhất của Effortless English là sự trôi chảy khi nghe và nói."], [392.9, "Several years ago, I was good at helping students speak English easily and fast.", "Vài năm trước, tôi giỏi giúp học viên nói tiếng Anh dễ dàng và nhanh."], [400.0, "I also knew from research that grammar study did not help.", "Tôi cũng biết qua nghiên cứu rằng học ngữ pháp không giúp ích."], [405.9, "Every other school and teacher focuses on grammar study.", "Mọi trường và giáo viên khác đều tập trung vào học ngữ pháp."], [412.0, "I focused on my strengths.", "Tôi tập trung vào thế mạnh của mình."], [414.8, "I became better and better and better at teaching students to speak English easily and fast.", "Tôi ngày càng giỏi hơn trong việc dạy học viên nói tiếng Anh dễ dàng và nhanh."], [422.7, "I didn't focus on writing, although that is a legitimate area to study.", "Tôi không tập trung vào viết, dù đó cũng là một mảng đáng học."], [428.8, "I didn't do what everyone else does: teach useless grammar rules.", "Tôi không làm điều mọi người làm: dạy những quy tắc ngữ pháp vô ích."], [434.4, "I focused on my strengths.", "Tôi tập trung vào thế mạnh của mình."], [436.7, "Eventually, I created the best system in the world for learning to speak English easily and fast, with no grammar study.", "Cuối cùng, tôi tạo ra hệ thống tốt nhất thế giới để học nói tiếng Anh dễ dàng và nhanh, không cần học ngữ pháp."], [447.0, "It's remarkable. It's unique.", "Nó xuất sắc. Nó độc đáo."], [449.0, "It's totally different than any other system in the world.", "Nó hoàn toàn khác mọi hệ thống khác trên thế giới."], [453.2, "That's why Effortless English succeeded.", "Đó là lý do Effortless English thành công."], [457.0, "Use the same strategy with your career or business.", "Hãy dùng chiến lược tương tự cho sự nghiệp hay doanh nghiệp của bạn."], [462.1, "Do not copy others.", "Đừng sao chép người khác."], [464.0, "In fact, strive to be different than everyone else.", "Thực ra, hãy nỗ lực để khác biệt với mọi người."], [469.6, "Pick a few things and be remarkable at those things.", "Chọn vài thứ và trở nên xuất chúng ở những thứ đó."], [474.1, "Stand out!", "Hãy nổi bật!"], [476.0, "People will criticize you, it's true.", "Người ta sẽ chỉ trích bạn, đúng vậy."], [478.9, "But in the end, you will live your dreams, and they will forever be disappointed.", "Nhưng cuối cùng, bạn sẽ sống với ước mơ của mình, còn họ sẽ mãi thất vọng."], [487.8, "Follow Seth Godin's advice. Take a chance at greatness, uniqueness and big success.", "Hãy làm theo lời khuyên của Seth Godin. Nắm lấy cơ hội để vĩ đại, độc đáo và thành công lớn."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[[0.4, "s", "Welcome to the mini-story for Stand Out."], [5.6, "s", "Let's start."], [8.3, "s", "There is a shy girl."], [10.6, "s", "She's very timid."], [12.8, "s", "She hates to stand out."], [15.6, "s", "She works at a computer company."], [18.9, "s", "The girl's name is Tiffany."], [23.1, "s", "Tiffany is petrified of other people's opinions."], [27.6, "s", "She's scared that people will laugh at her."], [31.9, "s", "She worries she will be humiliated."], [36.4, "s", "She worries she will be humiliated if she is different."], [42.6, "s", "So, Tiffany always does the same thing that everyone else does."], [48.4, "s", "She dresses the same as everyone else."], [50.5, "s", "She never says an opinion that's different than prevailing wisdom."], [57.7, "s", "But Tiffany has a problem."], [60.1, "s", "She's unhappy."], [61.9, "s", "She wants to be an artist."], [64.0, "s", "Every day she goes to work and acts the same, but really she wants to be an artist."], [71.8, "s", "She says to herself, I can't be an artist."], [76.1, "s", "I must have a legitimate job."], [78.7, "s", "I can't be different."], [83.0, "s", "One day, Tiffany's boss comes to her desk."], [85.9, "s", "He says, I'm sorry, but you're fired."], [92.0, "s", "Tiffany is surprised and shocked."], [94.6, "s", "She asks, but why?"], [97.5, "s", "Well, says her boss, you're just awfully boring."], [102.5, "s", "You never do anything interesting."], [106.0, "s", "Tiffany goes home and cries."], [109.2, "s", "She cries for 72 days."], [113.6, "s", "On the 73rd day, she says, I'm sick of being boring."], [119.4, "s", "I'm sick of being unhappy."], [122.1, "s", "I want creativity."], [124.0, "s", "I want ecstasy."], [125.7, "s", "I will be an artist."], [129.0, "s", "Tiffany learns to draw and paint."], [131.7, "s", "She sells her paintings for a lot of money, she becomes a very successful artist."], [139.7, "s", "And she's very happy."], [145.3, "s", "Okay, let's go back this time with questions."], [149.0, "s", "This time, with questions, I'm going to pretend, I'm going to imagine the story already happened."], [158.0, "s", "Right so it already happened I'll be asking about the story as if it was in the past okay so what."], [171.6, "s", "Kind of girl was there."], [177.1, "s", "Well there was a shy and timid girl was."], [183.5, "s", "There a brave strong girl or was there a timid girl."], [191.2, "s", "Well there was a timid girl."], [194.7, "s", "There was a very timid girl."], [197.7, "q", "What was the timid girl's name?"], [202.7, "a", "The timid girl's name was Tiffany."], [206.4, "q", "Where did the timid girl work at a computer company?"], [213.5, "a", "The timid girl worked at a computer company."], [218.6, "q", "So did the timid girl like to stand out?"], [225.1, "a", "No, no."], [225.7, "s", "The timid girl did not like to stand out."], [228.0, "s", "She was timid."], [229.5, "s", "She hated to stand out."], [234.2, "q", "Did the timid girl want to be different?"], [239.3, "a", "No, she didn't."], [240.4, "s", "She didn't want to be different."], [241.8, "s", "She didn't want to stand out."], [244.6, "s", "She was timid."], [248.1, "s", "All right, so the timid girl's name was Tiffany."], [253.4, "s", "She was very scared of other people's opinions."], [260.1, "q", "How scared was she?"], [265.2, "a", "Well, she was petrified."], [267.9, "s", "Super scared of other people's opinions."], [272.6, "s", "Tiffany was petrified."], [274.5, "s", "Very, very scared."], [276.8, "s", "She was petrified of other people's opinions."], [281.2, "s", "Was Tiffany the timid girl petrified of other people's opinions?"], [287.0, "q", "Or was she relaxed about other people's opinions?"], [292.1, "a", "Well of course she was petrified, scared of other people's opinions."], [299.3, "q", "Now who was petrified?"], [303.8, "a", "Tiffany, the timid girl."], [305.6, "s", "Tiffany the timid girl was petrified."], [311.2, "q", "Was Tiffany's boss petrified?"], [315.8, "a", "No, no."], [317.1, "s", "Tiffany's boss wasn't petrified."], [318.5, "s", "He wasn't scared."], [319.3, "s", "Tiffany was petrified of other people's opinions."], [324.3, "s", "She was scared that people would laugh at her."], [328.0, "s", "She worried she would be humiliated if she was different."], [335.2, "q", "What did she worry about being humiliated?"], [342.4, "a", "She worried about being humiliated."], [346.4, "q", "Was she worried about being very embarrassed?"], [351.0, "a", "Yes, that's right."], [352.1, "s", "She worried about being very embarrassed, she worried about being humiliated."], [358.5, "q", "Why would she be humiliated?"], [364.4, "a", "She would be humiliated if she was different."], [368.1, "s", "She thought, she thought she would be humiliated if she was different."], [377.0, "q", "Who thought she would be humiliated?"], [380.8, "a", "That's right, Tiffany the timid girl thought she would be humiliated if she was different."], [387.2, "s", "So she always did the same thing as everyone else."], [392.9, "s", "She dressed the same as everyone else."], [396.2, "s", "She never said an opinion that was different than prevailing wisdom."], [406.2, "s", "She never said an opinion that was different from prevailing wisdom."], [416.4, "q", "Did Tiffany always agree with prevailing wisdom?"], [421.4, "a", "Yes, that's right, she always agreed with prevailing wisdom."], [428.8, "s", "She always agreed with the common opinion."], [432.6, "s", "She always agreed with the popular opinion, the normal opinion."], [438.0, "s", "She always agreed with prevailing wisdom."], [442.9, "q", "Did she agree with prevailing wisdom or did she disagree with prevailing wisdom?"], [451.0, "a", "She agreed."], [451.6, "s", "She always agreed with prevailing wisdom How often did she agree with prevailing wisdom?"], [462.5, "q", "How often?"], [464.7, "a", "Always she always agreed with prevailing wisdom."], [470.7, "q", "Did she sometimes agree, or did she always agree with prevailing wisdom?"], [476.2, "a", "She."], [478.6, "s", "Always agreed with prevailing wisdom who always agreed with prevailing wisdom."], [485.5, "s", "Tiffany the timid girl always agreed with prevailing wisdom but she had a problem what was her problem."], [498.9, "s", "Well she wanted to be an artist she was unhappy because she wanted to be an artist every day she went to work and acted the same."], [511.9, "s", "But really she wanted to be an artist."], [517.5, "s", "She said to herself though."], [520.2, "s", "I can't be an artist."], [523.2, "s", "I must have a legitimate job."], [526.2, "s", "I can't be different."], [530.6, "q", "What kind of job did she have to have,?"], [538.0, "a", "A legitimate job."], [539.5, "s", "She had to have a legitimate job."], [544.3, "s", "She had to have an acceptable and important job."], [550.7, "s", "She had to have a legitimate job."], [554.0, "q", "What kind of job did she have to have?"], [559.9, "a", "A legitimate job."], [562.1, "s", "Tiffany had to have a legitimate job."], [564.6, "s", "She thought she had to have a legitimate job."], [569.8, "q", "And who, who thought that?"], [574.3, "a", "Tiffany."], [575.3, "s", "Tiffany thought she had to have a legitimate job."], [579.5, "s", "She thought she couldn't be different."], [584.3, "q", "Did she really need a legitimate job?"], [589.3, "a", "No, not really."], [591.3, "s", "No, not really."], [592.2, "s", "She didn't really need a legitimate job."], [594.8, "s", "But she thought she had to have a legitimate job."], [601.2, "s", "Well, something changed."], [604.6, "s", "One day, Tiffany's boss came to her desk."], [608.7, "s", "He said, I'm sorry, but you're fired."], [615.1, "s", "Tiffany was surprised and shocked."], [617.3, "s", "She asked, but why?"], [619.7, "q", "Why am I losing my job?"], [623.6, "a", "Well, said her boss, you're just awfully boring."], [630.3, "q", "Was Tiffany a little bit boring or very boring?"], [637.0, "a", "She was very boring she was awfully boring very boring."], [646.8, "q", "Was she very awfully boring sometimes no?"], [655.2, "a", "Not sometimes she was awfully boring all the time."], [661.3, "q", "Who thought Tiffany was awfully boring her?"], [668.2, "a", "Boss right her boss thought she was awfully boring."], [673.9, "q", "Was her boss awfully boring or was Tiffany awfully boring?"], [681.7, "a", "Tiffany was awfully boring she was very boring who was awfully boring Tiffany the timid girl was awfully boring she never did anything interesting."], [698.0, "s", "Oh no; so he said, you're awfully boring, and you're fired."], [706.1, "s", "Losing your job: you're fired."], [709.7, "s", "Tiffany went home and cried; she cried and cried for 72 days; she cried and did not stop."], [722.9, "s", "72 days she cried."], [725.4, "q", "How many days did she cry?"], [728.9, "a", "72."], [730.4, "s", "He cried 72 days."], [732.7, "s", "On the 73rd day she said I'm sick of being boring."], [741.4, "s", "I'm sick of being unhappy."], [744.4, "s", "I want creativity."], [746.6, "s", "I want ecstasy."], [748.4, "s", "I will be an artist."], [752.9, "q", "Did Tiffany want to be a little bit happy?"], [757.7, "a", "No, no, no."], [759.5, "s", "Not a little bit."], [760.8, "s", "She wanted ecstasy."], [763.5, "s", "She wanted to be super, super happy."], [767.5, "s", "She wanted ecstasy, super happiness."], [772.3, "s", "Super big happiness she wanted ecstasy when."], [780.1, "q", "Did she want ecstasy?"], [784.4, "a", "Well immediately she immediately wanted ecstasy now immediately she wanted ecstasy she wanted super happiness did she want ecstasy from working in a computer company."], [802.9, "s", "No."], [804.8, "s", "She didn't feel ecstasy when she worked at the computer company."], [810.9, "s", "She wanted ecstasy from working as an artist, from being an artist."], [817.0, "s", "She said, I will be an artist."], [821.0, "q", "Who wanted ecstasy?"], [824.6, "a", "Tiffany, the timid girl."], [826.4, "s", "Tiffany, the timid girl wanted ecstasy."], [829.7, "s", "But now she's not timid now she's not timid now she's strong right now she's brave now she has courage."], [838.7, "s", "Now she wants to stand out; she says, I want ecstasy, I want super happiness, I will be an artist."], [849.4, "s", "So Tiffany learned to draw and paint; she sold her paintings for a lot of money."], [858.0, "s", "She became a very successful artist."], [861.2, "s", "And she was very, very happy."]]$j$::jsonb,
