iness or want to start your own business."], [688.8, "Standing out is not a luxury."], [692.0, "It's a necessity."], [694.4, "You start your own business, you must be different."], [697.7, "I mean, think about it as a customer, right?"], [702.3, "You're not going to choose a new company if they're the same."], [706.5, "Why would you?"], [708.1, "Why would you change companies,?"], [711.2, "Buy from someone else, if they're the same as the company you already use?"], [717.7, "If I drive a Toyota and I'm happy with Toyotas, I like Toyotas."], [725.4, "Why would I change to another company?"], [731.1, "Well, I won't."], [732.0, "I won't change to another company unless another company does something so interesting and different."], [742.0, "And exciting to me that I must change."], [748.6, "Now, that's different for every customer, of course."], [753.2, "But let's say, you know, you want me as a customer and I like fast cars."], [758.6, "Well, if you create a really fast, cool car that's not too expensive, then maybe I'll change if it's very different."], [765.6, "But if it's the same as a Toyota, I won't change."], [770.0, "So this is even worse when you start a new business because people are a little worried about new businesses, right?"], [775.8, "You're new."], [776.4, "You're not big."], [777.0, "They don't know your name; they know nothing about you."], [782.2, "So for a new business, it's even more important to stand out."], [788.4, "If you have a huge company like Toyota or Honda, well, you can be a little safe; everybody knows your name already."], [799.8, "But if you have a new business, it's vital, extremely important, to be different;"], [807.0, "different in a very interesting way for some small group of customers, some niche."], [814.3, "You know that word niche?"], [815.5, "Niche means it's a small part of a market."], [818.6, "You don't try to sell to everybody."], [820.8, "Like I don't try to sell to all English students."], [826.1, "I can't."], [827.4, "It's impossible."], [828.4, "Right?"], [828.5, "It's a huge number."], [829.7, "It'd be great if every English student in the world bought my lessons."], [832.7, "I'd be richer than Bill Gates."], [834.2, "But the truth is, everybody's not going to buy my lessons."], [840.8, "I have to find small niches, small groups that fit me, that fit my style, my personality, my methods;"], [852.1, "groups whose problems I can solve better than even very big companies."], [859.3, "So that's what my niche, my market niche, is: very independent learners who can use computers and the internet."], [870.6, "And who are focused on speaking and listening."], [875.6, "Who want to speak faster, naturally,?"], [878.3, "Automatically."], [880.0, "That's my niche."], [881.0, "That's who I sell to."], [882.0, "That's who I focus on."], [883.2, "That's who I make lessons for."], [885.4, "That's who I help."], [887.8, "I don't help students who want to learn writing and want to memorize grammar rules."], [894.5, "I don't help students who want to take tests."], [899.3, "It's a big market, but I don't do it."], [901.5, "So you have to decide this."], [902.6, "You have to decide first, who's your market?"], [904.3, "Which small group are you going to help solve their problems?"], [909.8, "And then number two, you have to stand out to that group."], [912.2, "You have to be different and remarkable."], [915.3, "Crazy."], [916.7, "Extreme."], [918.3, "Very, very something so that they notice you and talk about you."], [925.4, "People talk about me."], [926.7, "They even, when I was teaching in a school, they talk about me, AJ's a crazy teacher."], [931.1, "He's always yelling at my school."], [933.8, "All the students knew me."], [936.6, "Even the students in other classes, because I was always yelling and jumping around and telling crazy stories."], [945.3, "I was very, very, very different."], [947.4, "I stood out."], [949.0, "It's the past tense, right?"], [950.0, "I stood out."], [952.8, "Now, a lot of students really loved my style."], [956.3, "They loved me."], [957.2, "Oh, AJ's fantastic."], [958.5, "He's crazy, he's fun, he tells these great stories."], [962.2, "His method works."], [963.6, "I'm improving my speaking so much."], [965.8, "Yay, AJ, woo, we love you, mwah, mwah, mwah, mwah."], [969.7, "But, not all."], [972.7, "Some students in my class hated me."], [977.8, "They hated me."], [979.6, "He's always yelling and telling these stupid stories."], [983.8, "He never teaches from the grammar book."], [987.5, "He never uses the textbook."], [990.1, "He never gives us tests."], [993.0, "It's not serious."], [994.2, "I don't like it."], [995.9, "Some of these students complain to my boss."], [999.5, "He doesn't use the textbook."], [1001.2, "He never follows the textbook or the system at the school."], [1007.5, "Right?"], [1009.0, "And then my boss would get upset with me and meet with me."], [1011.7, "Oh, I hear that you're not using the textbook."], [1015.0, "Some students are complaining about you."], [1017.8, "That is the risk."], [1020.2, "That is the price for standing out."], [1023.5, "If you stand out that will always happen."], [1029.8, "But that's good; in marketing, in business, that is good; that's what you want."], [1037.8, "You want people to have strong feelings about you and your business, or your career; you want that."], [1048.0, "Strong feelings means some people really hate you: they don't like your style, they don't like your product, they don't like your company."], [1061.0, "But the magic part is that a lot of other people really love you."], [1069.0, "They will be super loyal customers; they will tell everybody about you, or your business."], [1077.5, "They will not leave you."], [1080.8, "They will be your salespeople."], [1084.0, "Better than you can do it."], [1085.9, "They're going to tell lots and lots and lots and lots of other people about you."], [1090.4, "Who cares about the people who hate you?"], [1092.0, "It doesn't matter."], [1092.9, "You can create a huge successful business just with the people that love you, love you, love you."], [1100.3, "People who hate you, let them find somebody else."], [1103.0, "It's okay."], [1103.4, "You can't be so sensitive in business."], [1107.0, "You just can't be sensitive."], [1110.2, "You want strong reactions."], [1112.1, "Strong reactions will give you a successful business."], [1115.8, "Strong reactions will give you a successful career."], [1119.1, "Now it won't be boring."], [1120.9, "It won't be safe."], [1123.2, "There will be some bad days."], [1125.4, "But overall."], [1127.5, "That's the path to big success in anything, to be honest, but especially in business."], [1134.4, "So think about that, and start to take small actions first, and then later big actions, to stand out, to be different."], [1144.6, "Stop playing it safe go get your dreams all right I'll see you next time bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["stand out", "/stænd aʊt/", "nổi bật"], ["remarkable", "/rɪˈmɑːkəbl/", "xuất chúng, đáng chú ý"], ["unanimous", "/juˈnænɪməs/", "nhất trí, tuyệt đối"], ["praise", "/preɪz/", "lời khen"], ["timid", "/ˈtɪmɪd/", "nhút nhát"], ["unnoticed", "/ʌnˈnəʊtɪst/", "không bị chú ý"], ["criticism", "/ˈkrɪtɪsɪzəm/", "sự chỉ trích"], ["fit in", "/fɪt ɪn/", "hòa nhập, hòa vào đám đông"], ["color inside the lines", "/ˈkʌlər ɪnˈsaɪd ðə laɪnz/", "tô trong đường kẻ, làm theo khuôn khổ"], ["pattern", "/ˈpætn/", "khuôn mẫu"], ["awfully", "/ˈɔːfli/", "cực kỳ"], ["invisible", "/ɪnˈvɪzəbl/", "vô hình"], ["prevailing wisdom", "/prɪˈveɪlɪŋ ˈwɪzdəm/", "quan niệm phổ biến"], ["petrified of", "/ˈpetrɪfaɪd əv/", "sợ chết khiếp"], ["you're set", "/jʊə set/", "bạn nắm chắc phần thắng"], ["anonymous", "/əˈnɒnɪməs/", "vô danh"], ["take a chance", "/teɪk ə tʃɑːns/", "nắm lấy cơ hội, liều thử"], ["uniqueness", "/juˈniːknəs/", "sự độc đáo"], ["security", "/sɪˈkjʊərəti/", "sự an toàn, ổn định"], ["promotion", "/prəˈməʊʃn/", "sự thăng chức"], ["attain", "/əˈteɪn/", "đạt được"], ["stuck", "/stʌk/", "mắc kẹt"], ["terrified", "/ˈterɪfaɪd/", "sợ khiếp vía"], ["humiliation", "/hjuːˌmɪliˈeɪʃn/", "sự bẽ mặt, nhục nhã"], ["embarrassed", "/ɪmˈbærəst/", "xấu hổ"], ["statistic", "/stəˈtɪstɪk/", "con số thống kê"], ["move up", "/muːv ʌp/", "thăng tiến"], ["take risks", "/teɪk rɪsks/", "chấp nhận rủi ro"], ["exaggerate", "/ɪɡˈzædʒəreɪt/", "phóng đại"], ["extreme", "/ɪkˈstriːm/", "cực độ, đi đến tận cùng"], ["legitimate", "/lɪˈdʒɪtɪmət/", "chính đáng"], ["strive to", "/straɪv tə/", "nỗ lực để"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["it's likely that some people won't like you", "nhiều khả năng có người không thích bạn"], ["Nobody gets unanimous praise, ever", "Không ai được khen ngợi tuyệt đối"], ["Criticism comes to those who stand out", "Sự chỉ trích đến với những ai nổi bật"], ["the safe thing to do was to fit in", "điều an toàn là hòa vào đám đông"], ["Playing it safe. Following the rules.", "Chơi an toàn. Tuân theo luật lệ."], ["the best ways to avoid failure", "cách tốt nhất để tránh thất bại"], ["is petrified of being different", "sợ chết khiếp chuyện khác người"], ["take a chance at greatness", "nắm lấy cơ hội để vĩ đại"], ["We are taught to fit in", "Ta được dạy phải hòa nhập"], ["feel stuck in their jobs", "thấy mắc kẹt trong công việc"], ["What terrified me was humiliation", "Điều làm tôi khiếp sợ là sự bẽ mặt"], ["fail within 5 years", "thất bại trong vòng 5 năm"], ["take risks and do things that no one else is doing", "chấp nhận rủi ro và làm điều chưa ai làm"], ["make your strong points even stronger", "làm cho điểm mạnh càng mạnh hơn"], ["strive to be different than everyone else", "nỗ lực để khác biệt với mọi người"], ["live your dreams", "sống với ước mơ của mình"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["If + S + V, it's likely that + clause", "If you practice daily, it's likely that you'll improve fast.", "Nếu luyện mỗi ngày, nhiều khả năng bạn sẽ tiến bộ nhanh.", "it's likely that"], ["The best + S + can hope for is + to V", "The best we can hope for is to finish on time.", "Điều tốt nhất ta có thể mong là xong đúng hạn.", "hope for"], ["That's when + S + started + V-ing", "That's when I started learning English seriously.", "Đó là lúc tôi bắt đầu học tiếng Anh nghiêm túc.", "That's when"], ["Not + V-ing + is the same as + V-ing", "Not practicing is the same as forgetting.", "Không luyện tập cũng giống như quên đi.", "the same as"], ["What terrified/surprised me was + noun", "What surprised me was the price.", "Điều làm tôi ngạc nhiên là cái giá.", "What"], ["If + S + had + V3, S + would have + V3", "If I had known, I would have helped.", "Nếu tôi biết, tôi đã giúp rồi.", "would have"], ["S + was criticized by + noun + when + S + V", "She was criticized by her family when she quit her job.", "Cô ấy bị gia đình chỉ trích khi bỏ việc.", "criticized"], ["Focus on + V-ing + even + comparative", "Focus on making your English even better.", "Hãy tập trung làm tiếng Anh của bạn còn tốt hơn nữa.", "Focus on"]]$j$::jsonb
