 me."], [590.3, "s", "So regardless of how much money people make ultimately finally they should put some into investments."], [602.5, "s", "Investing is the process of money making more money."], [608.6, "s", "The idea that your money works so that you don't have to work."], [615.6, "q", "So, should people invest in assets or should people invest in liabilities?"], [626.8, "a", "Well, they should invest in assets."], [631.4, "s", "Assets make money every month or lose money every month."], [639.0, "s", "Assets make money every month."], [643.8, "q", "And liabilities?"], [645.2, "a", "Liabilities make money every month or lose money every month."], [652.3, "s", "Liabilities lose money every month."], [656.1, "s", "Assets make money every month."], [662.5, "s", "And that's from Robert Kiyosaki."], [666.5, "q", "Who wrote that?"], [669.7, "a", "Robert Kiyosaki."], [670.7, "s", "Robert Kiyosaki wrote that."], [675.0, "s", "Now me."], [676.2, "s", "I like the idea of measuring wealth in time, not dollars."], [682.2, "q", "So, do I like to measure wealth with time or with dollars?"], [689.4, "a", "Well, I also like to measure wealth with time."], [695.1, "s", "The important point is not how much money you have, but how much you enjoy your life."], [706.5, "q", "So what's important?"], [710.3, "a", "How much you enjoy your life."], [712.2, "s", "How much you enjoy your life is most important."], [716.2, "s", "I once lived in my van for one year."], [718.4, "s", "Most people thought I was poor, but I felt wealthy."], [725.6, "q", "Did I feel poor or did I feel wealthy?"], [731.0, "a", "I felt wealthy."], [735.4, "q", "Did most people think I was wealthy?"], [740.4, "a", "No."], [741.2, "s", "Most people didn't think I was wealthy."], [743.6, "s", "Most people thought I was poor."], [747.7, "q", "Did I feel poor?"], [751.0, "a", "No, I didn't."], [751.8, "s", "I didn't feel poor."], [753.6, "q", "How did I feel?"], [754.4, "a", "Well, I felt wealthy."], [757.4, "s", "That's right."], [758.1, "s", "Most people thought I was poor, but I felt wealthy."], [764.7, "q", "Why did I feel wealthy?"], [769.0, "a", "Because I had a lot of time and freedom."], [774.6, "q", "Did I have a lot of money?"], [778.0, "a", "No I didn't."], [779.1, "s", "I didn't have a lot of money."], [781.6, "q", "What did I have a lot of time and freedom?"], [787.3, "a", "I had a lot of time, and I had a lot of freedom."], [793.2, "q", "Did I work a lot?"], [797.0, "a", "No I didn't."], [797.8, "s", "I didn't work a lot."], [799.3, "s", "I worked very little."], [802.7, "s", "But I still enjoyed books, movies, music, and friends."], [807.3, "s", "I had a comfortable lifestyle that required very little work."], [813.2, "s", "On the other hand, I have known many people who make a lot of money, but they aren't wealthy."], [820.6, "s", "They must work long hours every week."], [823.3, "s", "They spend more than they earn."], [825.6, "s", "They have little freedom."], [827.6, "s", "They are tired and stressed."], [829.7, "s", "They have many liabilities and few assets."], [835.8, "q", "Now always think about wealth in terms of what?"], [844.7, "a", "Time."], [846.2, "s", "Always think about wealth in terms of time."], [850.6, "q", "Should you always think about wealth in terms of dollars?"], [856.9, "a", "No, you shouldn't always think about wealth in terms of dollars."], [862.5, "s", "You shouldn't always think about wealth in terms of money."], [867.8, "s", "You should always think about wealth in terms of time."], [873.6, "s", "Ask yourself, how long could you maintain your standard of living without working?"], [882.4, "s", "How long?"], [883.6, "s", "How long could you live comfortably without working?"], [891.7, "s", "One month?"], [893.6, "s", "One week?"], [896.0, "s", "One year?"], [898.4, "s", "Ten years?"], [901.2, "s", "How could you increase that amount of time?"], [905.6, "s", "How could you get more time without working?"], [913.7, "s", "Do you regularly save and invest your money?"], [920.6, "s", "Do you?"], [923.2, "s", "Do you collect assets or liabilities?"], [928.8, "s", "What do you collect?"], [933.5, "s", "Do you collect assets?"], [935.3, "s", "Do you collect things that make more and more money?"], [938.9, "s", "For example, businesses, savings accounts, some stocks, or do you collect liabilities?"], [952.2, "s", "Do you get more credit cards?"], [955.6, "s", "Do you get more loans?"], [958.2, "s", "What do you collect?"], [960.4, "q", "What do you get more of?"], [964.4, "a", "An asset is something that provides positive cash flow."], [968.2, "q", "Does an asset provide positive or negative cash flow?"], [978.2, "a", "An asset provides positive cash flow."], [983.9, "q", "What kind of cash flow does an asset provide?"], [991.1, "a", "Positive."], [992.0, "s", "Positive cash flow."], [994.1, "q", "An asset provides positive what?"], [1000.4, "a", "Cash flow."], [1001.4, "s", "An asset provides positive cash flow."], [1006.5, "q", "Does an asset provide negative cash flow?"], [1011.1, "a", "No, no."], [1012.7, "s", "It doesn't provide negative."], [1013.9, "s", "It provides positive cash flow."], [1018.1, "q", "Is your job an asset?"], [1023.0, "a", "Yes, it is."], [1023.8, "s", "Your job is an asset."], [1025.5, "s", "It gives you money every month."], [1029.5, "q", "Is your job a liability?"], [1034.6, "a", "No."], [1035.2, "s", "Your job is not a liability."], [1036.9, "s", "You don't lose money from your job."], [1040.2, "s", "You make money from your job every month."], [1043.5, "s", "If good investments are also assets, they pay you money every month."], [1054.5, "s", "If you own a home and rent it to another person."], [1061.1, "s", "And if they pay more rent than your monthly payment then."], [1069.1, "s", "Only then."], [1070.6, "s", "Is your rental house an asset."], [1074.0, "s", "Your business is an asset if it is profitable."], [1083.6, "q", "If your business is not profitable, is it an asset or 