  $j$[[0.0, "Hello, and welcome to the commentary for true wealth."], [5.2, "I like the quote at the beginning of this article by Robert Kiyosaki, and it's funny because actually I have been thinking in this way for many years."], [16.6, "I have been thinking about wealth in terms of time, and not money."], [23.7, "Long before I read Robert Kiyosaki's books."], [27.1, "I just recently read his books, and they're really great."], [31.4, "They're the rich dad books You know the basic book is called rich dad poor dad rich dad poor dad is the title of his main book, and it's a very good book."], [42.7, "It's a great one to go get it's."], [44.8, "Basically about money management and how to how to manage your money and how to become financially free and."], [52.9, "And there's a lot of good information in there."], [55.5, "And one of the key points is in this quote and in this article."], [61.0, "Which is this idea of thinking about wealth in terms of time."], [67.3, "It's a little unusual, right?"], [69.7, "I mean, we don't usually think about wealth in terms of time."], [72.7, "Most people don't talk about wealth in terms of time, right?"], [76.4, "Most people talk about how much money they have."], [79.1, "And everybody wants more, not less."], [82.2, "And if someone has a lot of money, we think they're wealthy, right?"], [88.8, "Somebody has a million dollars and a really nice Mercedes car and a big house; we say they're wealthy, typically."], [99.1, "And somebody is living in a small little apartment, and we say they're not wealthy."], [106.8, "But this is a very tricky kind of idea I think and it's a dangerous way to think."], [116.8, "Because I do know people with a lot of money and a lot of them are not happy."], [125.2, "And I'm not talking about their you know family problems or other or emotional problems okay everybody has those kind of problems maybe it doesn't matter if rich or poor."], [136.1, "You might have problems in your family, you might have emotional problems."], [139.7, "That's not what I'm talking about."], [140.8, "I'm talking about money problems."], [142.9, "I know plenty of rich people who still have money problems."], [148.0, "I know rich people who are not financially free."], [152.7, "In fact."], [154.2, "They're less free than people who make."], [158.3, "Very little money, some people who make very little money."], [162.1, "So the difference is not really the amount of money you have."], [165.9, "Robert Kiyosaki is correct."], [168.1, "It's the amount you have compared to the amount you need every month."], [177.0, "So in other words, the idea is it's the amount of freedom you have is what wealth really is."], [182.2, "We're really measuring freedom, financial freedom."], [188.7, "And financial So freedom means how long can you survive comfortably without working?"], [196.9, "If you lost your job today."], [199.5, "You got fired or your company closed."], [202.8, "How long could you survive without getting another job?"], [207.3, "How long could you be financially comfortable, happy, relaxed without another job?"], [217.8, "That's the real question, and that's what freedom is."], [221.4, "Freedom is freedom from work, freedom from jobs, freedom from stuff you have to do."], [230.4, "You may want to work, that's fine, but if you have to work, then that's different."], [237.1, "So that's what we're talking about with wealth, it's the amount of freedom you have."], [240.7, "If you have enough money to survive one year without working, well, that's a good amount of wealth."], [251.2, "That's a little bit of wealth."], [252.4, "That's nice."], [253.7, "That feels really good."], [255.9, "You know, if your job is gone tomorrow, you don't need to be too stressed."], [261.6, "You don't need to be too worried."], [263.1, "You have 12 months to find a new one."], [266.5, "That's not so bad."], [268.4, "But what if you only have one month of wealth?"], [273.3, "What if you know that after one month, you will have zero money?"], [279.2, "You'll have none?"], [280.8, "Well, that's very, very, very stressful."], [284.9, "Because if you lose your job today or tomorrow, you are in big trouble."], [290.8, "You have a huge problem."], [292.8, "You have a lot of stress."], [294.3, "Yes, you have to find a job immediately."], [299.0, "And you don't have time to find a really nice job."], [303.1, "You don't have time to find a great job with people you like, with good amount of money."], [308.9, "Right?"], [309.1, "Too much stress."], [309.9, "You don't have enough time."], [311.0, "You need something now."], [312.4, "So probably you will take the first job you find."], [316.2, "And you know, probably it's not a good one."], [318.3, "Probably you're going to have maybe lower pay."], [321.3, "Maybe your boss is not so nice."], [323.4, "The people are not so nice so this is an important question for the quality of."], [329.6, "our lives; I mean, for me, that's the biggest goal, that's the main point."], [334.9, "It's not how much money you have; I mean, who cares?"], [339.1, "You know, so many people worry about what other people think, so many people are trying to be rich, not wealthy."], [347.1, "And I think the difference is, you know, rich is you have a lot of money."], [353.2, "Wealthy is you have a lot of freedom."], [357.5, "And plenty of rich people are not free."], [360.8, "They must continue working."], [363.6, "There are plenty of rich people who if they lost their business or they lost their job."], [369.1, "You know, maybe it's a very nice job, maybe it pays a lot of money."], [372.7, "But if they lost that job, one month later they lose everything."], [377.0, "One month later, they have no money saved, so they have to find another job immediately."], [384.1, "They will be under a lot of stress."], [386.3, "If they don't find a job, they can lose their house, their car."], [390.0, "Everything is gone very quickly."], [393.6, "You know, we hear about this."], [394.8, "We hear about famous people sometimes."], [397.4, "Famous people who have millions and millions and millions of dollars."], [402.0, "They're super rich, and suddenly they lose everything."], [409.6, "And normal people like us, we think, God, that's crazy."], [412.5, "How did that happen?"], [414.6, "Well, it's because they were not wealthy."], [417.2, "They were still spending more money than they had."], [420.7, "They had $10 million, well, they were spending $11 million on expensive houses, huge houses."], [427.8, "Not just one house many houses and super expensive cars etc and."], [436.1, "Then suddenly they stopped getting they were stopped getting famous they stopped getting a lot of money and then they lost everything."], [446.6, "So being rich is really about trying to show other people; it's trying to be better than other people."], [454.8, "You know, I'll be honest: I don't like rich people; most rich people, I don't like them."], [462.2, "I think they're kind of stupid and shallow; they're fake, they're fake people."], [467.9, "They're trying to make other people think they're better, right?"], [472.2, "So they drive these cars that are, you know, super expensive, and most of them don't really care about cars."], [480.9, "They just care that other people look at them and think, wow, they're great."], [487.0, "And that's the same reason they buy these giant houses."], [491.3, "How much do you really need?"], [494.3, "A big house is nice, but do you really need 30 bedrooms?"], [499.3, "No, of course they don't."], [501.5, "What they need is they need other people to look at them and think they are better,?"], [507.3, "Better than."], [509.1, "It's ego."], [511.9, "I want to be better than other people."], [513.8, "I want other people to look at me and be jealous."], [516.3, "I want other people to think I'm higher than them."], [521.0, "That's being rich, and I don't care about being rich And I'm not going to tell you how to be rich, and I hope you won't choose that route."], [528.8, "What I am focused on is wealth?"], [532.6, "Because wealth is deeper wealth means the quality of your life Doesn't matter what other people think it means what kind of freedom."], [541.1, "Do you have in your life?"], [542.3, "Are you free to do everything you really want to do?"], [546.9, "Are you free to go after your dreams, to get your dreams?"], [553.5, "Maybe you want to be an artist."], [555.5, "Maybe you dreamed about painting."], [558.5, "But right now you can't paint."], [560.4, "Why not?"], [561.1, "Because you're too busy working all the time."], [564.0, "You have a stressful, difficult job."], [567.5, "You're not free."], [569.1, "In your heart you want to paint."], [571.0, "But you don't have time to paint, because for most people, painting does not make very much money."], [578.1, "It's hard to be a full-time painter."], [581.8, "But if you have wealth, if you have enough wealth, you can be a full-time painter."], [588.0, "If you have wealth, it means you have freedom."], [589.7, "It means you have the time and the money to do exactly what you want."], [594.5, "You can spend all day painting because now you have real freedom."], [599.3, "You have real wealth You know, maybe you don't want to be a painter."], [602.8, "Maybe you want to be a writer."], [605.4, "Maybe you want to you know, I don't know be a."], [609.1, "Athlete."], [610.7, "Maybe you do maybe you love business But if you have wealth you can do business because you love it."], [617.1, "You can do it to help people You can do it to be creative not just because you need more money."], [626.0, "So this is an important shift, and it might seem simple."], [631.6, "But if you make this a new habit, if you continually think about wealth in terms of time,"], [640.8, "always thinking, how long could I survive without working?"], [645.4, "Survive comfortably; not survive as a homeless person; survive in your same house."], [652.0, "Your same life."], [653.7, "Your same expenses you have now."], [655.4, "How long could you survive?"], [656.6, "And then think, how could I survive longer?"], [660.4, "Maybe you need to make more money."], [663.6, "Sure, that's part of it."], [665.4, "Maybe also you could reduce your liabilities or eliminate your liabilities."], [672.0, "Even if you don't have more money, if you eliminate your liabilities, ta-da!"], [677.3, "Now you have more wealth."], [680.3, "Another thing you could do is, you know, take some of your money that you save and invest it carefully so that now you start having a little more coming in."], [689.6, "For some people, just saving is a first step is important."], [693.1, "Most Americans, Americans don't save much money."], [696.3, "It's a big, big, big mistake."], [699.2, "So saving, just saving is a way to increase your wealth."], [705.1, "So the important part is just to change your thinking right now."], [709.0, "That's That's really what I want you to do with this article."], [712.0, "Change the way you think."], [713.0, "Think in terms of time."], [715.0, "Always asking yourself, how long could I survive without a job?"], [718.7, "If I lost my job, how long could I survive comfortably?"], [722.3, "If my business suddenly stopped, how long could I survive comfortably?"], [728.1, "Keep thinking in terms of time, time, time, not just money."], [732.1, "And it will start to change your actions and eventually it will change your life."], [738.1, "Alright, well good luck, I hope you enjoyed this article, and good luck in your life, I hope that you start to build real wealth, which means real freedom."], [747.9, "Great, I'll see you next time, bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
