  $j$[[0.2, "Hi."], [1.6, "Welcome to the commentary for The Process."], [6.7, "Are you starting to notice a pattern?"], [10.6, "Are you seeing some repetition in these articles?"], [15.8, "I'm sure you are."], [17.4, "There's a reason for that."], [19.7, "And the reason is."], [21.5, "I'm trying to change your way of thinking."], [24.6, "Your basic attitude, your basic approach to business and your career."], [31.6, "That's the most important step."], [33.8, "You're a smart person."], [35.2, "You're an intelligent person."], [37.2, "Most people are."], [39.7, "So you don't need me to tell you about your specific job."], [43.6, "You know your job very well."], [45.5, "You don't need me to tell you about your specific business."], [48.6, "You know it very well."], [51.3, "But what you probably need help with is changing the way you think about your career."], [62.8, "Changing the way you think about your business."], [66.6, "You see, the thing I learned most from creating this successful business is that most of the challenge."], [80.2, "Most of the problems and most of the success happens in your head."], [88.6, "When I changed my way of thinking, the business began to grow and grow and grow and grow."], [97.8, "Very fast."], [99.1, "I got great ideas."], [100.5, "I tried a lot of interesting new things."], [103.0, "Everything got better after I changed my way of thinking."], [109.4, "I was still the same person."], [111.7, "I still had the same basic ideas about teaching English."], [117.1, "But my attitude, my thinking changed."], [121.7, "And specifically, what I changed is what you find in this article."], [127.4, "I began to realize that the key to success was being very remarkable, remarkably different in a few different ways."], [143.5, "Now in the past, before I changed, I was already somewhat different, but I thought that was bad."], [150.6, "I thought that was something that I shouldn't talk about."], [155.4, "I thought that being like everyone else was the good way to go."], [161.9, "It was the good method."], [163.0, "It was the way to succeed."], [165.3, "I thought, oh, I need to tell my customers, tell my students that, oh, actually, you know, my methods, they're similar to normal methods."], [180.8, "Well, they're not."], [182.5, "And so I began to realize, the more I learned about marketing."], [186.3, "Especially."], [187.8, "And just business in general also, I began to realize that my differences were my strengths."], [195.5, "I began to realize those weren't weaknesses, those were the best parts of my business."], [201.0, "Instead of hiding them, instead of being quiet about them, I should yell about them."], [207.3, "I should stress them."], [208.8, "I should make them stronger and stronger and stronger."], [213.5, "When I change that way of thinking, The business began to grow and grow and grow very fast."], [223.7, "So I began to consciously."], [226.2, "Deliberately."], [228.1, "I began to think about it and with a plan deliberately I chose to go to the edge with different parts of my business."], [241.3, "Number one, I decided to go to the edge with grammar."], [245.3, "I already knew that teaching grammar rules, like analyzing grammar, memorizing grammar rules, I knew it didn't work."], [254.6, "I already knew that was a failed way to teach."], [256.9, "It was not successful."], [258.5, "But, you know, in the past I thought, oh, I need to do it a little bit."], [263.1, "Because that's what students want."], [265.4, "That's what my boss wants."], [268.7, "Well, when I changed my way of thinking I decided no grammar rules, none, zero."], [275.0, "I will go to the edge in this area."], [280.2, "And what's the farthest edge?"], [282.3, "What's the most extreme edge?"], [284.6, "What's the strongest edge in this area?"], [288.0, "The strongest edge is absolutely zero grammar rules."], [292.4, "Do not teach any grammar rules."], [295.0, "None."], [296.5, "That's the edge."], [298.1, "And that's the effortless English system now."], [301.6, "We never teach grammar rules."], [304.1, "You never, ever, ever memorize the past perfect or the future perfect progressive."], [310.3, "You never study that with effortless English."], [314.3, "So that's one edge that we have."], [316.3, "It's very remarkable, very different than most other schools, most other textbooks, most other lessons."], [325.4, "So that's one of our edges, and we do it on purpose."], [328.1, "We choose to do that."], [329.2, "It's not an accident."], [332.1, "Okay, another edge that I found was my energy, my enthusiasm."], [338.2, "Okay, and again, in the past, I worried about that."], [342.5, "I know it seems funny now, but in the past, I worried."], [345.0, "I knew I was so different."], [346.6, "I was always the teacher who was jumping around and yelling."], [350.4, "Right?"], [351.3, "I had all this crazy energy."], [354.7, "It's not an act."], [356.0, "That's really my personality."], [359.3, "I just have a lot of energy and I get excited."], [362.9, "Especially when I teach."], [364.5, "I enjoy teaching."], [365.6, "I like to perform."], [368.0, "It's kind of my personality."], [369.9, "So in the past I thought, oh you know, some people would criticize it, some people would complain about it, especially other teachers."], [377.8, "And so I tried to hide that."], [380.4, "But then when I changed my thinking, I went to the edge."], [385.9, "I decided, this isn't a bad thing."], [388.5, "This is a good thing."], [389.7, "This edge is a strength."], [392.4, "This edge will help me succeed."], [394.5, "I will try to be even more passionate, even more energetic."], [399.7, "And so in my classes I began to be super, incredibly energetic and passionate."], [407.6, "I jumped around even more, I yelled even more, I had even more energy, I had even crazier, funnier stories."], [418.9, "So that was another edge; it was not an accident, I chose this edge."], [426.7, "I chose to take this remarkable part of me and make it even more remarkable."], [435.2, "So that's the general process."], [438.0, "I mean the idea is very simple, right?"], [440.7, "What you do is you look at yourself or you look at your business and find something that's already a little different."], [452.5, "I don't know."], [453.5, "Everyone's different, right?"], [454.4, "So I don't know what it is, but something about you For example, even in your job, if you're still working at a job."], [461.7, "What about you is different?"], [463.6, "What about you is a little remarkable, not like everyone else?"], [469.9, "I don't know."], [470.4, "Maybe you're passionate and crazy and energetic like me."], [474.7, "Maybe you're the opposite."], [475.9, "Maybe you're super calm."], [479.1, "Maybe you're very friendly."], [480.4, "Maybe you are very efficient."], [483.3, "Maybe you're really angry and you get upset really easily and you yell and you scream a lot."], [491.9, "I don't know, maybe you never get angry."], [494.5, "I don't know what it is but find something that's very different and remarkable."], [501.0, "Now of course you have to compare to other people so what is it about you that's different than other people."], [509.1, "Find those things and then make them stronger."], [512.9, "Stop hiding them."], [514.9, "Do not think they are weaknesses."], [516.5, "They're not weaknesses, they are your best strengths."], [519.6, "They are your key to success."], [523.8, "So make them stronger and stronger and stronger."], [527.8, "That's how you go to the edge."], [529.8, "You take what you already have, something that's already different, a little different, And then you make it stronger and stronger, more and more different, more and more remarkable."], [542.0, "If you have a business, it's the same process."], [546.1, "You have a product or you have a service."], [549.5, "What about your product or service is already a little different?"], [556.8, "Maybe your product right now is not so special."], [559.3, "Maybe your service, your business is not so special."], [561.9, "But something is a little different, right?"], [565.3, "There's something that's a little different than normal."], [569.1, "Maybe your price is a little higher or a little lower."], [574.0, "Or maybe you're a little bit more friendly or a little bit less friendly."], [579.4, "I don't know."], [580.0, "But find the things that are a little bit different."], [584.8, "And then make them stronger and stronger and stronger."], [588.0, "If your price is a little bit higher, try to increase it more, right?"], [593.4, "People are always scared about that; I don't know why. You don't want to be cheap."], [599.6, "Being cheap is a bad strategy for business, except for a few very big companies; for most people, being the cheapest is a really bad idea."], [609.7, "So try the opposite: if you're already a little bit more expensive, raise your price even more, and see what happens."], [617.9, "Your sales might actually go up because now you're even more remarkable."], [624.8, "The point is try things that no one else tries."], [629.6, "Do things that no one else does."], [633.2, "Be more something than everybody else."], [638.4, "Maybe more cheap, maybe more expensive, maybe more friendly, maybe more efficient."], [644.5, "Maybe more luxurious, you know, you give a lot more bonuses, a lot of extra stuff."], [652.4, "For example, maybe you have a, you're a dentist, right, with teeth, you clean teeth."], [658.9, "Well, every dentist does basically the same thing, right?"], [662.4, "You come to their office, you sit down, they clean your teeth, you leave."], [666.4, "Most of them are very clean, so you're not going to be more clean than most dentists, probably."], [672.0, "It's hard to be even more clean, but maybe you could do it."], [676.2, "My mom works with a dentist, and she is super, super, super clean."], [681.4, "It's the cleanest dentist office ever."], [685.2, "They put plastic over everything, so they never touch anything directly with their hands."], [690.8, "And when a new patient comes, they take the plastic off, they put new plastic on the handles for the chairs, on everything."], [701.4, "So they are remarkably clean, even more than normal dentists."], [707.9, "And normal dentists are very clean already."], [710.4, "So they are remarkably clean."], [712.6, "But maybe you could do something else."], [714.1, "Maybe if you're a dentist, you could do a lot of extra friendly, nice things."], [723.4, "Maybe your office is remarkably beautiful."], [727.8, "Most dentist offices are ugly."], [731.0, "They're white."], [731.8, "They're kind of ugly."], [732.8, "They look like hospitals."], [734.1, "Maybe you have a lot of plants."], [735.9, "Maybe yours is brown and green."], [739.6, "Maybe you have big, colorful paintings on the walls."], [745.1, "Maybe it feels like a Starbucks instead of a dentist office."], [752.4, "That would be remarkably different."], [755.2, "That's the appearance, the decoration, the office."], [758.3, "That would be remarkably different."], [760.2, "Just another example."], [762.1, "There are many infinite ways you can choose to be different and remarkable."], [768.8, "You just need to think about it."], [772.9, "And it's the same in your career."], [774.2, "You need to be remarkably different in your career."], [778.4, "So that's all you need to do."], [779.6, "That's the big change I want you to make in your career or in your business."], [786.8, "Now, I'll talk more about details later."], [789.1, "I'll have some commentaries and an e-book about niche marketing and some specific business strategies."], [797.7, "But they're less important than this big idea."], [801.6, "That's why I keep repeating this big idea in different ways, right?"], [806.3, "Each of these articles is really saying the same big idea in a little bit different way."], [813.4, "But the same idea again and again and again, which is be different, be remarkable."], [819.9, "Don't be the same as everyone else."], [822.9, "Go to the edge with something in your personality."], [827.6, "In your product, in your service, in your actions."], [831.6, "In the way you dress, in the way you look."], [834.6, "Something."], [836.9, "Be very remarkable, very, very extremely different than everyone else."], [845.0, "I mean, that's it."], [846.0, "That's the central thing."], [847.2, "If there's one big secret for business success, for career success, this is it, and I'm going to say it a thousand times until you learn it deeply until you take action and do this."], [864.2, "Try it."], [865.1, "Do it."], [866.8, "This is it, man."], [868.1, "This is the key."], [869.0, "This is the secret."], [870.3, "If you need a secret for big business success, if you need a secret for career success, here it is."], [877.5, "So simple."], [881.0, "Very easy to understand."], [885.4, "The hard part is doing it."], [887.4, "That's the scary part."], [891.6, "Doing something very different is scary because people might laugh."], [897.0, "People might criticize."], [899.4, "People might think you're crazy."], [902.5, "Or you might just fail."], [904.6, "That's possible."], [906.0, "There's no foolproof plan."], [909.3, "Sometimes you will fail."], [911.7, "If you fail, what you do?"], [914.7, "Could you be normal again?"], [918.1, "No, of course not."], [920.7, "Do not just be normal again."], [922.2, "If you fail, say, okay, well, that failed."], [925.8, "I'm going to try a different edge."], [928.3, "I'm going to try to be remarkable, different, extreme, in a different kind of way."], [937.5, "Maybe you try to be extremely expensive."], [940.4, "You raise your price very high and it's not successful; you lose sales, your business goes down."], [947.5, "Okay, well, that did not succeed, so now you need to do something else."], [953.3, "Maybe you drop your price to normal and you change something else; you make something else remarkable."], [960.3, "Or maybe you keep your price very high, but you need to add more stuff so people think it's a good value."], [969.5, "Maybe you need to also be remarkably good at service."], [973.6, "Maybe you need to have a remarkably beautiful office."], [978.6, "Maybe you need to make more other things remarkable."], [982.8, "So then you can have a very, very remarkable high price."], [986.8, "I don't know, again, Seth Godin is right."], [989.4, "There's no foolproof formula."], [993.8, "But if you follow this general strategy and you keep trying."], [998.8, "You try something and you try something else, Then you try something else."], [1003.0, "Always trying to be different."], [1005.5, "Always trying to be remarkable."], [1007.4, "Always trying to push to the extreme in different parts of your career or business."], [1013.7, "If you keep doing that process, trying again and again and again, you will succeed."], [1020.2, "I guarantee you will succeed and you will succeed in a very big way."], [1026.1, "All right, so you're probably tired of hearing this same advice, but you know what?"], [1030.4, "But it's very important advice, and I really hope you'll follow it, because this is it."], [1036.6, "This is the big one."], [1038.4, "Follow this, everything else you'll figure out."], [1041.0, "Everything else will eventually work if you just follow this process."], [1046.6, "Alright, good luck to you."], [1049.0, "See you next time."], [1049.9, "Bye-bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["process", "/ˈprəʊses/", "quy trình"], ["foolproof", "/ˈfuːlpruːf/", "chắc ăn, không thể sai"], ["formula", "/ˈfɔːmjələ/", "công thức"], ["ritual", "/ˈrɪtʃuəl/", "nghi lễ"], ["incantation", "/ˌɪnkænˈteɪʃn/", "câu thần chú"], ["creativity", "/ˌkriːeɪˈtɪvəti/", "sự sáng tạo"], ["grounded in reality", "/ˈɡraʊndɪd ɪn riˈæləti/", "bám sát thực tế"], ["rearview mirror", "/ˈrɪəvjuː ˈmɪrə(r)/", "gương chiếu hậu"], ["tactic", "/ˈtæktɪk/", "chiến thuật"], ["edge", "/edʒ/", "giới hạn, mép, rìa"], ["deliver results", "/dɪˈlɪvə rɪˈzʌlts/", "mang lại kết quả"], ["financial model", "/faɪˈnænʃl ˈmɒdl/", "mô hình tài chính"], ["pricing", "/ˈpraɪsɪŋ/", "việc định giá"], ["redefine", "/ˌriːdɪˈfaɪn/", "định nghĩa lại"], ["innovation", "/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃn/", "sự đổi mới"], ["fringe", "/frɪndʒ/", "vùng rìa"], ["go to extremes", "/ɡəʊ tu ɪkˈstriːmz/", "đi đến cực độ"], ["push to the edge", "/pʊʃ tə ði edʒ/", "đẩy đến giới hạn"], ["wedding anniversary", "/ˈwedɪŋ ˌænɪˈvɜːsəri/", "ngày kỷ niệm cưới"], ["efficient", "/ɪˈfɪʃnt/", "hiệu quả"], ["accuracy", "/ˈækjərəsi/", "độ chính xác"], ["compete against", "/kəmˈpiːt əˈɡenst/", "cạnh tranh với"], ["tremendous", "/trəˈmendəs/", "to lớn"], ["enthusiasm", "/ɪnˈθjuːziæzəm/", "sự nhiệt huyết"], ["exclusively", "/ɪkˈskluːsɪvli/", "chỉ duy nhất"], ["packaging", "/ˈpækɪdʒɪŋ/", "bao bì"], ["mediocrity", "/ˌmiːdiˈɒkrəti/", "sự tầm thường"], ["excellence", "/ˈeksələns/", "sự xuất sắc"], ["doubt", "/daʊt/", "nghi ngờ"], ["vibrant", "/ˈvaɪbrənt/", "sôi nổi, rực rỡ"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["a foolproof way to create a big success", "cách chắc ăn để tạo thành công lớn"], ["stay firmly grounded in reality", "vẫn bám chắc vào thực tế"], ["Of course not. There is no plan.", "Dĩ nhiên là không. Không có kế hoạch nào."], ["By definition, ...", "Theo định nghĩa, ..."], ["I'm sorry to tell you that ...", "Rất tiếc phải nói với bạn rằng ..."], ["Go for the edges", "Hãy hướng tới các giới hạn"], ["it's not clear that you'd last very long", "chưa chắc bạn trụ được lâu"], ["go to extremes in some area", "đi đến tận cùng ở một mảng nào đó"], ["push friendliness to the edge", "đẩy sự thân thiện đến giới hạn"], ["People are amazed at ...", "Mọi người kinh ngạc trước ..."], ["which is why we can compete against ...", "đó là lý do chúng tôi có thể cạnh tranh với ..."], ["do everything well, but nothing remarkably", "làm mọi thứ tốt nhưng chẳng có gì xuất chúng"], ["not worry about the rest", "mặc kệ phần còn lại"], ["the path of mediocrity", "con đường của sự tầm thường"], ["Do it again and again", "Làm đi làm lại"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["Is there + a/any + noun + that + S + can + V?", "Is there a book that I can read on the plane?", "Có cuốn sách nào tôi có thể đọc trên máy bay không?", "Is there"], ["If you're looking for + noun, I'm sorry to tell you that ...", "If you're looking for a shortcut, I'm sorry to tell you that there isn't one.", "Nếu bạn tìm đường tắt, rất tiếc là không có đâu.", "I'm sorry to tell you"], ["To be + adj, you have to + V", "To be fluent, you have to listen a lot.", "Để nói trôi chảy, bạn phải nghe nhiều.", "you have to"], ["S + do(es) + much more/much less + than + noun", "She works much less than her colleagues but earns more.", "Cô ấy làm ít hơn hẳn đồng nghiệp mà kiếm nhiều hơn.", "much less than"], ["S + figured out how to + V", "We figured out how to fix the problem.", "Chúng tôi đã tìm ra cách khắc phục vấn đề.", "figured out"], ["S + can be + adj + by + V-ing", "You can be healthier by walking every day.", "Bạn có thể khỏe hơn bằng cách đi bộ mỗi ngày.", "by"], ["..., which is why + clause", "The food is cheap, which is why the place is always full.", "Đồ ăn rẻ, đó là lý do quán lúc nào cũng đông.", "which is why"], ["You can + V, but + clause", "You can do everything well, but nothing remarkably.", "Bạn có thể làm mọi thứ tốt, nhưng chẳng có gì xuất chúng.", "but"]]$j$::jsonb
)
