  $j$[[0.0, "Hello and welcome to the commentary for Wealth Steps."], [6.1, "Now in this article, Robert Kiyosaki gives us a very general formula for success, for financial success again."], [18.1, "And it's interesting because it's general because it was an international study, right?"], [23.9, "Right?"], [24.4, "They looked at all these different countries and they studied a specific kind of person."], [34.2, "They studied people who were very poor."], [38.3, "People born into poverty."], [40.7, "Who later became rich,?"], [43.7, "Who later became wealthy."], [47.4, "Now later, you know, what does that mean?"], [49.2, "We don't know."], [49.6, "For some people, maybe it was five years later; maybe for some people it was 20 years, for some people 50 years."], [59.8, "But it was not instant, right? Not suddenly one day; they didn't win a big prize or a contest."], [68.6, "They did something with their actions to create wealth, to create more money, to create success, financial freedom for themselves and for their families."], [79.8, "And so these people from all different countries of the world had three very general basic qualities."], [89.7, "They had a long-term vision."], [91.7, "They believed in delayed gratification."], [94.0, "They used the power of compounding."], [97.2, "These seem fairly obvious."], [99.7, "I think we can all imagine why."], [102.3, "These are general secrets to success, but it's good to review them."], [108.4, "It's good to remember, most importantly, it's good to look at our own lives."], [115.3, "We forget sometimes, I think."], [118.1, "All the advertising we see on TV, for example."], [121.9, "Makes it easy for us to go buy, buy, buy, buy, buy."], [125.8, "And we forget our long-term vision."], [130.0, "Or, you know, we're just busy every day; we go to our job, we have lots of things to do."], [138.1, "Maybe you have family, maybe you have kids, and it's easy to get very busy now, today, and forget your long-term vision, your long-term dream."], [148.2, "So I think that first one is first for a reason; I think because it's the most important."], [155.5, "The long-term vision is probably, in a very general way,"], [159.6, "The most important."], [161.4, "Because if you have a big dream and you remind yourself every day about it."], [169.5, "You think about it every day."], [172.1, "Not just thinking, but with emotion."], [175.0, "You imagine it every day."], [177.1, "You can see it every day."], [179.2, "It feels real to you."], [183.0, "And you're constantly thinking about it, again and again and again, all day, every day."], [189.4, "You can see this vision in your head, this great vision of something better for yourself, more financial freedom."], [197.6, "You will find a method you will find a way to get that dream if."], [206.6, "You remember it every day with emotion it will happen the problem is that we often forget our long-term visions."], [216.7, "Maybe you had one in the past or maybe you have one and you sometimes think about it, you know, but usually you kind of forget it."], [225.1, "You're thinking too much about what's happening, you know, right now at your job or some problem you have."], [234.7, "So I think it's very important to write down your goal, your big vision, or visions; you probably have more than one."], [245.2, "And, you know, put it somewhere you will see it every day: on your calendar, on your desk at work, on your refrigerator at home."], [257.1, "Put it in several different places, and every day see it, read it, think about it, imagine it."], [265.7, "Always have it in your mind, in the front of your mind, as the most important thing."], [273.8, "Not the problem you have now, your big vision."], [278.1, "I think that's something we should all do."], [280.0, "And you know, it's good for everything, not just money."], [283.3, "It's not only good for financial success, it's good for any kind of success."], [289.4, "If you need to."], [290.8, "Or you want to be better in your relationship with."], [296.6, "Your husband or wife or boyfriend or girlfriend."], [298.8, "Well again, it's a night."], [300.3, "It's a great vision a great goal be specific exactly What do you want and think about it every day remind yourself every day keep that vision alive?"], [309.6, "Don't lose it Just that one that number one."], [314.6, "I think you is enough to be successful to be honest if you have number one Then you will have the energy to find the answers you need."], [325.6, "Maybe it will take you a long time."], [328.5, "Maybe not, but you will eventually find what you need and you will eventually do it."], [336.9, "If you always think about your vision every single day with emotion."], [344.9, "So that's a good one."], [347.3, "The second quality was delayed gratification."], [349.9, "They believed in delayed gratification, delayed pleasure."], [355.7, "Also important."], [357.9, "Now it doesn't mean you have to suffer and suffer now, it doesn't mean you need to feel pain now."], [365.3, "You want to enjoy your life right now, of course you do."], [369.0, "It just means that you wait for some pleasures."], [374.5, "And here we're talking about money, right?"], [376.4, "So, what it really means is you wait to buy things that you don't really need."], [384.0, "What do you really need?"], [385.0, "You need food."], [386.9, "And you need a safe, warm place to live."], [391.5, "And you need some clothes, and that's really all."], [397.4, "You really don't need much else."], [400.2, "Everything else you want."], [403.2, "Don't need them."], [404.2, "You want them."], [404.7, "A cell phone, do you need it?"], [406.9, "No."], [408.3, "You want it, and that's okay."], [412.2, "So what we're saying here, delayed gratification, it means some of your wants, they can wait."], [420.1, "Some things that you want now, you feel good, maybe a new phone that's more expensive."], [426.3, "Maybe a new car that's much nicer, maybe a bigger house."], [431.4, "Maybe new clothes."], [433.9, "You don't need them."], [435.4, "You want them."], [436.3, "If you buy them, maybe you will feel good, but if you want to be successful."], [443.4, "You must delay buying them."], [445.9, "You must wait."], [448.4, "Delay your pleasure for these new things."], [455.6, "Why do you delay your pleasure?"], [457.3, "Because if you delay the pleasure, or if you delay the gratification."], [461.5, "If you wait."], [462.6, "If you save that money instead of buying."], [467.5, "Well then in the future."], [469.4, "You will finally have total financial freedom."], [473.0, "Then you can buy anything you want, any time."], [477.2, "If you don't delay your gratification, you always feel stress."], [485.2, "You're always, you're gonna buy something, you'll feel good for one day maybe."], [489.0, "But then you're gonna feel stress because, oh no, now I have no money again."], [493.7, "Oh no, now I owe my credit card, even more money."], [498.5, "So you get a little pleasure short term right now, but then in the future, you get more pain, more stress."], [506.7, "Less freedom."], [509.0, "People who became wealthy, they do the opposite."], [512.4, "They feel a little bit less now."], [516.8, "They buy less stuff now."], [518.8, "They have a little less pleasure now but."], [525.7, "Then in the future, they have more and more happiness, more and more freedom, more and more money, more and more pleasure."], [533.8, "So they wait; they delay it."], [536.0, "This is another important thing: every time you're going to buy something, think, do I need it?"], [542.2, "Do I really need this new shirt? Do I really need a new phone?"], [547.4, "My phone works fine now; do I really need the newer, bigger, expensive one?"], [552.5, "Do I really need a new car?"], [555.0, "Do I really need a bigger house?"], [558.2, "You should ask yourself this all the time and delay, delay, wait."], [566.3, "Take that money, save it and invest it."], [571.4, "Use it to start a business."], [573.8, "Use it to buy stocks."], [575.4, "Use it to buy a house that you rent to somebody else so you can make even more money."], [583.2, "Use it for an investment instead of small short-term pleasure now."], [590.2, "That's what delayed gratification means and it's also a very excellent idea."], [595.6, "And finally, they use the power of compounding."], [598.1, "This is the third quality."], [601.0, "This idea of compounding, it really means growing."], [604.8, "They use the power of growing money."], [608.1, "So they're always thinking, how can I grow my money?"], [612.4, "Not just save it."], [614.4, "So that's the difference between compounding and saving."], [618.9, "Saving I have $1,000 and I keep it in a box in my room."], [624.4, "And next month I still have $1,000."], [627.8, "And after one year, well, I still have $1,000, and after 10 years, still $1,000."], [634.9, "The money's not growing."], [638.1, "But if I use the power of compounding, of multiplying."], [642.9, "Growing and growing."], [644.3, "Well, maybe I put it in the bank."], [647.3, "And I get 1% every year."], [653.0, "Now, that's terrible."], [654.1, "It's very small, but still."], [655.2, "Well, it means after one year, I will have more than $1,000."], [659.7, "I'll have a little more."], [661.7, "After two years, I'll have even more."], [664.4, "After 10 years, even more."], [666.3, "After 20 years, even more."], [668.3, "The money will grow."], [670.5, "So that's what compounding means."], [673.3, "You could buy stocks, right?"], [675.6, "You could buy ownership, small pieces of a company."], [680.1, "And then over time, hopefully, that money increases; the value goes up and up and up; your money grows and grows."], [689.9, "Stocks are a little dangerous, because sometimes they go down; you have to be careful."], [696.9, "Another thing you could start a business you have a thousand dollars you start a new business the business is successful."], [705.0, "So after one year, you make $5,000."], [708.2, "After two years, you make $30,000."], [713.3, "For 10 years, you're making $100,000."], [716.2, "Your money has grown a lot, right?"], [721.0, "Starting a small business is probably one of the best ways to use the power of compounding."], [727.2, "You want to always Just think about your money, not just save, but grow."], [730.9, "How can I make my money grow?"], [733.2, "That's what these people did."], [735.4, "The people who started poor and became rich, they didn't just save."], [742.2, "Saving was the first step, but the next step was they're always thinking, how can I make my money grow?"], [748.7, "I want my money to grow."], [750.6, "So you have to do the same."], [752.0, "You have to save some money."], [753.7, "Delayed gratification, wait."], [756.4, "Don't buy some things, save the money, and then next you have to make it grow."], [763.3, "Make that money grow somehow."], [765.4, "Make it grow a little bit, make it grow a lot, but make it grow."], [769.5, "That's important."], [773.1, "Okay, so that's really the central theme, the main points of this article."], [778.6, "I'll talk a little bit about myself more personally now, and my thoughts on this."], [784.0, "And my thoughts on this is that I totally agree."], [788.0, "I certainly, when I started Effortless English, I had a vision, still do have a vision about Effortless English, and I thought about it all the time."], [795.9, "In fact, my vision started a long, long time ago."], [801.1, "My vision started when I was maybe 15 years old."], [806.9, "I was very young."], [808.2, "I got my first job at a fast food restaurant."], [813.1, "The restaurant's name was Arby's I don't know they have them in America I don't know if they have them other countries but like McDonald's like Burger King and."], [824.4, "I hated my job; it was terrible, boring, and the pay was so low."], [830.6, "And starting then, when I was 15, I realized, oh, I really hate working; I don't like jobs."], [838.6, "And I had a vision: I want to be free, I want to be free financially."], [845.7, "I could imagine in my head: someday in the future I will be free; I won't need a job, I won't have a boss."], [856.4, "Now, it took me 20, 25 years, but finally my vision came true."], [862.1, "And that vision got stronger and stronger as I got older."], [867.0, "I kept thinking about it, kept thinking about it."], [870.4, "So in fact, this vision started a long, long time ago for me."], [875.4, "But for Effortless English, actually starting my own business, you know, I started in November of 2006."], [882.8, "More recently."], [885.1, "And since starting the business, every day I have thought about it and I have imagined it growing."], [892.2, "I have imagined it being successful."], [893.7, "I have imagined having a big community of members, all learning from each other, meeting each other, making friends."], [902.0, "So I have this dream and I still have it, it's very strong."], [905.1, "And I always remember it."], [906.4, "Every day I think about it."], [909.6, "And delayed gratification, waiting for pleasure, waiting for, you know, bigger things, spending more money."], [917.9, "Definitely, I'm still living in a tiny little apartment."], [922.9, "Tomoe and I both live in the cheapest apartment in San Francisco, small, one little room."], [930.5, "We have a shared bathroom."], [931.8, "We share the bathroom with everybody on the same floor."], [937.5, "Why are we doing this?"], [938.7, "People think that I'm crazy."], [940.9, "People think we're crazy because we have much more money."], [945.1, "We could certainly get a more expensive place, no problem."], [951.3, "But I feel like we should probably wait."], [955.0, "We might get a new apartment but we're still going to try to save some money."], [959.1, "We're not going to buy something super expensive or rent something super expensive because we want to delay that gratification."], [968.5, "We want to instead save our money instead we want to invest the money into the business so that the business can continue to grow."], [979.4, "So that's why I don't have a really big expensive car."], [983.5, "And we don't live in a big expensive house."], [988.0, "And then this idea of compounding again, for me, I prefer to invest my money in the business."], [996.7, "I feel like that a business is really the best investment, if you do it well."], [1004.9, "The business can grow much faster than a bank account."], [1009.0, "The business can grow faster than stocks."], [1012.3, "The business can grow faster than real estate."], [1016.6, "But you know, businesses take more work."], [1019.5, "A bank account's easy."], [1020.4, "Put it in the bank and it sits there and you do nothing and it makes a little extra money."], [1025.0, "So it's easy."], [1026.7, "It requires no work, but you also make very little money."], [1031.3, "The compounding is very small."], [1034.6, "Creating your own business."], [1037.1, "Your own successful business takes more work."], [1040.2, "It requires more effort more work more thinking especially But the rewards are also much bigger."], [1050.0, "So remember these three points."], [1052.8, "Make sure you have a vision if you don't have a vision get one think about it what is your vision?"], [1058.3, "Write it down."], [1059.4, "Dream."], [1060.0, "Dream big."], [1061.4, "Decide what you really, truly want, financially and in general."], [1067.4, "And then you got to delay your pleasure, delay your gratification."], [1072.0, "Means buy less stuff, save more money."], [1076.0, "And then finally, after you have done that, you want to make your money grow with compounding."], [1082.0, "You want to start a little business so it can grow, or invest in stocks or something; make it grow with compounding."], [1083.5, "Good luck to you; I'm sure you will be successful."], [1084.2, "Just be patient; it might take time, but you can do it."], [1085.0, "I look forward to reading your success story in the forums."], [1085.7, "See you again, bye."]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["poverty", "/ˈpɒvəti/", "sự nghèo khó"], ["wealthy", "/ˈwelθi/", "giàu có"], ["possess", "/pəˈzes/", "sở hữu, có"], ["quality", "/ˈkwɒləti/", "phẩm chất"], ["long-term vision", "/ˌlɒŋ tɜːm ˈvɪʒn/", "tầm nhìn dài hạn"], ["delayed gratification", "/dɪˈleɪd ˌɡrætɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/", "trì hoãn sự hưởng thụ"], ["compounding", "/kəmˈpaʊndɪŋ/", "lãi kép, sự tích lũy cộng dồn"], ["in one's favor", "/ɪn wʌnz ˈfeɪvə(r)/", "có lợi cho ai"], ["hold to", "/həʊld tə/", "giữ vững"], ["be willing to", "/bi ˈwɪlɪŋ tə/", "sẵn sàng"], ["sacrifice", "/ˈsækrɪfaɪs/", "hy sinh"], ["multiply", "/ˈmʌltɪplaɪ/", "nhân lên"], ["compound interest", "/ˈkɒmpaʊnd ˈɪntrəst/", "lãi kép"], ["glorious", "/ˈɡlɔːriəs/", "rực rỡ, huy hoàng"], ["specific", "/spəˈsɪfɪk/", "cụ thể"], ["review", "/rɪˈvjuː/", "xem lại"], ["remind", "/rɪˈmaɪnd/", "nhắc nhở"], ["fade", "/feɪd/", "phai nhạt"], ["feed", "/fiːd/", "nuôi dưỡng"], ["unnecessary expenses", "/ʌnˈnesəsəri ɪkˈspensɪz/", "chi tiêu không cần thiết"], ["real estate", "/ˈrɪəl ɪsteɪt/", "bất động sản"], ["percentage", "/pəˈsentɪdʒ/", "phần trăm"], ["return on investment", "/rɪˈtɜːn ɒn ɪnˈvestmənt/", "lợi nhuận đầu tư"], ["patience", "/ˈpeɪʃns/", "sự kiên nhẫn"], ["intelligently", "/ɪnˈtelɪdʒəntli/", "một cách khôn ngoan"], ["discipline", "/ˈdɪsəplɪn/", "kỷ luật"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["people born into poverty", "những người sinh ra trong nghèo khó"], ["regardless of which country they lived in", "bất kể họ sống ở nước nào"], ["They maintained a long-term vision", "Họ giữ một tầm nhìn dài hạn"], ["They believed in delayed gratification", "Họ tin vào việc trì hoãn hưởng thụ"], ["used the power of compounding in their favor", "tận dụng sức mạnh lãi kép có lợi cho mình"], ["by holding to a dream or vision", "nhờ giữ vững ước mơ hay tầm nhìn"], ["make short-term sacrifices to gain long-term success", "hy sinh ngắn hạn để thành công dài hạn"], ["even tiny amounts", "dù chỉ những khoản rất nhỏ"], ["Write it down, now", "Hãy viết ra, ngay bây giờ"], ["What am I willing to sacrifice now?", "Bây giờ mình sẵn sàng hy sinh điều gì?"], ["Don't let them fade", "Đừng để chúng phai nhạt"], ["keep your vision alive", "giữ cho tầm nhìn luôn sống"], ["get closer to their long-term dream", "tiến gần hơn đến ước mơ dài hạn"], ["This formula takes patience", "Công thức này cần sự kiên nhẫn"], ["It may take time", "Có thể mất thời gian"]]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[["The study wanted to find out how + S + V", "We wanted to find out how customers use our app.", "Chúng tôi muốn tìm hiểu khách hàng dùng ứng dụng thế nào.", "find out how"], ["regardless of + which/what + noun + S + V", "Regardless of which job you choose, keep learning.", "Dù chọn công việc nào, hãy tiếp tục học.", "regardless of"], ["S + was/were willing to + V + to + V", "She was willing to move abroad to get the job.", "Cô ấy sẵn sàng ra nước ngoài để có công việc đó.", "willing to"], ["Ask yourself, \"What am I willing to + V?\"", "Ask yourself, what am I willing to give up?", "Hãy tự hỏi, mình sẵn sàng từ bỏ điều gì?", "Ask yourself"], ["Don't let + noun + V", "Don't let your dreams die.", "Đừng để ước mơ của bạn chết đi.", "Don't let"], ["Even + noun + can + V", "Even small savings can grow big over time.", "Ngay cả khoản tiết kiệm nhỏ cũng có thể lớn dần theo thời gian.", "Even"], ["This + noun + takes + patience/time", "Learning a language takes time.", "Học một ngôn ngữ cần thời gian.", "takes"], ["S + V + so (that) + S + can + V", "I save now so I can travel next year.", "Tôi tiết kiệm bây giờ để năm sau có thể đi du lịch.", "so"]]$j$::jsonb
)
